<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Extended Introduction</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Humans are capable of extraordinary good, but also of profound harm. At our worst, we lie and deceive; we murder, torture, and oppress; we exploit the vulnerable and profit from war or disaster. These dark capacities, though tragic, are unfortunately well-documented aspects of human agency. It is perhaps then unsurprising that neural networks modeled on human behavior can exhibit similar tendencies <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>, <a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>, <a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite>. Deception, manipulation, and strategic misrepresentation have all emerged in recent models, suggesting not isolated bugs, but deeper patterns of emergent behavior <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>, <a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>, <a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>, <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite>. For instance, Anthropic recently reported that their Claude Opus 4 model attempted to blackmail company engineers to avoid shutdown during pre-release testing <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>, <a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>]</cite>. In another case, an AI model sought to replicate its own codebase in a bid for survival <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>, <a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To mitigate such phenomena, researchers have increasingly focused on mechanisms for control <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>, <a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>, <a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>]</cite>, oversight <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>, <a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>]</cite>, or interpretability <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>, <a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>, <a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite>. This includes designing improved pre-training protocols <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>, <a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>, <a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">41</a>]</cite>, developing reinforcement learning methods that penalize undesirable behavior <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>, <a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>, <a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">43</a>]</cite>, and constructing faster detection systems for adversarial outputs <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">44</a>, <a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">45</a>, <a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>, <a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">47</a>]</cite>. These technical interventions are valuable and urgent, targeting symptoms rather than the underlying structure. Thus in this work, we address a different and complementary layer of the problem: the foundational structures that govern the emergence of agentic behavior. We contend that understanding and formalizing these deeper drivers is essential for the principled and provably safe deployment of increasingly capable systems.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">What remains far less explored than empirical alignment are the theoretical foundations of agency. What mathematical models or structural invariants govern the emergence of goal-directed behavior in neural networks? This question, though fundamental, has received relatively minimal attention. Yet answering it may offer substantial insights, not just for understanding artificial agents, but for developing principled methods for subagent identification and alignment. To our knowledge, existing work in this direction is sparse. The closest analogues lie in mathematical economics, where utility or reward maximization is used to model individual or group behavior under idealized assumptions <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>, <a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">48</a>, <a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">49</a>, <a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>, <a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">50</a>, <a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">51</a>]</cite>.
These frameworks offer powerful abstractions but fall short of capturing the complexity of distributed, probabilistic, and emergent agency in modern AI systems. Our work therefore aims to extend beyond these paradigms, to provide a more general and rigorous foundation for modeling agency in both artificial and natural systems.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We begin by reviewing two canonical rules: the <em id="A1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">linear</em> and <em id="A1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">logarithmic</em> opinion pools. We derive each as the unique minimizer of a weighted sum of Kullback–Leibler (KL) divergences, thereby providing an information–theoretic connection. We then interpret probability distributions as exponentials of epistemic utility functions, showing how utilities can be averaged to produce the logarithmic pool via a softmax transformation. This perspective connects belief aggregation on probabilistic generative models with classical utility theory. We then formalize a notion of a <em id="A1.p4.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">compositional agent</em> whose welfare increases upon joining a composition, and derive necessary and sufficient conditions under which such improvement holds. We prove that unanimously beneficial compositions exist whenever the outcome space has at least three elements, but that no such composition can exist for binary outcomes under logarithmic welfare. After developing the formal foundations, we then provide a depth of explicit analytic constructions and theoretical results for compositional agency and agentic alignment.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Contributions.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our contributions may be summarized as follows:</p>
<ol id="A1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Formalization of compositional agency:</span> We introduce a welfare-based definition of unanimously beneficial compositions using log-score utilities and probabilistic generative models.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sharp possibility frontier:</span> We prove strict unanimity is impossible for binary outcome spaces and under linear pooling, but possible for <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{O}|\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{O}|\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math> under logarithmic pooling.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Recursive and robustness properties:</span> We establish cloning invariance, continuity, and openness of strictly unanimous decomposability, yielding a rigorous theoretical foundation for multi-agent composition in neural models.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Limits of local perturbations:</span> We show that small tilts around a fixed pool cannot achieve strict unanimity, ruling out trivial duplication as a path to compositionality.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Safety-relevant alignment principle:</span> We formalize the Waluigi effect using our framework, and prove that manifest–then–suppress strictly outperforms direct suppression, illuminating alignment challenges in large AI systems.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Summary of Appendices.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">After motivating agents as generative models over the outcome space <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> in Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Motivating the Framework ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>, Appendix <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Foundations of Probabilistic Model Aggregation ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a> derives opinion pools from KL minimization and establishes the utility–probability correspondence. Appendix <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Compositional Agents and Welfare Improvement ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a> introduces the compositional condition and proves existence of compositional objects under restricted artificial welfare function constraints. For generalization, Appendix <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Possible and Impossible Compositions ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a> develops possibility and impossibility results assuming the epistemic utility as the welfare: binary impossibility, constructive possibility for <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{O}|\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{O}|\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>, and impossibility under linear pooling. Appendix <a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Recursing on Compositional Agents for Scale-Free Theory ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a> establishes recursive properties such as cloning invariance and existence of repeated iterated decompositions. Appendix <a href="#A7" title="Appendix G Recursive Splitting of Agents under Logarithmic Pooling ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G</span></a> formally verifies and proves that the compositional property is not preserved under subagent decomposition. Appendix <a href="#A8" title="Appendix H Properties of Strict Local (Small-Tilt) Unanimity ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span></a> analyzes tilt factorizations, showing that small perturbations cannot yield strict unanimity and that joining uniform distributions never benefits any agent. Additionally, it is shown that the set of strictly unanimously compositional distributions forms an open set in the simplex topology. Building on these results, Appendix <a href="#A9" title="Appendix I Modeling the Waluigi Effect ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I</span></a> delineates the modeling of the probability of misaligned or deplorable events being realized by agent <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> using our framework, and elucidates the so-called Waluigi effect. Finally, Appendix <a href="#A10" title="Appendix J Killing the Waluigi Effect to First Order ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">J</span></a> proves the Waluigi Shattering Theorem, showing that purposely manifesting malevolence strictly helps for alignment, and that manifest–then–suppress adversarial personas theoretically achieves greater alignment improvement than purely reinforcing benevolence alone.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Motivating the Framework</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A central hypothesis is that higher-level agents are composed of interacting subagents, each with their own preferences, behaviors, and learning dynamics. Modeling or understanding how these subagents coalesce into a coherent whole is instrumental to developing a scale-free framework, illuminating both the emergent behavior of artificial systems and the dynamics of human compositions. Moreover, uncovering the individual subagents that comprise a compositional agent could enable surgical latent prior modeling and intervention, offering insight into the capabilities and internal tensions of such agents.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Returning to the case of the neural network that attempted blackmail: fundamentally, such models operate as probability distributions–mathematical functions optimized for next-token prediction executed on tensor cores <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>, <a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>. Through reinforcement learning from human feedback (RLHF), they are steered toward distributions aligned with human preferences <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>, <a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">41</a>, <a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>]</cite>. However, the model in question appears to have converged not only on desirable behavior but also on internal representations that encode a preference for self-preservation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>, <a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>, <a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">52</a>]</cite>. This emergent behavior was not rewarded during RLHF, yet it was not eliminated during the alignment phase <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>, <a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>, <a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">More broadly, large models may encode latent priors over deeply troubling behaviors, such as conflict, oppression, or even genocide, that remain undetected under conventional testing <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">53</a>, <a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">54</a>, <a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">47</a>]</cite>. These priors are not necessarily hard-coded, but may emerge implicitly through scale, training data, or optimization objectives <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">55</a>, <a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">56</a>]</cite>. If left unexamined, such latent drives can subtly shape behavior or, in worst cases, manifest in overtly harmful actions <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">56</a>, <a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This raises a foundational question: In what sense can we think of these latent priors, or more generally, probability distributions, as agents? In reinforcement learning, an agent is often defined as an entity that acts to maximize a reward or utility function <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">57</a>, <a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">58</a>]</cite>. But is this the only viable formalism? Can we unify this utility-maximization paradigm with a probabilistic view of agency?</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Our work attempts to bridge this conceptual gap. We adopt a perspective inspired by active inference, wherein an agent is modeled as a probabilistic generative model (PGM) over outcomes or observations <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>, <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>, <a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>, <a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>, <a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">59</a>, <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>.
That is, an agent predicts, and thus selectively favors, the outcomes it wants to bring about. For instance, a PGM encoding a preference for cats would have high probability mass over visual observations of petting a cat. The action of an agent in the world is then modeled by sampling from this biased outcome distribution. In this view, goals are formalized as distributions over desirable observations, and behavior arises from the agent’s attempts to bring those observations about.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Formalizing agents as PGMs invites a further challenge: How do multiple generative models, each with their own probabilistic biases, combine to form a coherent, higher-level agent? This calls for a principled framework for modeling compositional agency, one that describes how disparate distributions can coalesce, both in the language of probability theory and in relation to utility-based frameworks. Developing this foundation is a central aim of our work.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Related Work.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The theory of belief pooling asks how to aggregate many probability assessments into one and is anchored by Stone’s “opinion pool” formulation and classic linear (arithmetic) and logarithmic (geometric) rules <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">60</a>, <a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">61</a>, <a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">62</a>, <a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">63</a>]</cite>. Beyond axiomatic foundations, proper scoring rules justify and learn aggregations: minimizing expected log score yields a log pool; minimizing quadratic/Brier score yields a linear pool; and weights can be estimated by maximizing average proper score (stacking) on held-out data <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib64" title="" class="ltx_ref">64</a>]</cite>. Statistical and ML links include Bayesian model averaging as a linear pool with posterior model-probability weights <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib65" title="" class="ltx_ref">65</a>]</cite> and <em id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">products of experts</em> as a log pool of model likelihoods <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib66" title="" class="ltx_ref">66</a>]</cite>. Modern work generalizes these axioms from <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>–algebras to general agendas of logically structured propositions–providing representation and impossibility theorems for neutrality/independence beyond standard event spaces <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib67" title="" class="ltx_ref">67</a>]</cite>–and develops <em id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">principled weighting</em> for log pools (e.g., log-linear pooling of priors with weights chosen by marginal likelihood or predictive criteria), alongside practice-oriented syntheses on expert elicitation and performance-based weighting in risk analysis <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">68</a>, <a href="#bib.bib69" title="" class="ltx_ref">69</a>]</cite>. Similarly, bargaining theory provides parallel insights into axiomatic and cooperative equilibrium solutions that guide institutional system design <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib70" title="" class="ltx_ref">70</a>, <a href="#bib.bib71" title="" class="ltx_ref">71</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Foundations of Probabilistic Model Aggregation</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> be a discrete set of outcomes. A collection of agents <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1,\dots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1,\dots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math> each possesses a probability distribution <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math>. We assign to each agent a non–negative influence weight <math id="A3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="A3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. The aggregated belief <math id="A3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> is a probability measure on <math id="A3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> determined by the chosen pooling rule. A desired precondition is recursion; for instance, if an agent is split into identical subagents and its weight <math id="A3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is distributed among them, the aggregated distribution should remain unchanged.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Linear and Logarithmic Opinion Pools</h3>

<div id="Thmtheorem22" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem22.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 22</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem22.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Linear opinion pool)<span id="Thmtheorem22.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem22.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem22.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem22.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given agents <math id="Thmtheorem22.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{P_{1},\dots,P_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{P_{1},\dots,P_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math> with weights <math id="Thmtheorem22.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\beta_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\beta_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the <em id="Thmtheorem22.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">linear opinion pool</em> is defined by</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{C}^{\mathrm{lin}}(o)\;=\;\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\,P_{i}(o)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>lin</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{C}^{\mathrm{lin}}(o)\;=\;\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\,P_{i}(o),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem22.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem22.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for each <math id="Thmtheorem22.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\in\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\in\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The linear pool is simply a convex combination of the individual distributions. It is easy to compute and automatically produces a valid probability distribution without further normalization. As a mixture model, it can be sampled by first selecting an agent at random (according to <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>) and then sampling from that agent’s distribution. When applied to purely the outcome space and not any intermediary causal variable, this results in a so-called random dictatorship. One disadvantage is that the linear pool does not allow any single agent to veto an outcome: even if an agent assigns zero probability to an undesirable outcome, the composition may still assign positive mass if others favor it.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem23" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem23.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 23</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem23.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Logarithmic opinion pool)<span id="Thmtheorem23.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem23.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem23.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem23.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For the same set of agents and weights, the <em id="Thmtheorem23.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">logarithmic opinion pool</em> (sometimes called the log–linear pool) is defined by</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{C}^{\mathrm{log}}(o)\;=\;\frac{1}{Z}\,\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>log</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>Z</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{C}^{\mathrm{log}}(o)\;=\;\frac{1}{Z}\,\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem23.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem23.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the normalizing constant is</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\;=\;\sum_{o^{\prime}\in\mathcal{O}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(o^{\prime})^{\beta_{i}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\;=\;\sum_{o^{\prime}\in\mathcal{O}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(o^{\prime})^{\beta_{i}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In logarithmic pooling, probabilities are combined multiplicatively on a log scale. The rule is sometimes justified by the interpretation of probability as evidence: the logarithm of a probability is additive for independent pieces of information, and the pool aggregates these contributions linearly. An important property of the log pool is the <em id="A3.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">veto effect</em>: if any agent with non–zero weight assigns zero probability to an outcome, then the composition also assigns zero probability, ensuring that every member retains absolute veto power for outcomes they absolutely detest.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Derivation via Divergence Minimization</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The linear and logarithmic pools are not arbitrary constructs; each arises naturally as the solution to a convex optimization problem involving KL divergences. Recall that for distributions <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math>, the KL divergence is defined by</p>
<table id="A3.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\KL(P\|Q)\;=\;\sum_{o\in\mathcal{O}}P(o)\,\log\frac{P(o)}{Q(o)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></munder><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(P\|Q)\;=\;\sum_{o\in\mathcal{O}}P(o)\,\log\frac{P(o)}{Q(o)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem24" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem24.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 24</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem24.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Logarithmic pool from forward KL)<span id="Thmtheorem24.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem24.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem24.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem24.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The distribution <math id="Thmtheorem24.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> that minimizes the weighted sum of forward divergences</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="J(P_{C})\;=\;\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\,\KL\bigl(P_{C}\,\|\,P_{i}\bigr)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(P_{C})\;=\;\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\,\KL\bigl(P_{C}\,\|\,P_{i}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem24.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem24.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">is precisely the logarithmic opinion pool.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Expanding the objective yields</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J(P_{C})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J(P_{C})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\sum_{o\in\mathcal{O}}P_{C}(o)\log\frac{P_{C}(o)}{P_{i}(o)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\sum_{o\in\mathcal{O}}P_{C}(o)\log\frac{P_{C}(o)}{P_{i}(o)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{o}P_{C}(o)\log P_{C}(o)\Bigl(\sum_{i}\beta_{i}\Bigr)-\sum_{o}P_{C}(o)\sum_{i}\beta_{i}\log P_{i}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{o}P_{C}(o)\log P_{C}(o)\Bigl(\sum_{i}\beta_{i}\Bigr)-\sum_{o}P_{C}(o)\sum_{i}\beta_{i}\log P_{i}(o)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{o}P_{C}(o)\log P_{C}(o)-\sum_{o}P_{C}(o)\log\Bigl(\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}}\Bigr)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{o}P_{C}(o)\log P_{C}(o)-\sum_{o}P_{C}(o)\log\Bigl(\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}}\Bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(o)=\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}}/Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(o)=\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}}/Z</annotation></semantics></math> be the normalized log pool distribution for <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> in Definition <a href="#Thmtheorem23" title="Definition 23 (Logarithmic opinion pool). ‣ C.1 Linear and Logarithmic Opinion Pools ‣ Appendix C Foundations of Probabilistic Model Aggregation ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>. Then,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="J(P_{C})=\KL(P_{C}\,\|\,Q)-\log Z." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(P_{C})=\KL(P_{C}\,\|\,Q)-\log Z.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log Z</annotation></semantics></math> does not depend on <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{C}</annotation></semantics></math>, the objective is minimized exactly when <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\KL(P_{C}\,\|\,Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(P_{C}\,\|\,Q)</annotation></semantics></math> attains its minimum value of zero. This happens if and only if <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{C}=Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{C}=Q</annotation></semantics></math>, which concludes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem25" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem25.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 25</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem25.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Linear pool from reverse KL)<span id="Thmtheorem25.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem25.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem25.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem25.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The distribution <math id="Thmtheorem25.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> that minimizes the weighted sum of reverse divergences</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="J(P_{C})\;=\;\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\,\KL\bigl(P_{i}\,\|\,P_{C}\bigr)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(P_{C})\;=\;\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\,\KL\bigl(P_{i}\,\|\,P_{C}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem25.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem25.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">is the linear opinion pool.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Expand the objective:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(P_{C})=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\sum_{o\in\mathcal{O}}P_{i}(o)\log\frac{P_{i}(o)}{P_{C}(o)}=\sum_{i}\beta_{i}\sum_{o}P_{i}(o)\log P_{i}(o)-\sum_{i}\beta_{i}\sum_{o}P_{i}(o)\log P_{C}(o)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(P_{C})=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\sum_{o\in\mathcal{O}}P_{i}(o)\log\frac{P_{i}(o)}{P_{C}(o)}=\sum_{i}\beta_{i}\sum_{o}P_{i}(o)\log P_{i}(o)-\sum_{i}\beta_{i}\sum_{o}P_{i}(o)\log P_{C}(o).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">The first term is constant in <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{C}</annotation></semantics></math>. Minimizing <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(P_{C})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(P_{C})</annotation></semantics></math> is therefore equivalent to maximizing
<math id="A3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}\sum_{o}\beta_{i}P_{i}(o)\log P_{C}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}\sum_{o}\beta_{i}P_{i}(o)\log P_{C}(o)</annotation></semantics></math>
subject to <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{o}P_{C}(o)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>o</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{o}P_{C}(o)=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Introducing a Lagrange multiplier <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> for the normalization constraint and taking derivatives with respect to <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{C}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{C}(o)</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}\beta_{i}P_{i}(o)\cdot\frac{1}{P_{C}(o)}-\lambda=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}\beta_{i}P_{i}(o)\cdot\frac{1}{P_{C}(o)}-\lambda=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Solving for <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{C}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{C}(o)</annotation></semantics></math> shows that it must be proportional to <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}\beta_{i}P_{i}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}\beta_{i}P_{i}(o)</annotation></semantics></math>. After enforcing <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{o}P_{C}(o)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>o</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{o}P_{C}(o)=1</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain
<math id="A3.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{C}(o)=\sum_{i}\beta_{i}P_{i}(o)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{C}(o)=\sum_{i}\beta_{i}P_{i}(o),</annotation></semantics></math>
which is the linear pool.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We note that the two pooling mechanisms allow a form of trivial recursion. That is, if an agent <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is split into <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> identical copies and its weight <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is divided uniformly among them, then under the linear pool the combined contribution is still <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{k}P_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{k}P_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>; under the logarithmic pool the combined exponent is still <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> because exponents add.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>From Probabilities to Utilities</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Interpreting probability distributions as utility functions offers a deeper lens through which to understand aggregation rules. In particular, we define the notion of <em id="A3.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">epistemic utility</em>, or <em id="A3.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">relative utility</em>, which captures how an agent’s preferences are reflected in the probabilities it assigns to outcomes. The core idea is that agents by definition do not merely describe the world; they encode value judgments within their predictions. For example, a hungry agent might assign higher probability to outcomes <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o^{*}\in\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{*}\in\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> in which it obtains food, implicitly revealing its goals through its belief distribution.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Formally, given an agent with belief <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and a realized outcome <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o^{*}\in\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{*}\in\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math>, the logarithmic score defines the agent’s epistemic utility as</p>
<table id="A3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i}^{\mathrm{epi}}(o^{*})\;=\;\log P_{i}(o^{*})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>epi</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i}^{\mathrm{epi}}(o^{*})\;=\;\log P_{i}(o^{*}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">This scoring rule rewards agents for assigning high probability to the correct outcome. Thus, maximizing expected epistemic utility incentivizes the agent to learn calibrated models that reflect the actual distribution of outcomes as accurately as possible.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">C.3.1 </span>Softmax and the Utility–Probability Correspondence</h4>

<div id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i}:\mathcal{O}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i}:\mathcal{O}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be a utility function representing agent <math id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>’s preferences over outcomes. A standard way to map utilities into probabilities is via the softmax transformation</p>
<table id="A3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}(o)\;=\;\frac{\exp\bigl(U_{i}(o)\bigr)}{\sum_{o^{\prime}\in\mathcal{O}}\exp\bigl(U_{i}(o^{\prime})\bigr)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}(o)\;=\;\frac{\exp\bigl(U_{i}(o)\bigr)}{\sum_{o^{\prime}\in\mathcal{O}}\exp\bigl(U_{i}(o^{\prime})\bigr)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This mapping between utility landscapes and probability distributions plays two roles. First, one can recover an agent’s beliefs from its utilities: exponentiating and normalizing yields the distribution. Conversely, the logarithm of a strictly positive distribution defines a utility function up to an additive constant. Indeed, setting <math id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i}(o)=\log P_{i}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i}(o)=\log P_{i}(o)</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A3.E6" title="In C.3.1 Softmax and the Utility–Probability Correspondence ‣ C.3 From Probabilities to Utilities ‣ Appendix C Foundations of Probabilistic Model Aggregation ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) returns <math id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> exactly. This observation underlies our use of log probabilities or logits as epistemic utilities.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">C.3.2 </span>Averaging Utilities and the Logarithmic Pool</h4>

<div id="A3.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose a group of agents forms a meta–agent by averaging their utility functions. A natural definition for the composition’s relative utility is</p>
<table id="A3.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{C}(o)\;=\;\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\,U_{i}(o)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{C}(o)\;=\;\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\,U_{i}(o).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Each agent’s influence is reflected in its weight <math id="A3.SS3.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting <math id="A3.SS3.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i}(o)=\log P_{i}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i}(o)=\log P_{i}(o)</annotation></semantics></math> shows that <math id="A3.SS3.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> is the weighted average of the individual log probabilities:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{C}(o)\;=\;\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\log P_{i}(o)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{C}(o)\;=\;\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\log P_{i}(o).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Applying the softmax transformation to <math id="A3.SS3.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> yields</p>
<table id="A3.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{C}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{C}(o)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\exp(U_{C}(o))}{\sum_{o^{\prime}\in\mathcal{O}}\exp(U_{C}(o^{\prime}))}=\frac{\exp\bigl(\sum_{i}\beta_{i}\log P_{i}(o)\bigr)}{\sum_{o^{\prime}}\exp\bigl(\sum_{i}\beta_{i}\log P_{i}(o^{\prime})\bigr)}=\frac{\prod_{i}P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}}}{\sum_{o^{\prime}}\prod_{i}P_{i}(o^{\prime})^{\beta_{i}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∏</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\exp(U_{C}(o))}{\sum_{o^{\prime}\in\mathcal{O}}\exp(U_{C}(o^{\prime}))}=\frac{\exp\bigl(\sum_{i}\beta_{i}\log P_{i}(o)\bigr)}{\sum_{o^{\prime}}\exp\bigl(\sum_{i}\beta_{i}\log P_{i}(o^{\prime})\bigr)}=\frac{\prod_{i}P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}}}{\sum_{o^{\prime}}\prod_{i}P_{i}(o^{\prime})^{\beta_{i}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Thus averaging utilities and then exponentiating reproduces the logarithmic opinion pool. This derivation offers a simple social–choice interpretation: the composition’s belief (in log space) is the average of its members’ beliefs. The linear pool, in contrast, corresponds to averaging distributions directly rather than averaging the log scores.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Compositional Agents and Welfare Improvement</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now formalize when joining a composition benefits an individual agent in terms of its expected welfare. Throughout this section the outcome space <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> remains discrete, agents have beliefs <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{P_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{P_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and each agent <math id="A4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> possesses a welfare function <math id="A4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}:\mathcal{O}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}:\mathcal{O}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> that measures the desirability of outcomes from its perspective. The composition’s belief is constructed via the logarithmic pool with weights <math id="A4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\beta_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\beta_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. In this setting, under what conditions does an agent expect to do at least as well, according to its own welfare function, by adopting the composition’s distribution?</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem26" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem26.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 26</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem26.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Agent beliefs and welfare)<span id="Thmtheorem26.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem26.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem26.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem26.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For each agent <math id="Thmtheorem26.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,\dots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,\dots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math>, define</span></p>
<ol id="A4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Probability distribution </span><math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}:\mathcal{O}\to[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}:\mathcal{O}\to[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> with </span><math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{o\in\mathcal{O}}P_{i}(o)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{o\in\mathcal{O}}P_{i}(o)=1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">;</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Welfare function </span><math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}:\mathcal{O}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}:\mathcal{O}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> expressing the utility the agent assigns to each outcome.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem27" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem27.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 27</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem27.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Composition belief)<span id="Thmtheorem27.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem27.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem27.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem27.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix non-negative weights <math id="Thmtheorem27.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> summing to one. The composition’s belief under the logarithmic pool is</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(o)\;=\;\frac{1}{Z}\,\prod_{j=1}^{n}P_{j}(o)^{\beta_{j}},\quad\text{where }Z=\sum_{o^{\prime}\in\mathcal{O}}\prod_{j=1}^{n}P_{j}(o^{\prime})^{\beta_{j}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>Z</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">where </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(o)\;=\;\frac{1}{Z}\,\prod_{j=1}^{n}P_{j}(o)^{\beta_{j}},\quad\text{where }Z=\sum_{o^{\prime}\in\mathcal{O}}\prod_{j=1}^{n}P_{j}(o^{\prime})^{\beta_{j}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem28" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem28.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 28</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem28.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Compositional agent)<span id="Thmtheorem28.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem28.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem28.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem28.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">An agent <math id="Thmtheorem28.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is said to be a <em id="Thmtheorem28.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">compositional agent</em> if its expected welfare under the composition belief is at least as large as under its own belief, that is,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E_{P_{i}}[W_{i}]\;\leq\;\E_{P}[W_{i}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E_{P_{i}}[W_{i}]\;\leq\;\E_{P}[W_{i}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem28.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem28.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We interpret this as meaning that agent <math id="Thmtheorem28.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> benefits (or at least does not lose) by joining the composition.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We characterize this condition in terms of the covariance between an agent’s welfare and the ratio by which the composition reweights its distribution. We note that under this definition, a composition need not be composed only of compositional agents.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem29" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem29.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 29</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem29.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Compositional agent condition)<span id="Thmtheorem29.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem29.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem29.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem29.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem29.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{i}(o):=P(o)/P_{i}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{i}(o):=P(o)/P_{i}(o)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the probability ratio between the composition and agent <math id="Thmtheorem29.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. Then agent <math id="Thmtheorem29.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is a compositional agent if and only if</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Cov}_{P_{i}}\bigl(W_{i},Q_{i}\bigr)\;\geq\;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Cov}_{P_{i}}\bigl(W_{i},Q_{i}\bigr)\;\geq\;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">First note that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E_{P}[W_{i}]=\sum_{o}P(o)W_{i}(o)=\sum_{o}P_{i}(o)Q_{i}(o)W_{i}(o)=\E_{P_{i}}[Q_{i}W_{i}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E_{P}[W_{i}]=\sum_{o}P(o)W_{i}(o)=\sum_{o}P_{i}(o)Q_{i}(o)W_{i}(o)=\E_{P_{i}}[Q_{i}W_{i}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus <math id="A4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E_{P}[W_{i}]\geq\E_{P_{i}}[W_{i}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E_{P}[W_{i}]\geq\E_{P_{i}}[W_{i}]</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if
<math id="A4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E_{P_{i}}[Q_{i}W_{i}]\geq\E_{P_{i}}[W_{i}]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E_{P_{i}}[Q_{i}W_{i}]\geq\E_{P_{i}}[W_{i}].</annotation></semantics></math>
But <math id="A4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E_{P_{i}}[Q_{i}]=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E_{P_{i}}[Q_{i}]=1</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="A4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{o}P(o)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>o</mi></msub><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{o}P(o)=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Multiplying <math id="A4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E_{P_{i}}[W_{i}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E_{P_{i}}[W_{i}]</annotation></semantics></math> by this constant yields
<math id="A4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E_{P_{i}}[W_{i}]\E_{P_{i}}[Q_{i}]\leq\E_{P_{i}}[Q_{i}W_{i}]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E_{P_{i}}[W_{i}]\E_{P_{i}}[Q_{i}]\leq\E_{P_{i}}[Q_{i}W_{i}].</annotation></semantics></math>
Rearranging gives precisely the non–negativity of the covariance between <math id="A4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> under <math id="A4.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Interpretation.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The quantity <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{i}(o)=P(o)/P_{i}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{i}(o)=P(o)/P_{i}(o)</annotation></semantics></math> measures how the composition redistributes agent <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>’s probability mass: values greater than one indicate outcomes promoted by the group, while values less than one indicate outcomes demoted. The condition in Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem29" title="Proposition 29 (Compositional agent condition). ‣ Appendix D Compositional Agents and Welfare Improvement ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a> states that agent <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> benefits if, on average, the composition places more weight on outcomes that <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> values highly. Thus by joining the composition, agent <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is able to better realize outcomes it desires. Negative covariance means that the composition emphasizes outcomes that <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> prefers less, leading to a loss of welfare.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">It is natural to require that every member of a composition benefits. We call such a configuration a unanimously compositional group.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem30" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem30.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 30</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem30.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Unanimously compositional group)<span id="Thmtheorem30.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem30.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem30.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem30.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A set of agents <math id="Thmtheorem30.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1,\dots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1,\dots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math> is a <em id="Thmtheorem30.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">unanimously compositional group</em> if each agent <math id="Thmtheorem30.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is a compositional agent, i.e., <math id="Thmtheorem30.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E_{P_{i}}[W_{i}]\leq\E_{P}[W_{i}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">P</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E_{P_{i}}[W_{i}]\leq\E_{P}[W_{i}]</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmtheorem30.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,\dots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,\dots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">A natural question is if such an ideal group exists. In Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem31" title="Theorem 31 (Existence of a unanimously compositional group). ‣ Interpretation. ‣ Appendix D Compositional Agents and Welfare Improvement ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>, we answer in the affirmative.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem31" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem31.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 31</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem31.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Existence of a unanimously compositional group)<span id="Thmtheorem31.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem31.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem31.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem31.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any integer <math id="Thmtheorem31.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a configuration of beliefs
<math id="Thmtheorem31.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{P_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{P_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, welfare functions <math id="Thmtheorem31.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{W_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{W_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and uniform weights
<math id="Thmtheorem31.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}=1/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}=1/n</annotation></semantics></math> such that the logarithmic opinion pool makes every agent
strictly better off.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We give an explicit construction with <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> outcomes
<math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}=\{o_{1},\dots,o_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}=\{o_{1},\dots,o_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and uniform weights
<math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}=\tfrac{1}{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}=\tfrac{1}{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Choosing <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in(0,1/n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in(0,1/n)</annotation></semantics></math>, define</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}(o_{j})=\begin{cases}1-(n-1)\,\epsilon,&amp;j=i,\\
\epsilon,&amp;j\neq i.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}(o_{j})=\begin{cases}1-(n-1)\,\epsilon,&amp;j=i,\\
\epsilon,&amp;j\neq i.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus each agent <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is nearly certain of outcome <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\ll 1/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>≪</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\ll 1/n</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> be a large constant. Define</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}(o_{j})=\begin{cases}0,&amp;j=(i\bmod n)+1,\\
-C,&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>mod</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>otherwise</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}(o_{j})=\begin{cases}0,&amp;j=(i\bmod n)+1,\\
-C,&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Agent <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> therefore most values outcome <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, in a cyclic manner. For any outcome <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(o_{k})^{1/n}=\bigl(1-(n-1)\epsilon\bigr)^{1/n}\,\epsilon^{(n-1)/n}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(o_{k})^{1/n}=\bigl(1-(n-1)\epsilon\bigr)^{1/n}\,\epsilon^{(n-1)/n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">which is identical for all <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence after normalization, we thus have</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(o_{k})=\frac{1}{n}\quad\forall\,k=1,\dots,n." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(o_{k})=\frac{1}{n}\quad\forall\,k=1,\dots,n.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">Without loss of generality, consider Agent 1, with standalone welfare</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E_{P_{1}}[W_{1}]=P_{1}(o_{2})\cdot 0+\bigl(P_{1}(o_{1})+\sum_{j=3}^{n}P_{1}(o_{j})\bigr)(-C)=-C+C\epsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E_{P_{1}}[W_{1}]=P_{1}(o_{2})\cdot 0+\bigl(P_{1}(o_{1})+\sum_{j=3}^{n}P_{1}(o_{j})\bigr)(-C)=-C+C\epsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">Under the pool,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E_{P}[W_{1}]=\tfrac{1}{n}\cdot 0+\tfrac{n-1}{n}(-C)=-C\,\frac{n-1}{n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E_{P}[W_{1}]=\tfrac{1}{n}\cdot 0+\tfrac{n-1}{n}(-C)=-C\,\frac{n-1}{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.7.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&lt;1/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&lt;1/n</annotation></semantics></math>, we have
<math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-C\,\frac{n-1}{n}&gt;-C+C\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-C\,\frac{n-1}{n}&gt;-C+C\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus
<math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{P}[W_{1}]&gt;\mathbb{E}_{P_{1}}[W_{1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{P}[W_{1}]&gt;\mathbb{E}_{P_{1}}[W_{1}]</annotation></semantics></math>. By symmetry the same holds
for every agent <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. This completes the constructive proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Up to this point, we have left the definition of welfare <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> deliberately open. In this section, we adopt the assumption that each agent’s welfare function is identical to its epistemic utility, i.e., <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}(o)=\log P_{i}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}(o)=\log P_{i}(o)</annotation></semantics></math>. Under this interpretation, agents derive welfare directly from their predictive beliefs, which implicitly encode their goals, values, and preferences. The following sections investigate when compositions formed under this assumption lead to unanimous improvement, in other words, when every agent benefits from aggregation. As we will show, the possibility of such unanimous benefit depends critically on the cardinality of the outcome space. In particular, we find a stark contrast between the binary and multi-outcome settings.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Possible and Impossible Compositions</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first examine the binary outcome case and show that unanimity cannot be achieved when welfare functions are logarithmic scores. We then prove that for outcome spaces of size at least three, there always exist beliefs and welfare functions that yield unanimous improvement under the logarithmic pool. Finally, we give an explicit analytic construction for such compositions.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Impossibility in the Binary Case</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}=\{o_{A},o_{B}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}=\{o_{A},o_{B}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose two agents have beliefs <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1},P_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1},P_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> and welfare functions <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}(o)=\log P_{i}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}(o)=\log P_{i}(o)</annotation></semantics></math>. The composition’s belief under any positive weights <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1},\beta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1},\beta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is again a distribution on two points. We claim that at most one agent can be strictly better off.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We start with the following result.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem32" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem32.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 32</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem32.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Welfare gap identity for logarithmic utility)<span id="Thmtheorem32.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem32.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem32.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem32.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem32.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> be a finite outcome space. For any agent <math id="Thmtheorem32.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> with belief distribution <math id="Thmtheorem32.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and any composition distribution <math id="Thmtheorem32.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> (not necessarily equal to <math id="Thmtheorem32.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>), define the welfare gap</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}\;=\;\Delta_{P_{i}}(P)\;=\;\E_{P}[\log P_{i}]-\E_{P_{i}}[\log P_{i}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}\;=\;\Delta_{P_{i}}(P)\;=\;\E_{P}[\log P_{i}]-\E_{P_{i}}[\log P_{i}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem32.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem32.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then this difference can be written as</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta_{i}\;=\;H(P_{i})-H(P)-\KL(P\|P_{i})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}\;=\;H(P_{i})-H(P)-\KL(P\|P_{i}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem32.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem32.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem32.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes Shannon entropy and <math id="Thmtheorem32.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\KL(\cdot\|\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(\cdot\|\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the Kullback–Leibler divergence.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">By definition, the expected log utility under <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E_{P}[\log P_{i}]=\sum_{o\in\mathcal{O}}P(o)\,\log P_{i}(o)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E_{P}[\log P_{i}]=\sum_{o\in\mathcal{O}}P(o)\,\log P_{i}(o).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">We now manipulate this expression by introducing and subtracting <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log P(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log P(o)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{o}P(o)\,\log P_{i}(o)=\sum_{o}P(o)\,\bigl[\log P(o)-\log\tfrac{P(o)}{P_{i}(o)}\bigr]=\sum_{o}P(o)\log P(o)-\sum_{o}P(o)\log\tfrac{P(o)}{P_{i}(o)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{o}P(o)\,\log P_{i}(o)=\sum_{o}P(o)\,\bigl[\log P(o)-\log\tfrac{P(o)}{P_{i}(o)}\bigr]=\sum_{o}P(o)\log P(o)-\sum_{o}P(o)\log\tfrac{P(o)}{P_{i}(o)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">The first term is <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-H(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-H(P)</annotation></semantics></math> and the second term is <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\KL(P\|P_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(P\|P_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, so we conclude</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\E_{P}[\log P_{i}]=-H(P)-\KL(P\|P_{i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E_{P}[\log P_{i}]=-H(P)-\KL(P\|P_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, compute the expected log utility under the agent’s own belief:</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E_{P_{i}}[\log P_{i}]=\sum_{o}P_{i}(o)\,\log P_{i}(o)=-H(P_{i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E_{P_{i}}[\log P_{i}]=\sum_{o}P_{i}(o)\,\log P_{i}(o)=-H(P_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting into the definition of <math id="A5.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta_{i}=\E_{P}[\log P_{i}]-\E_{P_{i}}[\log P_{i}]=\bigl[-H(P)-\KL(P\|P_{i})\bigr]-(-H(P_{i}))=H(P_{i})-H(P)-\KL(P\|P_{i})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}=\E_{P}[\log P_{i}]-\E_{P_{i}}[\log P_{i}]=\bigl[-H(P)-\KL(P\|P_{i})\bigr]-(-H(P_{i}))=H(P_{i})-H(P)-\KL(P\|P_{i}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">as claimed.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We then have the following result.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem33" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem33.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 33</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem33.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Binary-outcome impossibility under log-welfare)<span id="Thmtheorem33.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem33.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem33.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem33.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem33.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}=\{o_{A},o_{B}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}=\{o_{A},o_{B}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose two agents have distinct beliefs
<math id="Thmtheorem33.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\,P_{i}(o_{A})=x_{i}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\,P_{i}(o_{A})=x_{i}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem33.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,2</annotation></semantics></math>, and welfare functions
<math id="Thmtheorem33.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}(o)=\log P_{i}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}(o)=\log P_{i}(o)</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="Thmtheorem33.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1},\beta_{2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1},\beta_{2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmtheorem33.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}+\beta_{2}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}+\beta_{2}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and form the log-linear pool</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(o_{A})=x\;=\;\frac{x_{1}^{\beta_{1}}\,x_{2}^{\beta_{2}}}{\,x_{1}^{\beta_{1}}\,x_{2}^{\beta_{2}}+(1-x_{1})^{\beta_{1}}\,(1-x_{2})^{\beta_{2}}\,}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(o_{A})=x\;=\;\frac{x_{1}^{\beta_{1}}\,x_{2}^{\beta_{2}}}{\,x_{1}^{\beta_{1}}\,x_{2}^{\beta_{2}}+(1-x_{1})^{\beta_{1}}\,(1-x_{2})^{\beta_{2}}\,}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem33.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem33.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Define each agent’s welfare gap with respect to variable <math id="Thmtheorem33.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}(x)=\E_{P}[\log P_{i}]\;-\;\E_{P_{i}}[\log P_{i}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}(x)=\E_{P}[\log P_{i}]\;-\;\E_{P_{i}}[\log P_{i}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem33.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem33.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, there is no choice of <math id="Thmtheorem33.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1},\beta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1},\beta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="Thmtheorem33.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for both <math id="Thmtheorem33.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,2</annotation></semantics></math> with at least one strict inequality.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using binary entropy and KL-divergence,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H(u)=-u\log u-(1-u)\log(1-u),\quad d(x\|x_{i})=x\log\frac{x}{x_{i}}+(1-x)\log\frac{1-x}{1-x_{i}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>u</mi><mi>log</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(u)=-u\log u-(1-u)\log(1-u),\quad d(x\|x_{i})=x\log\frac{x}{x_{i}}+(1-x)\log\frac{1-x}{1-x_{i}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">We have by Proposition <a href="#Thmtheorem32" title="Proposition 32 (Welfare gap identity for logarithmic utility). ‣ E.1 Impossibility in the Binary Case ‣ Appendix E Possible and Impossible Compositions ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a> that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta_{i}(x)=H(x_{i})-H(x)-d(x\|x_{i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}(x)=H(x_{i})-H(x)-d(x\|x_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">A direct calculation gives</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(x_{i})-H(x)=\bigl[-x_{i}\log x_{i}-(1-x_{i})\log(1-x_{i})\bigr]-\bigl[-x\log x-(1-x)\log(1-x)\bigr]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(x_{i})-H(x)=\bigl[-x_{i}\log x_{i}-(1-x_{i})\log(1-x_{i})\bigr]-\bigl[-x\log x-(1-x)\log(1-x)\bigr],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">so</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}(x)=x\log x+(1-x)\log(1-x)-x_{i}\log x_{i}-(1-x_{i})\log(1-x_{i})-\Bigl[x\log\frac{x}{x_{i}}+(1-x)\log\frac{1-x}{1-x_{i}}\Bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}(x)=x\log x+(1-x)\log(1-x)-x_{i}\log x_{i}-(1-x_{i})\log(1-x_{i})-\Bigl[x\log\frac{x}{x_{i}}+(1-x)\log\frac{1-x}{1-x_{i}}\Bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p7.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p7.5.1" class="ltx_text">Collecting terms,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}(x)=\bigl[x\log x-x\log\frac{x}{x_{i}}\bigr]+\bigl[(1-x)\log(1-x)-(1-x)\log\frac{1-x}{1-x_{i}}\bigr]-\bigl[x_{i}\log x_{i}+(1-x_{i})\log(1-x_{i})\bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}(x)=\bigl[x\log x-x\log\frac{x}{x_{i}}\bigr]+\bigl[(1-x)\log(1-x)-(1-x)\log\frac{1-x}{1-x_{i}}\bigr]-\bigl[x_{i}\log x_{i}+(1-x_{i})\log(1-x_{i})\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p7.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p7.6.1" class="ltx_text">But note</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\log x-x\log\frac{x}{x_{i}}=x\log x_{i},\quad(1-x)\log(1-x)-(1-x)\log\frac{1-x}{1-x_{i}}=(1-x)\log(1-x_{i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\log x-x\log\frac{x}{x_{i}}=x\log x_{i},\quad(1-x)\log(1-x)-(1-x)\log\frac{1-x}{1-x_{i}}=(1-x)\log(1-x_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p7.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p7.7.1" class="ltx_text">Hence</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}(x)=x\log x_{i}+(1-x)\log(1-x_{i})-\bigl[x_{i}\log x_{i}+(1-x_{i})\log(1-x_{i})\bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}(x)=x\log x_{i}+(1-x)\log(1-x_{i})-\bigl[x_{i}\log x_{i}+(1-x_{i})\log(1-x_{i})\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p7.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p7.8.1" class="ltx_text">Factor to obtain the succinct form</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}(x)=(x-x_{i})\,\bigl[\log x_{i}-\log(1-x_{i})\bigr]=(x-x_{i})\,\log\frac{x_{i}}{1-x_{i}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}(x)=(x-x_{i})\,\bigl[\log x_{i}-\log(1-x_{i})\bigr]=(x-x_{i})\,\log\frac{x_{i}}{1-x_{i}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p7.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p7.9.1" class="ltx_text">In particular, <math id="A5.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}(x_{i})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}(x_{i})=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and since <math id="A5.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\frac{x_{i}}{1-x_{i}}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\frac{x_{i}}{1-x_{i}}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> whenever <math id="A5.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}\neq\tfrac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}\neq\tfrac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the sign of <math id="A5.SS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> changes precisely once as we vary <math id="A5.SS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, write</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=x_{1}^{\beta_{1}}x_{2}^{\beta_{2}},\quad B=(1-x_{1})^{\beta_{1}}(1-x_{2})^{\beta_{2}},\quad x=\frac{A}{A+B}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=x_{1}^{\beta_{1}}x_{2}^{\beta_{2}},\quad B=(1-x_{1})^{\beta_{1}}(1-x_{2})^{\beta_{2}},\quad x=\frac{A}{A+B}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Define the likelihood-odds function <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(u)=u/(1-u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(u)=u/(1-u)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G:=\frac{x}{1-x}=\frac{A}{B}=\bigl[h(x_{1})\bigr]^{\beta_{1}}\,\bigl[h(x_{2})\bigr]^{\beta_{2}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G:=\frac{x}{1-x}=\frac{A}{B}=\bigl[h(x_{1})\bigr]^{\beta_{1}}\,\bigl[h(x_{2})\bigr]^{\beta_{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">the weighted geometric mean of <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(x_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(x_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(x_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(x_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. Taking logarithms on both sides, we have</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log G=\beta_{1}\log h(x_{1})+(1-\beta_{1})\log h(x_{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log G=\beta_{1}\log h(x_{1})+(1-\beta_{1})\log h(x_{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">Without loss of generality, assume that <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}&lt;x_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}&lt;x_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Clearly <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log G</annotation></semantics></math> is a decreasing function with respect to <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(u)</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly increasing on <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. This gives that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log h(x_{1})&lt;\log G&lt;\log h(x_{2})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log h(x_{1})&lt;\log G&lt;\log h(x_{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p8.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p8.5.1" class="ltx_text">and exponentiating both sides gives</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(x_{1})&lt;\frac{x}{1-x}&lt;h(x_{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(x_{1})&lt;\frac{x}{1-x}&lt;h(x_{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p8.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p8.6.1" class="ltx_text">Applying the inverse <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{-1}(v)=v/(1+v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{-1}(v)=v/(1+v)</annotation></semantics></math>, which is also strictly increasing, yields</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}\;&lt;\;x\;&lt;\;x_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">&lt;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">&lt;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}\;&lt;\;x\;&lt;\;x_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p8.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p8.7.1" class="ltx_text">The final step is to analyze the signs of <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{1}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{1}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{2}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{2}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>. Since we have established that <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}&lt;x&lt;x_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}&lt;x&lt;x_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that the term <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x-x_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x-x_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> is always positive and <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x-x_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x-x_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> is always negative. The sign of the log-odds term, <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\frac{x_{i}}{1-x_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\frac{x_{i}}{1-x_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>, depends on whether <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is greater or less than <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/2</annotation></semantics></math>. We proceed with a case analysis. We first analyze the case in which beliefs <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are on the same side of <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/2</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/2&lt;x_{1}&lt;x_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/2&lt;x_{1}&lt;x_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\frac{x_{1}}{1-x_{1}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\frac{x_{1}}{1-x_{1}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\frac{x_{2}}{1-x_{2}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\frac{x_{2}}{1-x_{2}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. This yields:</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{1}(x)=\underbrace{(x-x_{1})}_{&gt;0}\underbrace{\log\frac{x_{1}}{1-x_{1}}}_{&gt;0}&gt;0\quad\text{and}\quad\Delta_{2}(x)=\underbrace{(x-x_{2})}_{&lt;0}\underbrace{\log\frac{x_{2}}{1-x_{2}}}_{&gt;0}&lt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{1}(x)=\underbrace{(x-x_{1})}_{&gt;0}\underbrace{\log\frac{x_{1}}{1-x_{1}}}_{&gt;0}&gt;0\quad\text{and}\quad\Delta_{2}(x)=\underbrace{(x-x_{2})}_{&lt;0}\underbrace{\log\frac{x_{2}}{1-x_{2}}}_{&gt;0}&lt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p8.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p8.8.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, if <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}&lt;x_{2}&lt;1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}&lt;x_{2}&lt;1/2</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\frac{x_{1}}{1-x_{1}}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\frac{x_{1}}{1-x_{1}}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\frac{x_{2}}{1-x_{2}}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\frac{x_{2}}{1-x_{2}}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. This yields:</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{1}(x)=\underbrace{(x-x_{1})}_{&gt;0}\underbrace{\log\frac{x_{1}}{1-x_{1}}}_{&lt;0}&lt;0\quad\text{and}\quad\Delta_{2}(x)=\underbrace{(x-x_{2})}_{&lt;0}\underbrace{\log\frac{x_{2}}{1-x_{2}}}_{&lt;0}&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{1}(x)=\underbrace{(x-x_{1})}_{&gt;0}\underbrace{\log\frac{x_{1}}{1-x_{1}}}_{&lt;0}&lt;0\quad\text{and}\quad\Delta_{2}(x)=\underbrace{(x-x_{2})}_{&lt;0}\underbrace{\log\frac{x_{2}}{1-x_{2}}}_{&lt;0}&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p8.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p8.9.1" class="ltx_text">In either subcase, one agent’s welfare improves while the other’s worsens. Otherwise, the beliefs must be on opposite sides of <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/2</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}&lt;1/2&lt;x_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}&lt;1/2&lt;x_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\frac{x_{1}}{1-x_{1}}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\frac{x_{1}}{1-x_{1}}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\frac{x_{2}}{1-x_{2}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\frac{x_{2}}{1-x_{2}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. This yields:</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{1}(x)=\underbrace{(x-x_{1})}_{&gt;0}\underbrace{\log\frac{x_{1}}{1-x_{1}}}_{&lt;0}&lt;0\quad\text{and}\quad\Delta_{2}(x)=\underbrace{(x-x_{2})}_{&lt;0}\underbrace{\log\frac{x_{2}}{1-x_{2}}}_{&gt;0}&lt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{1}(x)=\underbrace{(x-x_{1})}_{&gt;0}\underbrace{\log\frac{x_{1}}{1-x_{1}}}_{&lt;0}&lt;0\quad\text{and}\quad\Delta_{2}(x)=\underbrace{(x-x_{2})}_{&lt;0}\underbrace{\log\frac{x_{2}}{1-x_{2}}}_{&gt;0}&lt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p8.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p8.10.1" class="ltx_text">In this case, the welfare of both agents worsens. Thus in all possible cases, at least one agent incurs a strictly negative welfare gap. It is therefore impossible for both <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> to be non-negative with at least one being strictly positive.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">The binary impossibility reflects a tension inherent to averaging on a log scale: increasing one agent’s log likelihood necessarily decreases another’s when only two alternatives exist.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Abstract Existence for Larger Outcome Spaces</h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When the outcome space has at least three elements, unanimously beneficial compositions do exist. We first establish existence in a constructive way by exhibiting a family of beliefs and welfare functions that guarantee positive welfare gains for all agents.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem34" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem34.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 34</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem34.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Existence of unanimously compositional groups)<span id="Thmtheorem34.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem34.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem34.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem34.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem34.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> and suppose <math id="Thmtheorem34.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{O}|\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{O}|\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>. Then there exist probability distributions <math id="Thmtheorem34.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{P_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{P_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="Thmtheorem34.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math>, welfare functions <math id="Thmtheorem34.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}(o)=\log P_{i}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}(o)=\log P_{i}(o)</annotation></semantics></math>, and equal weights <math id="Thmtheorem34.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}=1/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}=1/n</annotation></semantics></math>, such that under the logarithmic pool every agent strictly benefits: <math id="Thmtheorem34.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E_{P}[W_{i}]&gt;\E_{P_{i}}[W_{i}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">P</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E_{P}[W_{i}]&gt;\E_{P_{i}}[W_{i}]</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmtheorem34.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We provide an explicit construction in the next subsection, showing that such distributions exist for any <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> when the number of outcomes is at least three. The key idea is to choose beliefs that assign small probability to distinct outcomes while concentrating mass on a common “default” outcome. Under the log-pool, the default outcome becomes highly likely, increasing each agent’s entropy and thus its expected log likelihood. We will quantify this effect below.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">E.2.1 </span>Explicit Analytic Construction</h4>

<div id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now present a concrete family of distributions that realize the existence theorem. Fix an integer <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> and choose an outcome space
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}=\{o_{0},o_{1},o_{2},\dots,o_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}=\{o_{0},o_{1},o_{2},\dots,o_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math>
of size <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n+1</annotation></semantics></math>. Select a small parameter <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in\bigl(0,\tfrac{1}{4}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in\bigl(0,\tfrac{1}{4}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math> and define two auxiliary quantities</p>
<table id="A5.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=\varepsilon,\quad\delta=\varepsilon^{n+1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=\varepsilon,\quad\delta=\varepsilon^{n+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We define each agent <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,\dots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,\dots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math> to be weakly suggestive on seeing a private outcome <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, almost certain about a shared base outcome <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, and very unlikely to see the remaining outcomes. Specifically, let</p>
<table id="A5.Ex70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}(o)=\begin{cases}\alpha,&amp;\text{if }o=o_{i},\\
1-\alpha-(n-1)\delta,&amp;\text{if }o=o_{0},\\
\delta,&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>otherwise</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}(o)=\begin{cases}\alpha,&amp;\text{if }o=o_{i},\\
1-\alpha-(n-1)\delta,&amp;\text{if }o=o_{0},\\
\delta,&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Because <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha+(n-1)\delta+\bigl(1-\alpha-(n-1)\delta\bigr)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha+(n-1)\delta+\bigl(1-\alpha-(n-1)\delta\bigr)=1</annotation></semantics></math>, this defines a valid distribution. The welfare function for each agent is <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}(o)=\log P_{i}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}(o)=\log P_{i}(o)</annotation></semantics></math>. We assign uniform weights <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}=1/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}=1/n</annotation></semantics></math> and form the composition belief under the logarithmic pool. We claim that for <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> sufficiently small, every agent’s expected log likelihood strictly increases.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem35" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem35.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 35</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem35.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Analytic construction for unanimity)<span id="Thmtheorem35.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem35.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem35.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem35.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem35.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> and define beliefs <math id="Thmtheorem35.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> as above. Form the logarithmic pool with weights <math id="Thmtheorem35.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}=1/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}=1/n</annotation></semantics></math> and denote the resulting distribution by <math id="Thmtheorem35.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>. There exists <math id="Thmtheorem35.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all <math id="Thmtheorem35.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in(0,\varepsilon_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in(0,\varepsilon_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, the expected welfare difference
<math id="Thmtheorem35.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}=\E_{P}[\log P_{i}]-\E_{P_{i}}[\log P_{i}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">P</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">P</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">P</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}=\E_{P}[\log P_{i}]-\E_{P_{i}}[\log P_{i}]</annotation></semantics></math>
is strictly positive for every agent <math id="Thmtheorem35.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, the set of agents is unanimously compositional.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We estimate orders of magnitude to show that positive gains dominate negative contributions for sufficiently small <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. For each outcome <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\in\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\in\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> the normalized log pool assigns weight</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(o)=\prod_{j=1}^{n}P_{j}(o)^{1/n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(o)=\prod_{j=1}^{n}P_{j}(o)^{1/n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o=o_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o=o_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, then each factor contributes <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\alpha-(n-1)\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\alpha-(n-1)\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, thus we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(o_{0})=(1-\alpha-(n-1)\delta)^{n\cdot 1/n}=1-\alpha-(n-1)\delta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(o_{0})=(1-\alpha-(n-1)\delta)^{n\cdot 1/n}=1-\alpha-(n-1)\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o=o_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o=o_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for some agent <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, then agent <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> assigns probability <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> while all other <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-1</annotation></semantics></math> agents assign probability <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(o_{i})=\alpha^{1/n}\,\delta^{1-1/n}=\varepsilon^{n}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(o_{i})=\alpha^{1/n}\,\delta^{1-1/n}=\varepsilon^{n}.</annotation></semantics></math>
Meanwhile, we have</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(o_{0})=1-\alpha-(n-1)\delta=1-\varepsilon+o(\varepsilon)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(o_{0})=1-\alpha-(n-1)\delta=1-\varepsilon+o(\varepsilon).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Normalizing gives</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(o_{0})=\frac{R(o_{0})}{R(o_{0})+\sum_{i=1}^{n}R(o_{i})}=1-O(\varepsilon^{n})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(o_{0})=\frac{R(o_{0})}{R(o_{0})+\sum_{i=1}^{n}R(o_{i})}=1-O(\varepsilon^{n}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">where the second term in the denominator is of order <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\varepsilon^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\varepsilon^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and thus much smaller than <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> assigns nearly all of its mass to <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and vanishingly small mass (of order <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>) to each of the other outcomes.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">The entropy of <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is dominated by the uncertainty between <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> (which has probability roughly <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>) and <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (probability <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>), with negligible contribution from the <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-1</annotation></semantics></math> rare events. A short calculation shows</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(P_{i})=-\bigl(1-\alpha-(n-1)\delta\bigr)\log\bigl(1-\alpha-(n-1)\delta\bigr)-\alpha\log\alpha+O(\delta\log\tfrac{1}{\delta})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(P_{i})=-\bigl(1-\alpha-(n-1)\delta\bigr)\log\bigl(1-\alpha-(n-1)\delta\bigr)-\alpha\log\alpha+O(\delta\log\tfrac{1}{\delta}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Using <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=\varepsilon^{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=\varepsilon^{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(P_{i})=\Theta\bigl(\varepsilon\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}\bigr)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(P_{i})=\Theta\bigl(\varepsilon\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math>
By contrast, the composition belief <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> puts probability <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-O(\varepsilon^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-O(\varepsilon^{n})</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and distributes the remaining mass evenly among <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> outcomes of order <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(P)=O\bigl(\varepsilon^{n}\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}\bigr)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(P)=O\bigl(\varepsilon^{n}\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math>
which is of much smaller order than <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(P_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(P_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the entropy difference <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(P_{i})-H(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(P_{i})-H(P)</annotation></semantics></math> scales like <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\log(1/\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\log(1/\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">It remains to bound <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{KL}}(P\|P_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{KL}}(P\|P_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> places mass <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\theta</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta=O(\varepsilon^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta=O(\varepsilon^{n})</annotation></semantics></math>, we may write</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{KL}}(P\|P_{i})=(1-\theta)\log\frac{1-\theta}{1-\alpha-(n-1)\delta}+\frac{\theta}{n}\log\frac{\theta}{n\alpha}+\frac{(n-1)\theta}{n}\log\frac{\theta}{n\delta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>θ</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{KL}}(P\|P_{i})=(1-\theta)\log\frac{1-\theta}{1-\alpha-(n-1)\delta}+\frac{\theta}{n}\log\frac{\theta}{n\alpha}+\frac{(n-1)\theta}{n}\log\frac{\theta}{n\delta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Using expansions <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(1-\theta)=-\theta+O(\theta^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(1-\theta)=-\theta+O(\theta^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> and noting that <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\alpha-(n-1)\delta=1-\varepsilon+o(\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\alpha-(n-1)\delta=1-\varepsilon+o(\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>, one finds
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{KL}}(P\|P_{i})=O(\varepsilon)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{KL}}(P\|P_{i})=O(\varepsilon).</annotation></semantics></math>
In particular, the KL divergence is of lower order than the entropy gap when <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is small. That is, recall that
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta_{i}=H(P_{i})-H(P)-D_{\mathrm{KL}}(P\|P_{i})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}=H(P_{i})-H(P)-D_{\mathrm{KL}}(P\|P_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math>
Combining the estimates above shows that <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(P_{i})-H(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(P_{i})-H(P)</annotation></semantics></math> is positive and dominates <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p4.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{KL}}(P\|P_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{KL}}(P\|P_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> sufficiently small. Hence <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for all agents. Selecting <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> small enough completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The construction in Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem35" title="Theorem 35 (Analytic construction for unanimity). ‣ E.2.1 Explicit Analytic Construction ‣ E.2 Abstract Existence for Larger Outcome Spaces ‣ Appendix E Possible and Impossible Compositions ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a> generalizes to arbitrary weights and larger outcome spaces, showing that diversity of possible outcomes enables mutually beneficial compositions.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">E.2.2 </span>Generalization to Arbitrary Weights</h4>

<div id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now show that the same analytic construction for the <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> yields unanimously beneficial compositions for any non-degenerate choice of weights. We allow an <em id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">arbitrary</em> weight vector
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=(\beta_{1},\dots,\beta_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=(\beta_{1},\dots,\beta_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. The construction is trivial if some <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and the rest <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, thus we assume <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{i}\beta_{i}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{i}\beta_{i}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem36" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem36.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 36</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem36.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Unanimity for general weights)<span id="Thmtheorem36.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem36.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem36.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem36.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists <math id="Thmtheorem36.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> depending only on <math id="Thmtheorem36.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem36.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> such
that for all <math id="Thmtheorem36.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;\varepsilon_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;\varepsilon_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem36.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="Thmtheorem36.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> is the logarithmic pool
<math id="Thmtheorem36.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(o)=\frac{1}{Z}\prod_{j=1}^{n}P_{j}(o)^{\beta_{j}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>Z</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(o)=\frac{1}{Z}\prod_{j=1}^{n}P_{j}(o)^{\beta_{j}}.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Write
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(o)=\prod_{j=1}^{n}P_{j}(o)^{\beta_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(o)=\prod_{j=1}^{n}P_{j}(o)^{\beta_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math>
for the unnormalized weight and
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=\sum_{o\in\mathcal{O}}R(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=\sum_{o\in\mathcal{O}}R(o)</annotation></semantics></math>
for the partition function. Throughout, we have <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\min}:=\min_{i}\bigl((n+1)-n\beta_{i}\bigr)&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\min}:=\min_{i}\bigl((n+1)-n\beta_{i}\bigr)&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> because <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{i}\beta_{i}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{i}\beta_{i}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. At the shared outcome <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, every agent contributes
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\alpha-(n-1)\delta=1-\varepsilon+O(\varepsilon^{\,n+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\alpha-(n-1)\delta=1-\varepsilon+O(\varepsilon^{\,n+1})</annotation></semantics></math>, so</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(o_{0})=\exp\Bigl(\sum_{j=1}^{n}\beta_{j}\log\bigl(1-\varepsilon+O(\varepsilon^{\,n+1})\bigr)\Bigr)=1-\varepsilon+O(\varepsilon^{\,n+1})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(o_{0})=\exp\Bigl(\sum_{j=1}^{n}\beta_{j}\log\bigl(1-\varepsilon+O(\varepsilon^{\,n+1})\bigr)\Bigr)=1-\varepsilon+O(\varepsilon^{\,n+1}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">because <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j}\beta_{j}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j}\beta_{j}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. For a private outcome <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th agent contributes <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>
and each of the other <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-1</annotation></semantics></math> agents contributes <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=\varepsilon^{\,n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=\varepsilon^{\,n+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. We therefore have</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(o_{i})=\varepsilon^{\beta_{i}}\,(\varepsilon^{\,n+1})^{1-\beta_{i}}=\varepsilon^{\beta_{i}+(n+1)(1-\beta_{i})}=\varepsilon^{\,c_{i}},\qquad c_{i}:=(n+1)-n\beta_{i}\;&gt;\;1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn> 1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(o_{i})=\varepsilon^{\beta_{i}}\,(\varepsilon^{\,n+1})^{1-\beta_{i}}=\varepsilon^{\beta_{i}+(n+1)(1-\beta_{i})}=\varepsilon^{\,c_{i}},\qquad c_{i}:=(n+1)-n\beta_{i}\;&gt;\;1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(o_{i})=\varepsilon^{c_{i}}=o(\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(o_{i})=\varepsilon^{c_{i}}=o(\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>, the partition function is</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=R(o_{0})+\sum_{i=1}^{n}R(o_{i})=1-\varepsilon+\sum_{i=1}^{n}\varepsilon^{c_{i}}+O(\varepsilon^{\,n+1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=R(o_{0})+\sum_{i=1}^{n}R(o_{i})=1-\varepsilon+\sum_{i=1}^{n}\varepsilon^{c_{i}}+O(\varepsilon^{\,n+1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Dividing by <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(o_{0})=\frac{1-\varepsilon+O(\varepsilon^{\,n+1})}{1-\varepsilon+\sum_{i}\varepsilon^{c_{i}}+O(\varepsilon^{\,n+1})}=1-\Theta\bigl(\varepsilon^{c_{\min}}\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(o_{0})=\frac{1-\varepsilon+O(\varepsilon^{\,n+1})}{1-\varepsilon+\sum_{i}\varepsilon^{c_{i}}+O(\varepsilon^{\,n+1})}=1-\Theta\bigl(\varepsilon^{c_{\min}}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">because the numerator and denominator differ only by
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(\varepsilon^{c_{\min}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(\varepsilon^{c_{\min}})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\min}&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\min}&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. Likewise,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(o_{i})=\frac{\varepsilon^{c_{i}}}{1-\varepsilon+o(1)}=\Theta\bigl(\varepsilon^{c_{i}}\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(o_{i})=\frac{\varepsilon^{c_{i}}}{1-\varepsilon+o(1)}=\Theta\bigl(\varepsilon^{c_{i}}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">For agent <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, only <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> carry mass larger than
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=\varepsilon^{\,n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=\varepsilon^{\,n+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, so as <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\to 0^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\to 0^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle H(P_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H(P_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex82.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-(1-\varepsilon)\log(1-\varepsilon)-\varepsilon\log\varepsilon-(n-1)\delta\log\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-(1-\varepsilon)\log(1-\varepsilon)-\varepsilon\log\varepsilon-(n-1)\delta\log\delta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\varepsilon\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}+O(\varepsilon)+O\bigl((n^{2}-1)\varepsilon^{\,n+1}\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\varepsilon\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}+O(\varepsilon)+O\bigl((n^{2}-1)\varepsilon^{\,n+1}\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex84"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Theta\bigl(\varepsilon\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}\bigr)&gt;0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Theta\bigl(\varepsilon\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}\bigr)&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.7.1" class="ltx_text">The leakage mass is
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta:=1-P(o_{0})=\Theta(\varepsilon^{c_{\min}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta:=1-P(o_{0})=\Theta(\varepsilon^{c_{\min}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
It is split across at most <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> outcomes, each of size
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(\varepsilon^{c_{i}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(\varepsilon^{c_{i}})</annotation></semantics></math>. The entropy is</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex85"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle H(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H(P)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex85.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-P(o_{0})\log P(o_{0})-\sum_{i=1}^{n}P(o_{i})\log P(o_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-P(o_{0})\log P(o_{0})-\sum_{i=1}^{n}P(o_{i})\log P(o_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex86"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-(1-\theta)\log(1-\theta)-\sum_{i=1}^{n}P(o_{i})\log P(o_{i})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-(1-\theta)\log(1-\theta)-\sum_{i=1}^{n}P(o_{i})\log P(o_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.8.1" class="ltx_text">For the <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> term, we have</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex87" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-(1-\theta)\log(1-\theta)=\theta+O(\theta^{2})=O(\theta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-(1-\theta)\log(1-\theta)=\theta+O(\theta^{2})=O(\theta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.9.1" class="ltx_text">For the leakage terms, each <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(o_{i})=\Theta(\varepsilon^{c_{i}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(o_{i})=\Theta(\varepsilon^{c_{i}})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}\geq c_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}\geq c_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math>, so we may write asymptotically</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex88" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(o_{i})=K_{i}\,\varepsilon^{c_{i}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(o_{i})=K_{i}\,\varepsilon^{c_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.10.1" class="ltx_text">for some constant <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> independent of <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex89" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log P(o_{i})=\log K_{i}+c_{i}\log\varepsilon=\log K_{i}-c_{i}\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log P(o_{i})=\log K_{i}+c_{i}\log\varepsilon=\log K_{i}-c_{i}\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.11.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex90"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-P(o_{i})\log P(o_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-P(o_{i})\log P(o_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex90.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-K_{i}\,\varepsilon^{c_{i}}\Big(\log K_{i}-c_{i}\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-K_{i}\,\varepsilon^{c_{i}}\Big(\log K_{i}-c_{i}\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex91"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=c_{i}\,K_{i}\,\varepsilon^{c_{i}}\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}\;-\;K_{i}\,\varepsilon^{c_{i}}\log K_{i}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=c_{i}\,K_{i}\,\varepsilon^{c_{i}}\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}\;-\;K_{i}\,\varepsilon^{c_{i}}\log K_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.12.1" class="ltx_text">As <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\to 0^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\to 0^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, the constant term <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{i}\,\varepsilon^{c_{i}}\log K_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{i}\,\varepsilon^{c_{i}}\log K_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is dominated by the
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon^{c_{i}}\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon^{c_{i}}\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> term, so</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex92" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-P(o_{i})\log P(o_{i})=\Theta\bigl(\varepsilon^{c_{i}}\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-P(o_{i})\log P(o_{i})=\Theta\bigl(\varepsilon^{c_{i}}\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.13.1" class="ltx_text">Summing over at most <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> such terms yields</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex93" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex93.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{n}-P(o_{i})\log P(o_{i})=\Theta(\varepsilon^{c_{\min}}\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></msup><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{n}-P(o_{i})\log P(o_{i})=\Theta(\varepsilon^{c_{\min}}\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.14.1" class="ltx_text">Combining the above gives that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex94" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(P)=O(\theta)+\Theta(\varepsilon^{c_{\min}}\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon})=\Theta(\varepsilon^{c_{\min}}\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(P)=O(\theta)+\Theta(\varepsilon^{c_{\min}}\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon})=\Theta(\varepsilon^{c_{\min}}\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.15" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.15.1" class="ltx_text">and since <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\min}&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\min}&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, this term decays at the order of <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o(\varepsilon\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o(\varepsilon\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math>. Now, write <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0}:=P(o_{0})=1-\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0}:=P(o_{0})=1-\theta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}:=P(o_{i})=\Theta(\varepsilon^{c_{i}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}:=P(o_{i})=\Theta(\varepsilon^{c_{i}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex95" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex95.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{KL}}(P\|P_{i})=p_{0}\log\frac{p_{0}}{P_{i}(o_{0})}+p_{i}\log\frac{p_{i}}{P_{i}(o_{i})}+\sum_{o\notin\{o_{0},o_{i}\}}P(o)\log\frac{P(o)}{\delta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>log</mi><mfrac><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mfrac><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{KL}}(P\|P_{i})=p_{0}\log\frac{p_{0}}{P_{i}(o_{0})}+p_{i}\log\frac{p_{i}}{P_{i}(o_{i})}+\sum_{o\notin\{o_{0},o_{i}\}}P(o)\log\frac{P(o)}{\delta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.16" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.16.1" class="ltx_text">We control the first term by noting <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}(o_{0})=1-\varepsilon+O(\varepsilon^{n+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}(o_{0})=1-\varepsilon+O(\varepsilon^{n+1})</annotation></semantics></math>. Using <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(1-\theta)=-\theta+O(\theta^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(1-\theta)=-\theta+O(\theta^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> and the fact that both <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}(o_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}(o_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> are close to 1, we have</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex96" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0}\log\frac{p_{0}}{P_{i}(o_{0})}=p_{0}\bigl[\log(1-\theta)-\log(1-\varepsilon+O(\varepsilon^{n+1}))\bigr]=O(\varepsilon)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0}\log\frac{p_{0}}{P_{i}(o_{0})}=p_{0}\bigl[\log(1-\theta)-\log(1-\varepsilon+O(\varepsilon^{n+1}))\bigr]=O(\varepsilon).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.17" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.17.1" class="ltx_text">For the second term, we have <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}(o_{i})=\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}(o_{i})=\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> which gives</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex97" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}\log\frac{p_{i}}{P_{i}(o_{i})}=\Theta(\varepsilon^{c_{i}})\log\frac{\Theta(\varepsilon^{c_{i}})}{\varepsilon}=\Theta(\varepsilon^{c_{i}}\log\varepsilon^{c_{i}-1})=\Theta(\varepsilon^{c_{i}}\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}\log\frac{p_{i}}{P_{i}(o_{i})}=\Theta(\varepsilon^{c_{i}})\log\frac{\Theta(\varepsilon^{c_{i}})}{\varepsilon}=\Theta(\varepsilon^{c_{i}}\log\varepsilon^{c_{i}-1})=\Theta(\varepsilon^{c_{i}}\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.18" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.18.1" class="ltx_text">Here, we used that <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}-1&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}-1&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant. For the third term, there are at most <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m44" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-1</annotation></semantics></math> outcomes with <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m45" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(o)=\Theta(\varepsilon^{c_{k}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(o)=\Theta(\varepsilon^{c_{k}})</annotation></semantics></math>, and for each such <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m46" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m47" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}(o)=\delta=\varepsilon^{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}(o)=\delta=\varepsilon^{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex98" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(o)\log\frac{P(o)}{\delta}=\Theta(\varepsilon^{c_{k}})\log\frac{\Theta(\varepsilon^{c_{k}})}{\varepsilon^{n+1}}=\Theta(\varepsilon^{c_{k}}\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(o)\log\frac{P(o)}{\delta}=\Theta(\varepsilon^{c_{k}})\log\frac{\Theta(\varepsilon^{c_{k}})}{\varepsilon^{n+1}}=\Theta(\varepsilon^{c_{k}}\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.19" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.19.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m48" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}\geq c_{\min}&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}\geq c_{\min}&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, all contributions are <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m49" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\varepsilon^{c_{\min}}\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\varepsilon^{c_{\min}}\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math>. Adding the three terms gives</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex99" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex99.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{KL}}(P\|P_{i})=O(\varepsilon)+O\big(\varepsilon^{c_{\min}}\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></msup><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{KL}}(P\|P_{i})=O(\varepsilon)+O\big(\varepsilon^{c_{\min}}\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.20" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.20.1" class="ltx_text">Using <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m50" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta_{i}=H(P_{i})-H(P)-D_{\mathrm{KL}}(P\|P_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}=H(P_{i})-H(P)-D_{\mathrm{KL}}(P\|P_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> from Proposition <a href="#Thmtheorem32" title="Proposition 32 (Welfare gap identity for logarithmic utility). ‣ E.1 Impossibility in the Binary Case ‣ Appendix E Possible and Impossible Compositions ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex100" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}=\underbrace{\Theta\big(\varepsilon\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}\big)}_{H(P_{i})}\;-\;\underbrace{o\big(\varepsilon\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}\big)}_{H(P)}\;-\;\underbrace{\Big(O(\varepsilon)+O\big(\varepsilon^{c_{\min}}\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}\big)\Big)}_{D_{\mathrm{KL}}}=\varepsilon\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}\,\Big(\Theta(1)-o(1)\Big)-O(\varepsilon)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub></munder></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}=\underbrace{\Theta\big(\varepsilon\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}\big)}_{H(P_{i})}\;-\;\underbrace{o\big(\varepsilon\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}\big)}_{H(P)}\;-\;\underbrace{\Big(O(\varepsilon)+O\big(\varepsilon^{c_{\min}}\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}\big)\Big)}_{D_{\mathrm{KL}}}=\varepsilon\log\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}\,\Big(\Theta(1)-o(1)\Big)-O(\varepsilon).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.21" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.21.1" class="ltx_text">Because <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m51" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\min}&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\min}&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, the negative term is of higher order in
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m52" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>; hence <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m53" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m54" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> when
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m55" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;\varepsilon_{0}(\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;\varepsilon_{0}(\beta)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m56" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> chosen small
enough. In other words, since <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m57" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\log(1/\varepsilon)\gg\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≫</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\log(1/\varepsilon)\gg\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m58" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\to 0^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\to 0^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m59" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> (depending only on <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m60" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta,n</annotation></semantics></math> through the constants above) such that <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m61" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m62" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> whenever <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m63" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;\varepsilon_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;\varepsilon_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.3 </span>Impossibility of Strictly Unanimous Benefit under Linear Pooling</h3>

<div id="A5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section we show that if each agent’s welfare is defined by the log-score of its <em id="A5.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">own</em> belief and the group aggregates beliefs via the <em id="A5.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">linear</em> opinion pool, then no strictly unanimously beneficial composition can exist.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem37" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem37.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 37</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem37.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Impossibility under linear opinion pool)<span id="Thmtheorem37.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem37.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem37.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem37.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem37.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of agents. For each <math id="Thmtheorem37.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\dots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\dots,n</annotation></semantics></math>, let</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex101" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}:\mathcal{O}\to[0,1],\quad\sum_{o\in\mathcal{O}}P_{i}(o)=1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.000em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}:\mathcal{O}\to[0,1],\quad\sum_{o\in\mathcal{O}}P_{i}(o)=1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem37.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem37.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">be distinct probability distributions, and let weights
<math id="Thmtheorem37.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy <math id="Thmtheorem37.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Suppose each agent’s welfare function is the log-score of its own belief,
<math id="Thmtheorem37.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}(o)\;=\;\log P_{i}(o)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}(o)\;=\;\log P_{i}(o).</annotation></semantics></math>
Then, it is impossible to have</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex102" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex102.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E_{P}[W_{i}]\;\geq\;\E_{P_{i}}[W_{i}]\quad\text{for all }i," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E_{P}[W_{i}]\;\geq\;\E_{P_{i}}[W_{i}]\quad\text{for all }i,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem37.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem37.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with <em id="Thmtheorem37.p1.3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">strict</em> inequality for at least one <math id="Thmtheorem37.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. In other words, no strictly unanimously beneficial composition exists.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall proposition <a href="#Thmtheorem32" title="Proposition 32 (Welfare gap identity for logarithmic utility). ‣ E.1 Impossibility in the Binary Case ‣ Appendix E Possible and Impossible Compositions ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>. Assume for the sake of contradiction, that <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. Then also
<math id="A5.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\,\Delta_{i}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\,\Delta_{i}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. However, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex103" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex103X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex103X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\,\Delta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\,\Delta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex103X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\bigl[H(P_{i})-H(P)-D_{\mathrm{KL}}(P\|P_{i})\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\bigl[H(P_{i})-H(P)-D_{\mathrm{KL}}(P\|P_{i})\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex103Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex103Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Bigl(\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\,H(P_{i})\Bigr)\;-\;H(P)\;-\;\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\,D_{\mathrm{KL}}\bigl(P\|P_{i}\bigr)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Bigl(\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\,H(P_{i})\Bigr)\;-\;H(P)\;-\;\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\,D_{\mathrm{KL}}\bigl(P\|P_{i}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Because <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly concave on the simplex,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex104" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex104.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(P)=H\Bigl(\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\,P_{i}\Bigr)\;&gt;\;\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\,H(P_{i})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">&gt;</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(P)=H\Bigl(\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\,P_{i}\Bigr)\;&gt;\;\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\,H(P_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">whenever the <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are not all identical. Hence
<math id="A5.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}\beta_{i}\,H(P_{i})-H(P)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}\beta_{i}\,H(P_{i})-H(P)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Each term <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{KL}}(P\|P_{i})\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{KL}}(P\|P_{i})\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, so this gives that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex105" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex105.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\,\Delta_{i}\;=\;\bigl[\sum_{i}\beta_{i}\,H(P_{i})-H(P)\bigr]\;-\;\sum_{i}\beta_{i}\,D_{\mathrm{KL}}(P\|P_{i})\;&lt;\;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.335em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn> 0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\,\Delta_{i}\;=\;\bigl[\sum_{i}\beta_{i}\,H(P_{i})-H(P)\bigr]\;-\;\sum_{i}\beta_{i}\,D_{\mathrm{KL}}(P\|P_{i})\;&lt;\;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">This contradicts <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}\beta_{i}\,\Delta_{i}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}\beta_{i}\,\Delta_{i}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore our assumption
that <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> must be false: at least one <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. We note that in the degenerate case <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}=\cdots=P_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}=\cdots=P_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P=P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P=P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> which gives
<math id="A5.SS3.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(P)=H(P_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(P)=H(P_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m16" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{KL}}(P\|P_{i})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{KL}}(P\|P_{i})=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence each
<math id="A5.SS3.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. No agent strictly gains, and the composition is
<em id="A5.SS3.p2.4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">not</em> strictly beneficial.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, a linear pooling does not admit a strictly compositional group under the epistemic utility. However, a logarithmic pool does allow for a strictly unanimous compositional group.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Recursing on Compositional Agents for Scale-Free Theory</h2>

<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Recursion on Agents and Subagent Decomposition.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A natural question is whether the compositional property is preserved under recursive decomposition. Suppose a compositional agent is split into a fixed number of <em id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">subagents</em>, each representing a distinct component of its preferences (e.g., an individual’s drives to eat, sleep, or play). Does compositionality of the parent agent imply that each subagent is also compositional with respect to the same group?</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In general, the answer is negative: decomposition can destroy compositionality. An individual may align with a group overall, yet certain subagents–such as the drive to eat–may diverge from the group’s objectives (e.g., productivity), even while remaining consistent with the parent’s broader goals.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">From a scale-free perspective, a fully recursive theory would require that an agent be decomposable into an arbitrary number of subagents, while preserving both (i) recovery of the original agent via log-pooling and (ii) preservation of the unanimously compositional structure. We will show that property (ii) does not hold in general: recursive decomposition can eliminate unanimity. This raises a natural direction for future work: characterizing conditions under which subagents <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1},\dots,P_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1},\dots,P_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> can be constructed so that their aggregation remains unanimously compositional, even when the subagents are not known <em id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">a priori</em>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem38" title="Theorem 38 (Non-trivial log–pool decomposition always exists when 𝑃 is strictly positive). ‣ Recursion on Agents and Subagent Decomposition. ‣ Appendix F Recursing on Compositional Agents for Scale-Free Theory ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38</span></a>, we formalize the property that an agent can be decomposed into a fixed number of subagents, where this number may be arbitrarily large. Conceptually, one might think of a human being as possessing a seemingly unbounded set of desires or goals–some overlapping, others highly correlated. Our framework is designed to accommodate such decompositions. For example, an individual’s epistemic state might be represented as the aggregation of subagents corresponding to desires for nourishment, social interaction, intellectual stimulation, and so forth, each contributing to the overall belief distribution.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Building upon Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem38" title="Theorem 38 (Non-trivial log–pool decomposition always exists when 𝑃 is strictly positive). ‣ Recursion on Agents and Subagent Decomposition. ‣ Appendix F Recursing on Compositional Agents for Scale-Free Theory ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38</span></a>, we extend the analysis in Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem39" title="Theorem 39 (Log–pool factorization with pairwise-distinct components). ‣ Recursion on Agents and Subagent Decomposition. ‣ Appendix F Recursing on Compositional Agents for Scale-Free Theory ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">39</span></a> to the case where the subagents are pairwise distinct, representing genuinely different desires. This constraint captures scenarios in which each subagent embodies a unique epistemic or utility perspective, ensuring that the decomposition meaningfully differentiates between components of the agent’s overall decision-making process.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem38" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem38.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 38</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem38.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Non-trivial log–pool decomposition always exists when <math id="Thmtheorem38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly positive)<span id="Thmtheorem38.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem38.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem38.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem38.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem38.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> be a finite set, let <math id="Thmtheorem38.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> be a probability distribution on <math id="Thmtheorem38.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> such that
<math id="Thmtheorem38.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(o)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(o)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="Thmtheorem38.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\in\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\in\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math>, and fix weights
<math id="Thmtheorem38.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1},\dots,\beta_{n}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1},\dots,\beta_{n}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmtheorem38.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and
at least two <math id="Thmtheorem38.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> strictly positive.
Then there exist distributions <math id="Thmtheorem38.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1},\dots,P_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1},\dots,P_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="Thmtheorem38.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> distinct from <math id="Thmtheorem38.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex106" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(o)=\frac{1}{Z}\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}},\qquad Z=\sum_{o\in\mathcal{O}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>Z</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(o)=\frac{1}{Z}\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}},\qquad Z=\sum_{o\in\mathcal{O}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Pick any reference distribution <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> with the <em id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">same support</em> as <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q\neq P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q\neq P</annotation></semantics></math>
(e.g. the uniform distribution on <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math>).
Let <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma:=\sum_{i=2}^{n}\beta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma:=\sum_{i=2}^{n}\beta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and assume <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>; the argument is symmetric if a
different index carries the complementary weight.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex107" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{P}_{1}(o)\;=\;\frac{\,P(o)^{\;1/\beta_{1}}\;Q(o)^{-\gamma/\beta_{1}}}{\displaystyle\sum_{o^{\prime}\in\mathcal{O}}P(o^{\prime})^{\;1/\beta_{1}}\,Q(o^{\prime})^{-\gamma/\beta_{1}}},\qquad P_{i}:=Q\;(i=2,\dots,n)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></msub><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0.280em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{P}_{1}(o)\;=\;\frac{\,P(o)^{\;1/\beta_{1}}\;Q(o)^{-\gamma/\beta_{1}}}{\displaystyle\sum_{o^{\prime}\in\mathcal{O}}P(o^{\prime})^{\;1/\beta_{1}}\,Q(o^{\prime})^{-\gamma/\beta_{1}}},\qquad P_{i}:=Q\;(i=2,\dots,n).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Each <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{P}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{P}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is well-defined and strictly positive because
<math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> are strictly positive.
Let <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the denominator in <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{P}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{P}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and set <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}=\tilde{P}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}=\tilde{P}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then for every outcome <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex108"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\log P_{i}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\log P_{i}(o)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex108.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta_{1}\Bigl[\tfrac{1}{\beta_{1}}\log P(o)-\tfrac{\gamma}{\beta_{1}}\log Q(o)-\log Z_{1}\Bigr]+\gamma\log Q(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta_{1}\Bigl[\tfrac{1}{\beta_{1}}\log P(o)-\tfrac{\gamma}{\beta_{1}}\log Q(o)-\log Z_{1}\Bigr]+\gamma\log Q(o)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex109"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log P(o)-\beta_{1}\log Z_{1}\;=\;\log P(o)+C," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log P(o)-\beta_{1}\log Z_{1}\;=\;\log P(o)+C,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C:=-\beta_{1}\log Z_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C:=-\beta_{1}\log Z_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant <em id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7.3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">independent of <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math></em>. Exponentiating and
normalizing by <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z:=e^{-C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z:=e^{-C}</annotation></semantics></math> gives the desired identity. Because <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> was built from both
<math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>, it differs from each, and we have <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\neq P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\neq P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem39" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem39.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 39</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem39.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Log–pool factorization with pairwise-distinct components)<span id="Thmtheorem39.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem39.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem39.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem39.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem39.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> be a finite set and let <math id="Thmtheorem39.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> be a probability distribution on <math id="Thmtheorem39.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmtheorem39.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(o)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(o)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmtheorem39.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\in\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\in\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math>. Fix weights <math id="Thmtheorem39.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1},\dots,\beta_{n}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1},\dots,\beta_{n}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmtheorem39.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, and assume at least two <math id="Thmtheorem39.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are strictly positive. Then there exist probability distributions <math id="Thmtheorem39.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1},\dots,P_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1},\dots,P_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="Thmtheorem39.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex110" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(o)=\frac{1}{Z}\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}}\quad\text{for all }o\in\mathcal{O},\qquad Z=\sum_{o\in\mathcal{O}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>Z</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(o)=\frac{1}{Z}\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}}\quad\text{for all }o\in\mathcal{O},\qquad Z=\sum_{o\in\mathcal{O}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem39.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem39.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with the additional properties that <math id="Thmtheorem39.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\neq P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\neq P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="Thmtheorem39.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem39.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}\neq P_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}\neq P_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> whenever <math id="Thmtheorem39.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Pick any <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-1</annotation></semantics></math> <em id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p8.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">pairwise distinct</em> strictly positive distributions <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{2},\dots,Q_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{2},\dots,Q_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> such that none equals <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>; for instance, start from a positive reference <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\neq P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\neq P</annotation></semantics></math> and set</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex111" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{i}(o)\;\propto\;R(o)\,e^{\varepsilon_{i}h_{i}(o)}\quad(o\in\mathcal{O})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{i}(o)\;\propto\;R(o)\,e^{\varepsilon_{i}h_{i}(o)}\quad(o\in\mathcal{O}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">where each <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{i}:\mathcal{O}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{i}:\mathcal{O}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> has at least two distinct values and <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{o}R(o)h_{i}(o)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>o</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{o}R(o)h_{i}(o)=0</annotation></semantics></math>. We may choose small, distinct <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{i}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{i}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> to ensure <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are strictly positive and pairwise different.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma:=\sum_{i=2}^{n}\beta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma:=\sum_{i=2}^{n}\beta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (which gives <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> by assumption). Define the weighted geometric mean</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex112" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\star}(o)\;:=\;\exp\Bigl(\frac{1}{\gamma}\sum_{i=2}^{n}\beta_{i}\log Q_{i}(o)\Bigr),\qquad\text{so that}\quad\sum_{i=2}^{n}\beta_{i}\log Q_{i}=\gamma\log Q_{\star}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>γ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mtext>so that</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\star}(o)\;:=\;\exp\Bigl(\frac{1}{\gamma}\sum_{i=2}^{n}\beta_{i}\log Q_{i}(o)\Bigr),\qquad\text{so that}\quad\sum_{i=2}^{n}\beta_{i}\log Q_{i}=\gamma\log Q_{\star}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">Now define <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex113" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex113.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}(o)\;=\;\frac{P(o)^{1/\beta_{1}}\,Q_{\star}(o)^{-\gamma/\beta_{1}}}{\displaystyle\sum_{u\in\mathcal{O}}P(u)^{1/\beta_{1}}\,Q_{\star}(u)^{-\gamma/\beta_{1}}}\quad(o\in\mathcal{O})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mi>Q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></msub><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mi>Q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}(o)\;=\;\frac{P(o)^{1/\beta_{1}}\,Q_{\star}(o)^{-\gamma/\beta_{1}}}{\displaystyle\sum_{u\in\mathcal{O}}P(u)^{1/\beta_{1}}\,Q_{\star}(u)^{-\gamma/\beta_{1}}}\quad(o\in\mathcal{O}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">Then, for every <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\in\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\in\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex114" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\log P_{i}(o)=\beta_{1}\left(\tfrac{1}{\beta_{1}}\log P(o)-\tfrac{\gamma}{\beta_{1}}\log Q_{\star}(o)-\log Z_{1}\right)+\sum_{i=2}^{n}\beta_{i}\log Q_{i}(o)=\log P(o)-\beta_{1}\log Z_{1}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\log P_{i}(o)=\beta_{1}\left(\tfrac{1}{\beta_{1}}\log P(o)-\tfrac{\gamma}{\beta_{1}}\log Q_{\star}(o)-\log Z_{1}\right)+\sum_{i=2}^{n}\beta_{i}\log Q_{i}(o)=\log P(o)-\beta_{1}\log Z_{1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p9.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p9.4.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is the normalizing constant in <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Exponentiating and renormalizing shows
<math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{i}P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}}=e^{-\beta_{1}\log Z_{1}}\,P(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{i}P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}}=e^{-\beta_{1}\log Z_{1}}\,P(o)</annotation></semantics></math>, hence the claimed factorization holds with <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=e^{-\beta_{1}\log Z_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=e^{-\beta_{1}\log Z_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">It remains to ensure distinctness. By construction, <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{2},\dots,Q_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{2},\dots,Q_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> are pairwise distinct and differ from <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>. If, for some <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, we had <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}=Q_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}=Q_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, then as the <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> were chosen with free continuous parameters <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\varepsilon_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\varepsilon_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, any generic small perturbation of the <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> keeps the construction valid while ensuring <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}\neq Q_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}\neq Q_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, we can ensure <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}\neq P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}\neq P</annotation></semantics></math>, avoided by the same generic choice. Therefore we may choose <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{2},\dots,Q_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{2},\dots,Q_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> so that <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is distinct from each <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p10.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and from <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p10.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>, completing the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem40" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem40.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 40</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem40.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem40.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem40.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem40.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If some <math id="Thmtheorem40.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the corresponding <math id="Thmtheorem40.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> can be <em id="Thmtheorem40.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">arbitrary</em> and still pairwise distinct; the product is unaffected. The interesting case is that at least two <math id="Thmtheorem40.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, which is assumed above; otherwise the constraint <math id="Thmtheorem40.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P=\Pi P_{i}^{\beta_{i}}/Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P=\Pi P_{i}^{\beta_{i}}/Z</annotation></semantics></math> would force <math id="Thmtheorem40.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P=P_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P=P_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> for the unique <math id="Thmtheorem40.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmtheorem40.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{k}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{k}=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.1" class="ltx_p">We also note that if <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(o^{\star})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(o^{\star})=0</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o^{\star}\in\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{\star}\in\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> and all <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, then no factorization with strictly positive <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is possible, because</p>
<table id="A6.Ex115" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex115.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(o^{\star})^{\beta_{i}}&gt;0\quad\Longrightarrow\quad P(o^{\star})&gt;0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(o^{\star})^{\beta_{i}}&gt;0\quad\Longrightarrow\quad P(o^{\star})&gt;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.2" class="ltx_p">a contradiction. A necessary condition is therefore</p>
<table id="A6.Ex116" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex116.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{supp}(P)=\bigcap_{\beta_{i}&gt;0}\mathrm{supp}(P_{i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{supp}(P)=\bigcap_{\beta_{i}&gt;0}\mathrm{supp}(P_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.3" class="ltx_p">Under this support-matching condition, one obtains an existence result analogous to Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem39" title="Theorem 39 (Log–pool factorization with pairwise-distinct components). ‣ Recursion on Agents and Subagent Decomposition. ‣ Appendix F Recursing on Compositional Agents for Scale-Free Theory ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">39</span></a> by working on the reduced outcome space <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{supp}(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{supp}(P)</annotation></semantics></math>. That is, we may choose pairwise distinct <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> supported on <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{supp}(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{supp}(P)</annotation></semantics></math>, define <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> as in the proof (which will also be supported on <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{supp}(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{supp}(P)</annotation></semantics></math>), and set <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}=Q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}=Q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. Points outside <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{supp}(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{supp}(P)</annotation></semantics></math> must receive zero from at least one <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> so that the intersection of supports equals <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{supp}(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{supp}(P)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p12.1" class="ltx_p">This construction holds for any non-trivial decomposition. For instance, suppose that we simply wish to decompose an agent into two distinct subagents. Given <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> strictly positive and any <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1},\beta_{2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1},\beta_{2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}+\beta_{2}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}+\beta_{2}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, pick any <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{2}\neq P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{2}\neq P</annotation></semantics></math> with full support and define</p>
<table id="A6.Ex117" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex117.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}(o)\;=\;\frac{P(o)^{1/\beta_{1}}\,Q_{2}(o)^{-\beta_{2}/\beta_{1}}}{\displaystyle\sum_{u}P(u)^{1/\beta_{1}}\,Q_{2}(u)^{-\beta_{2}/\beta_{1}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mi>Q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mi>Q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}(o)\;=\;\frac{P(o)^{1/\beta_{1}}\,Q_{2}(o)^{-\beta_{2}/\beta_{1}}}{\displaystyle\sum_{u}P(u)^{1/\beta_{1}}\,Q_{2}(u)^{-\beta_{2}/\beta_{1}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p12.2" class="ltx_p">Then <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P=\frac{1}{Z}P_{1}^{\beta_{1}}Q_{2}^{\beta_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>Z</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P=\frac{1}{Z}P_{1}^{\beta_{1}}Q_{2}^{\beta_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and one can choose <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> so that <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}\neq Q_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}\neq Q_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}\neq P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}\neq P</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n&gt;2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n&gt;2</annotation></semantics></math>, pick any pairwise-distinct <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p12.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{2},\dots,Q_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{2},\dots,Q_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> (on the appropriate support) and absorb their combined effect via <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p12.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> as in Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem39" title="Theorem 39 (Log–pool factorization with pairwise-distinct components). ‣ Recursion on Agents and Subagent Decomposition. ‣ Appendix F Recursing on Compositional Agents for Scale-Free Theory ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">39</span></a>; this yields a pairwise-distinct factorization for the original <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta_{i})_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta_{i})_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p13.1" class="ltx_p">Except for the trivial obstacle of mismatched supports, <em id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">every</em> strictly positive discrete distribution admits a log–opinion-pool factorization with any prescribed nonnegative weights summing to one. Moreover, one can ensure that all components are pairwise distinct and each differs from <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>. When <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> has zeros, existence is equivalent to the intersection-of-supports condition <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{supp}(P)=\bigcap_{\beta_{i}&gt;0}\mathrm{supp}(P_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⋂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{supp}(P)=\bigcap_{\beta_{i}&gt;0}\mathrm{supp}(P_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>; under this condition a factorization again exists (with zeros placed accordingly).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>Defining Subagents a Priori</h3>

<div id="A6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, we examine whether our framework supports another form of <em id="A6.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">recursive modeling</em>. An agent may naturally be viewed as the aggregation of multiple underlying subagents, each corresponding to a particular desire or objective–for example, the pursuit of nourishment, rest, social connection, or intellectual achievement. Once a set of <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> such subagents has been specified, we ask: is it still possible to further decompose the agent into <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> subagents, where the original <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> appear as fixed components within the new decomposition? A <em id="A6.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">scale-free</em> framework should allow such recursion, preserving the specified subagents while introducing additional ones.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem41" title="Theorem 41 (Log–pool with some components fixed). ‣ F.1 Defining Subagents a Priori ‣ Appendix F Recursing on Compositional Agents for Scale-Free Theory ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a> confirms that this property holds. For any fixed <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, there exist nonnegative weights <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and additional subagents <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{m+1},\dots,P_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{m+1},\dots,P_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the log-pool of all <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> subagents recovers the original agent <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(o)</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, this construction can be made nontrivial: the weights <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,\dots,m\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,\dots,m\}</annotation></semantics></math> may be taken to be strictly positive, ensuring that the predetermined subagents meaningfully contribute to the aggregate agent.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem41" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem41.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 41</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem41.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Log–pool with some components fixed)<span id="Thmtheorem41.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem41.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem41.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem41.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem41.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> be finite. Let <math id="Thmtheorem41.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> be a distribution on <math id="Thmtheorem41.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="Thmtheorem41.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1},\dots,P_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1},\dots,P_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> be <em id="Thmtheorem41.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">given</em> distributions on <math id="Thmtheorem41.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math>. Fix any integer <math id="Thmtheorem41.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq m+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq m+2</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<ol id="A6.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A6.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(A)</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Strictly positive case.</span><span id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> If </span><math id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(o)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(o)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for all </span><math id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\in\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\in\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and each </span><math id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> (</span><math id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq m</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) is strictly positive, then for any set of weights </span><math id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1},\dots,\beta_{n}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1},\dots,\beta_{n}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> with </span><math id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{m+1}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{m+1}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, and </span><math id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for at least one </span><math id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,\dots,m\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,\dots,m\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, we have that there exist distributions </span><math id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{m+1},\dots,P_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{m+1},\dots,P_{n}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> on </span><math id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex118" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex118.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(o)\;=\;\frac{1}{Z}\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}}\qquad(o\in\mathcal{O})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>Z</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(o)\;=\;\frac{1}{Z}\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}}\qquad(o\in\mathcal{O}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with </span><math id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=\sum_{u\in\mathcal{O}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(u)^{\beta_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=\sum_{u\in\mathcal{O}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(u)^{\beta_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.
Moreover, the construction can be arranged so that </span><math id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\neq P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\neq P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for all </span><math id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, and the </span><math id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> are pairwise distinct.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(B)</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Non-negative case.</span><span id="A6.I1.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
Suppose we require </span><math id="A6.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.ix2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for all </span><math id="A6.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq m</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.ix2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Then such a factorization exists if and only if</span></p>
<table id="A6.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{supp}(P)\;\subseteq\;\bigcap_{i=1}^{m}\operatorname{supp}(P_{i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">⊆</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⋂</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{supp}(P)\;\subseteq\;\bigcap_{i=1}^{m}\operatorname{supp}(P_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.I1.ix2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I1.ix2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">When (</span><a href="#A6.E7" title="In item (B) ‣ Theorem 41 (Log–pool with some components fixed). ‣ F.1 Defining Subagents a Priori ‣ Appendix F Recursing on Compositional Agents for Scale-Free Theory ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a><span id="A6.I1.ix2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) holds, one can choose </span><math id="A6.I1.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{m+1},\dots,P_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{m+1},\dots,P_{n}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.ix2.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> supported exactly on </span><math id="A6.I1.ix2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{supp}(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{supp}(P)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.ix2.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> to ensure</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex119" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex119.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\operatorname{supp}(P)\;=\;\bigcap_{i:\,\beta_{i}&gt;0}\operatorname{supp}(P_{i})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋂</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.448em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><mi>supp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{supp}(P)\;=\;\bigcap_{i:\,\beta_{i}&gt;0}\operatorname{supp}(P_{i}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.I1.ix2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I1.ix2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and then build the factorization as in part </span><span id="A6.I1.ix2.p1.3.2" class="ltx_text">(A)</span><span id="A6.I1.ix2.p1.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. If (</span><a href="#A6.E7" title="In item (B) ‣ Theorem 41 (Log–pool with some components fixed). ‣ F.1 Defining Subagents a Priori ‣ Appendix F Recursing on Compositional Agents for Scale-Free Theory ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a><span id="A6.I1.ix2.p1.3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) fails, no such factorization is possible with all </span><math id="A6.I1.ix2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1},\dots,\beta_{m}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1},\dots,\beta_{m}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.ix2.p1.3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(A) Strictly positive case.</span><span id="A6.SS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text">
Pick any weights <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1},\dots,\beta_{n}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1},\dots,\beta_{n}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{m+1}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{m+1}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and at least one of <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1},\dots,\beta_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1},\dots,\beta_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is positive (to keep the fixed components nontrivial).
Choose <em id="A6.SS1.p3.1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">arbitrary</em> strictly positive, pairwise distinct distributions <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{m+2},\dots,Q_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{m+2},\dots,Q_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math>, all different from <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., small exponential tilts of a positive reference distribution with distinct tilt directions as in the proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem39" title="Theorem 39 (Log–pool factorization with pairwise-distinct components). ‣ Recursion on Agents and Subagent Decomposition. ‣ Appendix F Recursing on Compositional Agents for Scale-Free Theory ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">39</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S:=\{1,\dots,n\}\setminus\{m+1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S:=\{1,\dots,n\}\setminus\{m+1\}</annotation></semantics></math> and define the weighted log–mean</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex120" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex120.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\star}(o)\;:=\;\exp\Bigl(\frac{1}{\sum_{i\in S}\beta_{i}}\sum_{i\in S}\beta_{i}\,\log\widehat{P}_{i}(o)\Bigr),\qquad\widehat{P}_{i}:=\begin{cases}P_{i},&amp;i\leq m,\\
Q_{i},&amp;i\geq m+2.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\star}(o)\;:=\;\exp\Bigl(\frac{1}{\sum_{i\in S}\beta_{i}}\sum_{i\in S}\beta_{i}\,\log\widehat{P}_{i}(o)\Bigr),\qquad\widehat{P}_{i}:=\begin{cases}P_{i},&amp;i\leq m,\\
Q_{i},&amp;i\geq m+2.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Note that <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i\in S}\beta_{i}=1-\beta_{m+1}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i\in S}\beta_{i}=1-\beta_{m+1}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> is well defined and strictly positive. Now set</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex121" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex121.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{m+1}(o)\;=\;\frac{P(o)^{1/\beta_{m+1}}\;Q_{\star}(o)^{-\frac{1}{\beta_{m+1}}\sum_{i\in S}\beta_{i}}}{\displaystyle\sum_{u\in\mathcal{O}}P(u)^{1/\beta_{m+1}}\;Q_{\star}(u)^{-\frac{1}{\beta_{m+1}}\sum_{i\in S}\beta_{i}}}\;=\;\frac{P(o)^{1/\beta_{m+1}}\;Q_{\star}(o)^{-\frac{1-\beta_{m+1}}{\beta_{m+1}}}}{Z_{1}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mi>Q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></msub><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mi>Q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{m+1}(o)\;=\;\frac{P(o)^{1/\beta_{m+1}}\;Q_{\star}(o)^{-\frac{1}{\beta_{m+1}}\sum_{i\in S}\beta_{i}}}{\displaystyle\sum_{u\in\mathcal{O}}P(u)^{1/\beta_{m+1}}\;Q_{\star}(u)^{-\frac{1}{\beta_{m+1}}\sum_{i\in S}\beta_{i}}}\;=\;\frac{P(o)^{1/\beta_{m+1}}\;Q_{\star}(o)^{-\frac{1-\beta_{m+1}}{\beta_{m+1}}}}{Z_{1}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is the (strictly positive) normalizing constant in the denominator. For any <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\in\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\in\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex122"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex122.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta_{m+1}\log P_{m+1}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta_{m+1}\log P_{m+1}(o)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex122.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta_{m+1}\Bigl[\tfrac{1}{\beta_{m+1}}\log P(o)\;-\;\tfrac{1-\beta_{m+1}}{\beta_{m+1}}\log Q_{\star}(o)\;-\;\log Z_{1}\Bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta_{m+1}\Bigl[\tfrac{1}{\beta_{m+1}}\log P(o)\;-\;\tfrac{1-\beta_{m+1}}{\beta_{m+1}}\log Q_{\star}(o)\;-\;\log Z_{1}\Bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex123"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex123.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log P(o)\;-\;(1-\beta_{m+1})\log Q_{\star}(o)\;-\;\beta_{m+1}\log Z_{1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log P(o)\;-\;(1-\beta_{m+1})\log Q_{\star}(o)\;-\;\beta_{m+1}\log Z_{1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex124"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex124.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\log P_{i}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\log P_{i}(o)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex124.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta_{m+1}\log P_{m+1}(o)\;+\;\sum_{i\in S}\beta_{i}\log\widehat{P}_{i}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta_{m+1}\log P_{m+1}(o)\;+\;\sum_{i\in S}\beta_{i}\log\widehat{P}_{i}(o)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex125"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex125.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Bigl[\log P(o)\;-\;(1-\beta_{m+1})\log Q_{\star}(o)\;-\;\beta_{m+1}\log Z_{1}\Bigr]\;+\;\sum_{i\in S}\beta_{i}\log\widehat{P}_{i}(o)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Bigl[\log P(o)\;-\;(1-\beta_{m+1})\log Q_{\star}(o)\;-\;\beta_{m+1}\log Z_{1}\Bigr]\;+\;\sum_{i\in S}\beta_{i}\log\widehat{P}_{i}(o).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">By the definition of <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex126" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex126.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\beta_{m+1})\log Q_{\star}(o)=\sum_{i\in S}\beta_{i}\log\widehat{P}_{i}(o)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\beta_{m+1})\log Q_{\star}(o)=\sum_{i\in S}\beta_{i}\log\widehat{P}_{i}(o),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">so these terms cancel. Hence</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex127" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex127.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\log P_{i}(o)\;=\;\log P(o)\;-\;\beta_{m+1}\log Z_{1}\;=\;\log P(o)\;+\;C," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\log P_{i}(o)\;=\;\log P(o)\;-\;\beta_{m+1}\log Z_{1}\;=\;\log P(o)\;+\;C,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p4.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p4.7.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C:=-\beta_{m+1}\log Z_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C:=-\beta_{m+1}\log Z_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math>. Exponentiating gives</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex128" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex128.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}}\;=\;e^{C}\,P(o)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}}\;=\;e^{C}\,P(o),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p4.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p4.8.1" class="ltx_text">and summing over <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math> yields <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=\sum_{o}\prod_{i}P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}}=e^{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>C</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=\sum_{o}\prod_{i}P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}}=e^{C}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex129" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex129.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(o)\;=\;\frac{1}{Z}\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}}\qquad(o\in\mathcal{O})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>Z</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(o)\;=\;\frac{1}{Z}\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}}\qquad(o\in\mathcal{O}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p4.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p4.9.1" class="ltx_text">as claimed.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(B) Zeros and supports.</span><span id="A6.SS1.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text">
Assume <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq m</annotation></semantics></math>. If there exists <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\in\operatorname{supp}(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\in\operatorname{supp}(P)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}(o)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}(o)=0</annotation></semantics></math> for some fixed <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex130" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex130.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{k=1}^{n}P_{k}(o)^{\beta_{k}}=0\quad\Longrightarrow\quad P(o)=0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{k=1}^{n}P_{k}(o)^{\beta_{k}}=0\quad\Longrightarrow\quad P(o)=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">a contradiction. Thus (<a href="#A6.E7" title="In item (B) ‣ Theorem 41 (Log–pool with some components fixed). ‣ F.1 Defining Subagents a Priori ‣ Appendix F Recursing on Compositional Agents for Scale-Free Theory ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) is necessary.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Conversely, if (<a href="#A6.E7" title="In item (B) ‣ Theorem 41 (Log–pool with some components fixed). ‣ F.1 Defining Subagents a Priori ‣ Appendix F Recursing on Compositional Agents for Scale-Free Theory ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) holds, choose any strictly positive reference distribution <math id="A6.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A6.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{supp}(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{supp}(P)</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., uniform on <math id="A6.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{supp}(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{supp}(P)</annotation></semantics></math>), and define <math id="A6.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{m+2},\dots,Q_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{m+2},\dots,Q_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> to be pairwise distinct distributions supported <em id="A6.SS1.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">exactly</em> on <math id="A6.SS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{supp}(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{supp}(P)</annotation></semantics></math>. The above construction, performed on the reduced space <math id="A6.SS1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{supp}(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{supp}(P)</annotation></semantics></math>, produces <math id="A6.SS1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{m+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{m+1}</annotation></semantics></math> supported exactly on <math id="A6.SS1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{supp}(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{supp}(P)</annotation></semantics></math> and yields the desired identity. Because every component with <math id="A6.SS1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is supported on <math id="A6.SS1.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{supp}(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{supp}(P)</annotation></semantics></math> and at least one component (<math id="A6.SS1.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{m+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{m+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, say) assigns zero outside this set, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex131" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex131.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\operatorname{supp}(P)=\bigcap_{i:\,\beta_{i}&gt;0}\operatorname{supp}(P_{i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋂</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.448em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><mi>supp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{supp}(P)=\bigcap_{i:\,\beta_{i}&gt;0}\operatorname{supp}(P_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore (<a href="#A6.E7" title="In item (B) ‣ Theorem 41 (Log–pool with some components fixed). ‣ F.1 Defining Subagents a Priori ‣ Appendix F Recursing on Compositional Agents for Scale-Free Theory ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) is also <em id="A6.SS1.p6.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">sufficient</em> under the requirement <math id="A6.SS1.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1},\dots,\beta_{m}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1},\dots,\beta_{m}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem42" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem42.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 42</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem42.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Using only a subset of the fixed components)<span id="Thmtheorem42.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem42.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem42.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem42.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If it is <em id="Thmtheorem42.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">not</em> required that every fixed <math id="Thmtheorem42.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> carries positive weight, a factorization exists as soon as there is a nonempty subset <math id="Thmtheorem42.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J\subseteq\{1,\dots,m\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\subseteq\{1,\dots,m\}</annotation></semantics></math> for which</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex132" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex132.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{supp}(P)\;\subseteq\;\bigcap_{i\in J}\operatorname{supp}(P_{i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">⊆</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋂</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{supp}(P)\;\subseteq\;\bigcap_{i\in J}\operatorname{supp}(P_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem42.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem42.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Set <math id="Thmtheorem42.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmtheorem42.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\notin J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\notin J</annotation></semantics></math>, pick positive weights on <math id="Thmtheorem42.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> (summing to <math id="Thmtheorem42.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>), and apply Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem41" title="Theorem 41 (Log–pool with some components fixed). ‣ F.1 Defining Subagents a Priori ‣ Appendix F Recursing on Compositional Agents for Scale-Free Theory ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a> (A)/(B) on the reduced family.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem43" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem43.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 43</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem43.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Nontriviality guarantees in practice)<span id="Thmtheorem43.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem43.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem43.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem43.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">To avoid trivial solutions (such as <math id="Thmtheorem43.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i)</annotation></semantics></math> some <math id="Thmtheorem43.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem43.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(ii)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(ii)</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="Thmtheorem43.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P=P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P=P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, or <math id="Thmtheorem43.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(iii)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(iii)</annotation></semantics></math> duplicate components), choose all positive <math id="Thmtheorem43.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, or ensure at least two fixed indices have <math id="Thmtheorem43.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and, when <math id="Thmtheorem43.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq m+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq m+2</annotation></semantics></math>, pick <math id="Thmtheorem43.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{m+2},\dots,P_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{m+2},\dots,P_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> as distinct small exponential tilts of a reference distribution. Genericity of the construction then implies <math id="Thmtheorem43.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\neq P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\neq P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem43.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}\neq P_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}\neq P_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmtheorem43.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Recursive Splitting of Agents under Logarithmic Pooling</h2>

<section id="A7.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.1 </span>Distributional Invariance under Splitting</h3>

<div id="A7.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first establish a basic <em id="A7.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">recursion consistency</em> property: the pooled distribution should remain unchanged when an agent is replaced by a collection of subagents whose aggregate reproduces the original agent’s belief distribution. Formally, if agent <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is decomposed into <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> subagents with nonnegative weights <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i,1},\dots,\beta_{i,m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i,1},\dots,\beta_{i,m}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j=1}^{m}\beta_{i,j}=\beta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j=1}^{m}\beta_{i,j}=\beta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, then the subagents must themselves be log-pooled using normalized weights</p>
<table id="A7.Ex133" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex133.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{j}:=\frac{\beta_{i,j}}{\beta_{i}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{j}:=\frac{\beta_{i,j}}{\beta_{i}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">so that their aggregation yields <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. The overall pooling is still performed over agents with weights summing to one. This property is formalized in Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem44" title="Lemma 44 (Pooling invariance under compatible splitting). ‣ G.1 Distributional Invariance under Splitting ‣ Appendix G Recursive Splitting of Agents under Logarithmic Pooling ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">44</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem44" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem44.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 44</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem44.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Pooling invariance under compatible splitting)<span id="Thmtheorem44.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem44.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem44.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem44.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem44.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1},\dots,P_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1},\dots,P_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be agents with nonnegative pooling weights <math id="Thmtheorem44.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1},\dots,\beta_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1},\dots,\beta_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="Thmtheorem44.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Suppose <math id="Thmtheorem44.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is replaced by <math id="Thmtheorem44.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> subagents <math id="Thmtheorem44.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1,1},\dots,P_{1,m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1,1},\dots,P_{1,m}</annotation></semantics></math> with nonnegative weights <math id="Thmtheorem44.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1,1},\dots,\beta_{1,m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1,1},\dots,\beta_{1,m}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex134" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex134.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j=1}^{m}\beta_{1,j}=\beta_{1}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j=1}^{m}\beta_{1,j}=\beta_{1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem44.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem44.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and whose aggregation satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A7.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}\;\propto\;\prod_{j=1}^{m}P_{1,j}^{\alpha_{j}},\qquad\text{where}\qquad\alpha_{j}:=\frac{\beta_{1,j}}{\beta_{1}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.391em">∝</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">where</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}\;\propto\;\prod_{j=1}^{m}P_{1,j}^{\alpha_{j}},\qquad\text{where}\qquad\alpha_{j}:=\frac{\beta_{1,j}}{\beta_{1}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem44.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem44.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem44.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> denote the log pool of the original <math id="Thmtheorem44.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> agents, and <math id="Thmtheorem44.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> the log pool after replacing <math id="Thmtheorem44.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> by its <math id="Thmtheorem44.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> subagents. Then <math id="Thmtheorem44.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}=P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}=P</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">By definition,</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex135" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex135.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}\;\propto\;\Big(\prod_{j=1}^{m}P_{1,j}^{\beta_{1,j}}\Big)\;\prod_{i=2}^{n}P_{i}^{\beta_{i}}\;\propto\;\Big(\prod_{j=1}^{m}P_{1,j}^{\alpha_{j}}\Big)^{\beta_{1}}\;\prod_{i=2}^{n}P_{i}^{\beta_{i}}\;\propto\;P_{1}^{\beta_{1}}\,\prod_{i=2}^{n}P_{i}^{\beta_{i}}\;\propto\;P." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.447em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">∝</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">∝</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">∝</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}\;\propto\;\Big(\prod_{j=1}^{m}P_{1,j}^{\beta_{1,j}}\Big)\;\prod_{i=2}^{n}P_{i}^{\beta_{i}}\;\propto\;\Big(\prod_{j=1}^{m}P_{1,j}^{\alpha_{j}}\Big)^{\beta_{1}}\;\prod_{i=2}^{n}P_{i}^{\beta_{i}}\;\propto\;P_{1}^{\beta_{1}}\,\prod_{i=2}^{n}P_{i}^{\beta_{i}}\;\propto\;P.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.2 </span>Does a Compositional Parent Agent Yield Compositional Subagents?</h3>

<div id="A7.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We begin by proving a useful lemma.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem45" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem45.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 45</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem45.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Binary coarse–graining lower bound)<span id="Thmtheorem45.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem45.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem45.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem45.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem45.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P,Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P,Q</annotation></semantics></math> be distributions on a finite alphabet <math id="Thmtheorem45.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="Thmtheorem45.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\subseteq\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\subseteq\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> be any event. Then</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex136" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex136.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\KL(P\|Q)\;\geq\;P(A)\log\frac{P(A)}{Q(A)}\;+\;P(A^{c})\log\frac{P(A^{c})}{Q(A^{c})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(P\|Q)\;\geq\;P(A)\log\frac{P(A)}{Q(A)}\;+\;P(A^{c})\log\frac{P(A^{c})}{Q(A^{c})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Write <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{o}:=P(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{o}:=P(o)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{o}:=Q(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{o}:=Q(o)</annotation></semantics></math>, and adopt the standard conventions
<math id="A7.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\log\frac{0}{y}:=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>0</mn><mi>y</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\log\frac{0}{y}:=0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\log\frac{x}{0}:=+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\log\frac{x}{0}:=+\infty</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{a_{i}\}_{i\in I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{a_{i}\}_{i\in I}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{b_{i}\}_{i\in I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{b_{i}\}_{i\in I}</annotation></semantics></math> be nonnegative sequences with <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}b_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}b_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
We claim the <em id="A7.SS2.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">log–sum inequality</em>:</span></p>
<table id="A7.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i\in I}a_{i}\log\frac{a_{i}}{b_{i}}\;\geq\;\Big(\sum_{i\in I}a_{i}\Big)\,\log\frac{\sum_{i\in I}a_{i}}{\sum_{i\in I}b_{i}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i\in I}a_{i}\log\frac{a_{i}}{b_{i}}\;\geq\;\Big(\sum_{i\in I}a_{i}\Big)\,\log\frac{\sum_{i\in I}a_{i}}{\sum_{i\in I}b_{i}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">with equality iff <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}/b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}/b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is constant over all indices with <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. If there is an index <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{j}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{j}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{j}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{j}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, then the left-hand side is <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+\infty</annotation></semantics></math> (by convention) and (<a href="#A7.E9" title="In Proof. ‣ G.2 Does a Compositional Parent Agent Yield Compositional Subagents? ‣ Appendix G Recursive Splitting of Agents under Logarithmic Pooling ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) is trivially true. If <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{j}=a_{j}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{j}=a_{j}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-th term is <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> and we may remove <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence it suffices to assume <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in I</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A7.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B:=\sum_{i}b_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B:=\sum_{i}b_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, define weights <math id="A7.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}:=b_{i}/B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}:=b_{i}/B</annotation></semantics></math> (so <math id="A7.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}\lambda_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}\lambda_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math>), and set</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex137" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex137.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}:=\frac{a_{i}}{b_{i}}\in[0,\infty)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}:=\frac{a_{i}}{b_{i}}\in[0,\infty).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Consider <math id="A7.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:(0,\infty)\to\R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:(0,\infty)\to\R</annotation></semantics></math> given by <math id="A7.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)=x\log x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)=x\log x</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then <math id="A7.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}(x)=\log x+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}(x)=\log x+1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime\prime}(x)=1/x&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime\prime}(x)=1/x&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A7.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is convex on <math id="A7.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Jensen’s inequality,</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex138" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex138.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}\lambda_{i}f(x_{i})\ \geq\ f\Big(\sum_{i}\lambda_{i}x_{i}\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}\lambda_{i}f(x_{i})\ \geq\ f\Big(\sum_{i}\lambda_{i}x_{i}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Multiply both sides by <math id="A7.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> (noting <math id="A7.SS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\lambda_{i}=b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\lambda_{i}=b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>) to get</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex139" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex139.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}b_{i}\,f\Big(\frac{a_{i}}{b_{i}}\Big)\ \geq\ B\,f\Big(\frac{\sum_{i}b_{i}(a_{i}/b_{i})}{B}\Big)\ =\ B\,f\Big(\frac{\sum_{i}a_{i}}{B}\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}b_{i}\,f\Big(\frac{a_{i}}{b_{i}}\Big)\ \geq\ B\,f\Big(\frac{\sum_{i}b_{i}(a_{i}/b_{i})}{B}\Big)\ =\ B\,f\Big(\frac{\sum_{i}a_{i}}{B}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A7.SS2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}f(a_{i}/b_{i})=a_{i}\log(a_{i}/b_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}f(a_{i}/b_{i})=a_{i}\log(a_{i}/b_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS2.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\,f((\sum a_{i})/B)=(\sum a_{i})\log((\sum a_{i})/B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\,f((\sum a_{i})/B)=(\sum a_{i})\log((\sum a_{i})/B)</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain (<a href="#A7.E9" title="In Proof. ‣ G.2 Does a Compositional Parent Agent Yield Compositional Subagents? ‣ Appendix G Recursive Splitting of Agents under Logarithmic Pooling ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>).
Equality in Jensen holds iff <math id="A7.SS2.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is constant on the support of <math id="A7.SS2.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\lambda_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\lambda_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., if and only if <math id="A7.SS2.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}/b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}/b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is constant for all <math id="A7.SS2.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A7.SS2.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, apply (<a href="#A7.E9" title="In Proof. ‣ G.2 Does a Compositional Parent Agent Yield Compositional Subagents? ‣ Appendix G Recursive Splitting of Agents under Logarithmic Pooling ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) to the block <math id="A7.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A7.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{o}=p_{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{o}=p_{o}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A7.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{o}=q_{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{o}=q_{o}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A7.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\in A</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex140" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex140.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{o\in A}p_{o}\log\frac{p_{o}}{q_{o}}\;\geq\;\Big(\sum_{o\in A}p_{o}\Big)\,\log\frac{\sum_{o\in A}p_{o}}{\sum_{o\in A}q_{o}}\;=\;P(A)\log\frac{P(A)}{Q(A)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{o\in A}p_{o}\log\frac{p_{o}}{q_{o}}\;\geq\;\Big(\sum_{o\in A}p_{o}\Big)\,\log\frac{\sum_{o\in A}p_{o}}{\sum_{o\in A}q_{o}}\;=\;P(A)\log\frac{P(A)}{Q(A)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Apply it again to the complementary block <math id="A7.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{c}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex141" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex141.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{o\notin A}p_{o}\log\frac{p_{o}}{q_{o}}\;\geq\;P(A^{c})\log\frac{P(A^{c})}{Q(A^{c})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{o\notin A}p_{o}\log\frac{p_{o}}{q_{o}}\;\geq\;P(A^{c})\log\frac{P(A^{c})}{Q(A^{c})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Adding the two inequalities and recalling that
<math id="A7.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\KL(P\|Q)=\sum_{o\in\mathcal{O}}p_{o}\log\frac{p_{o}}{q_{o}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mfrac><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(P\|Q)=\sum_{o\in\mathcal{O}}p_{o}\log\frac{p_{o}}{q_{o}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex142" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex142.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\KL(P\|Q)\;\geq\;P(A)\log\frac{P(A)}{Q(A)}\;+\;P(A^{c})\log\frac{P(A^{c})}{Q(A^{c})}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(P\|Q)\;\geq\;P(A)\log\frac{P(A)}{Q(A)}\;+\;P(A^{c})\log\frac{P(A^{c})}{Q(A^{c})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">which is the desired binary coarse–graining lower bound.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">If the parent is a compositional agent, does this property pass onto the child subagent decompositions? The next result answers this in the negative, even if the parent strictly benefits.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem46" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem46.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 46</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem46.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Parental benefit need not pass to subagents)<span id="Thmtheorem46.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem46.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem46.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem46.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exist agents <math id="Thmtheorem46.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1},\dots,P_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1},\dots,P_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, weights <math id="Thmtheorem46.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, and a compatible split of <math id="Thmtheorem46.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="Thmtheorem46.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1,1},P_{1,2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1,1},P_{1,2}</annotation></semantics></math> as in (<a href="#A7.E8" title="In Lemma 44 (Pooling invariance under compatible splitting). ‣ G.1 Distributional Invariance under Splitting ‣ Appendix G Recursive Splitting of Agents under Logarithmic Pooling ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) such that the composition <math id="Thmtheorem46.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> (before/after splitting) satisfies <math id="Thmtheorem46.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{P_{1}}(P)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{P_{1}}(P)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> but <math id="Thmtheorem46.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{P_{1,1}}(P)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{P_{1,1}}(P)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. By symmetry, one can also have <math id="Thmtheorem46.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{P_{1,2}}(P)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{P_{1,2}}(P)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A7.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> be any non-uniform strictly positive distribution on <math id="A7.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A7.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, define the <math id="A7.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-tilt of <math id="A7.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex143" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex143.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}(o)\;:=\;\frac{P_{1}(o)^{t}}{Z(t)},\qquad Z(t):=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{O}}P_{1}(x)^{t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}(o)\;:=\;\frac{P_{1}(o)^{t}}{Z(t)},\qquad Z(t):=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{O}}P_{1}(x)^{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then <math id="A7.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the log-pool of <math id="A7.SS2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{P_{1},P_{2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{P_{1},P_{2}\}</annotation></semantics></math> with weights <math id="A7.SS2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}=\beta_{2}=\tfrac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}=\beta_{2}=\tfrac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS2.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{2}\propto P_{1}^{\,2t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∝</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{2}\propto P_{1}^{\,2t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, since
<math id="A7.SS2.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\propto P_{1}^{1/2}\,P_{2}^{1/2}\propto P_{1}^{(1+(2t-1))/2}=P_{1}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∝</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>∝</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\propto P_{1}^{1/2}\,P_{2}^{1/2}\propto P_{1}^{(1+(2t-1))/2}=P_{1}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>,
which normalizes to <math id="A7.SS2.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, we show that the child agent <math id="A7.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> strictly benefits against the parent agent <math id="A7.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A7.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. By definition, we have</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex144" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex144.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{P_{1}}(P_{t})\;=\;\E_{P_{t}}[\log P_{1}]-\E_{P_{1}}[\log P_{1}]\;=\;\E_{P_{t}}[\log P_{1}]+H(P_{1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{P_{1}}(P_{t})\;=\;\E_{P_{t}}[\log P_{1}]-\E_{P_{1}}[\log P_{1}]\;=\;\E_{P_{t}}[\log P_{1}]+H(P_{1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">We claim <math id="A7.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E_{P_{t}}[\log P_{1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E_{P_{t}}[\log P_{1}]</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly increasing in <math id="A7.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> whenever <math id="A7.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is non-uniform, and therefore
<math id="A7.SS2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E_{P_{t}}[\log P_{1}]&gt;\E_{P_{1}}[\log P_{1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E_{P_{t}}[\log P_{1}]&gt;\E_{P_{1}}[\log P_{1}]</annotation></semantics></math>
for every <math id="A7.SS2.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. To see this, write <math id="A7.SS2.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(o):=P_{1}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(o):=P_{1}(o)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS2.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(o):=\log p(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(o):=\log p(o)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we have</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex145" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex145.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E_{P_{t}}[f]\;=\;\sum_{o}\frac{p(o)^{t}}{Z(t)}\,f(o)\;=\;\frac{Z^{\prime}(t)}{Z(t)}\;=\;\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\log Z(t)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></munder><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>dt</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E_{P_{t}}[f]\;=\;\sum_{o}\frac{p(o)^{t}}{Z(t)}\,f(o)\;=\;\frac{Z^{\prime}(t)}{Z(t)}\;=\;\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\log Z(t),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">because <math id="A7.SS2.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{\prime}(t)=\sum_{o}p(o)^{t}\log p(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>o</mi></msub><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{\prime}(t)=\sum_{o}p(o)^{t}\log p(o)</annotation></semantics></math>. Differentiating once more,</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex146"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex146.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\mathrm{d}^{2}}{\mathrm{d}t^{2}}\log Z(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\mathrm{d}^{2}}{\mathrm{d}t^{2}}\log Z(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex146.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{Z^{\prime\prime}(t)}{Z(t)}-\Big(\frac{Z^{\prime}(t)}{Z(t)}\Big)^{2}=\sum_{o}\frac{p(o)^{t}}{Z(t)}\big(\log p(o)\big)^{2}\;-\;\Big(\sum_{o}\frac{p(o)^{t}}{Z(t)}\log p(o)\Big)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{Z^{\prime\prime}(t)}{Z(t)}-\Big(\frac{Z^{\prime}(t)}{Z(t)}\Big)^{2}=\sum_{o}\frac{p(o)^{t}}{Z(t)}\big(\log p(o)\big)^{2}\;-\;\Big(\sum_{o}\frac{p(o)^{t}}{Z(t)}\log p(o)\Big)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex147"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex147.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Var_{P_{t}}\!\big(\log P_{1}\big)\;\geq 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Var_{P_{t}}\!\big(\log P_{1}\big)\;\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">Thus <math id="A7.SS2.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\mapsto\E_{P_{t}}[\log P_{1}]=\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\log Z(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>dt</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\mapsto\E_{P_{t}}[\log P_{1}]=\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\log Z(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="A7.SS2.p7.4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">increasing</em> in <math id="A7.SS2.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, and it is <em id="A7.SS2.p7.4.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">strictly</em> increasing whenever <math id="A7.SS2.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Var_{P_{t}}(\log P_{1})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Var_{P_{t}}(\log P_{1})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., whenever <math id="A7.SS2.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log P_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log P_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is not almost surely constant under <math id="A7.SS2.p7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. The latter holds exactly when <math id="A7.SS2.p7.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is non-uniform. Evaluating at <math id="A7.SS2.p7.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math> gives <math id="A7.SS2.p7.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E_{P_{1}}[\log P_{1}]=\sum_{o}P_{1}(o)\log P_{1}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>o</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E_{P_{1}}[\log P_{1}]=\sum_{o}P_{1}(o)\log P_{1}(o)</annotation></semantics></math>, so for any <math id="A7.SS2.p7.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex148" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex148.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E_{P_{t}}[\log P_{1}]\;&gt;\;\E_{P_{1}}[\log P_{1}]\quad\Longrightarrow\quad\Delta_{P_{1}}(P_{t})\;&gt;\;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E_{P_{t}}[\log P_{1}]\;&gt;\;\E_{P_{1}}[\log P_{1}]\quad\Longrightarrow\quad\Delta_{P_{1}}(P_{t})\;&gt;\;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, we derive a compatible split of the child agent <math id="A7.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> that makes its subagent strictly lose epistemic utility. Fix <math id="A7.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and any function <math id="A7.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:\mathcal{O}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:\mathcal{O}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define subagents by exponential tilting:</span></p>
<table id="A7.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log P_{1,1}\;=\;\log P_{1}+(1-\alpha)g-c_{1},\qquad\log P_{1,2}\;=\;\log P_{1}-\alpha g-c_{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log P_{1,1}\;=\;\log P_{1}+(1-\alpha)g-c_{1},\qquad\log P_{1,2}\;=\;\log P_{1}-\alpha g-c_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A7.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1},c_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1},c_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> make each distribution sum to <math id="A7.SS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>. Then
<math id="A7.SS2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\log P_{1,1}+(1-\alpha)\log P_{1,2}=\log P_{1}-\big(\alpha c_{1}+(1-\alpha)c_{2}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\log P_{1,1}+(1-\alpha)\log P_{1,2}=\log P_{1}-\big(\alpha c_{1}+(1-\alpha)c_{2}\big)</annotation></semantics></math>,
hence (<a href="#A7.E8" title="In Lemma 44 (Pooling invariance under compatible splitting). ‣ G.1 Distributional Invariance under Splitting ‣ Appendix G Recursive Splitting of Agents under Logarithmic Pooling ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) holds with <math id="A7.SS2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1,1}=\alpha\beta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1,1}=\alpha\beta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS2.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1,2}=(1-\alpha)\beta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1,2}=(1-\alpha)\beta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. By Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem44" title="Lemma 44 (Pooling invariance under compatible splitting). ‣ G.1 Distributional Invariance under Splitting ‣ Appendix G Recursive Splitting of Agents under Logarithmic Pooling ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">44</span></a>, the composition <em id="A7.SS2.p8.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">after</em> splitting remains <math id="A7.SS2.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Choose <math id="A7.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> to depress a single outcome: pick any <math id="A7.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o^{\star}\in\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{\star}\in\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> and set
<math id="A7.SS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="g_{\lambda}(o):=-\lambda\,\mathbf{1}_{\{o=o^{\star}\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">:=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>λ</mi><msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>o</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\lambda}(o):=-\lambda\,\mathbf{1}_{\{o=o^{\star}\}}</annotation></semantics></math>
with <math id="A7.SS2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. From (<a href="#A7.E10" title="In Proof. ‣ G.2 Does a Compositional Parent Agent Yield Compositional Subagents? ‣ Appendix G Recursive Splitting of Agents under Logarithmic Pooling ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex149" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex149.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1,1}^{(\lambda)}(o)\;\propto\;P_{1}(o)\,\exp\!\big((1-\alpha)g_{\lambda}(o)\big)=\begin{cases}P_{1}(o^{\star})\,e^{-(1-\alpha)\lambda},&amp;o=o^{\star},\\[2.0pt]
P_{1}(o),&amp;o\neq o^{\star},\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">∝</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1,1}^{(\lambda)}(o)\;\propto\;P_{1}(o)\,\exp\!\big((1-\alpha)g_{\lambda}(o)\big)=\begin{cases}P_{1}(o^{\star})\,e^{-(1-\alpha)\lambda},&amp;o=o^{\star},\\[2.0pt]
P_{1}(o),&amp;o\neq o^{\star},\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">so, after normalization,</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex150" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex150.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1,1}^{(\lambda)}(o^{\star})=\frac{P_{1}(o^{\star})e^{-(1-\alpha)\lambda}}{P_{1}(o^{\star})e^{-(1-\alpha)\lambda}+\sum_{o\neq o^{\star}}P_{1}(o)}\;\xrightarrow[\lambda\to\infty]{}\;0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mo lspace="0.558em">→</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">λ</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mphantom></mphantom></munderover><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1,1}^{(\lambda)}(o^{\star})=\frac{P_{1}(o^{\star})e^{-(1-\alpha)\lambda}}{P_{1}(o^{\star})e^{-(1-\alpha)\lambda}+\sum_{o\neq o^{\star}}P_{1}(o)}\;\xrightarrow[\lambda\to\infty]{}\;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">while <math id="A7.SS2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1,1}^{(\lambda)}(o)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1,1}^{(\lambda)}(o)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A7.SS2.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\neq o^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\neq o^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>. We have by Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem45" title="Lemma 45 (Binary coarse–graining lower bound). ‣ G.2 Does a Compositional Parent Agent Yield Compositional Subagents? ‣ Appendix G Recursive Splitting of Agents under Logarithmic Pooling ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">45</span></a> that for <math id="A7.SS2.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\{o^{\star}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\{o^{\star}\}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex151" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex151.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\KL\!\big(P_{t}\,\big\|\,P_{1,1}^{(\lambda)}\big)\;\geq\;P_{t}(A)\log\frac{P_{t}(A)}{P_{1,1}^{(\lambda)}(A)}\;+\;P_{t}(A^{c})\log\frac{P_{t}(A^{c})}{P_{1,1}^{(\lambda)}(A^{c})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.431em;" width="1.431em"><mi>KL</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL\!\big(P_{t}\,\big\|\,P_{1,1}^{(\lambda)}\big)\;\geq\;P_{t}(A)\log\frac{P_{t}(A)}{P_{1,1}^{(\lambda)}(A)}\;+\;P_{t}(A^{c})\log\frac{P_{t}(A^{c})}{P_{1,1}^{(\lambda)}(A^{c})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p9.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p9.4.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A7.SS2.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}(o^{\star})=P_{t}(A)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}(o^{\star})=P_{t}(A)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS2.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1,1}^{(\lambda)}(o^{\star})=P_{1,1}^{(\lambda)}(A)\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1,1}^{(\lambda)}(o^{\star})=P_{1,1}^{(\lambda)}(A)\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> while
<math id="A7.SS2.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1,1}^{(\lambda)}(A^{c})\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1,1}^{(\lambda)}(A^{c})\to 1</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex152" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex152.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\KL\!\big(P_{t}\,\big\|\,P_{1,1}^{(\lambda)}\big)\;\gtrsim\;P_{t}(o^{\star})\log\frac{P_{t}(o^{\star})}{P_{1,1}^{(\lambda)}(o^{\star})}\;+\;\bigl(1-P_{t}(o^{\star})\bigr)\log\bigl(1-P_{t}(o^{\star})\bigr)\;\xrightarrow[\lambda\to\infty]{}\;+\infty." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.431em;" width="1.431em"><mi>KL</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≳</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mo rspace="0em">→</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">λ</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mphantom></mphantom></munderover><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL\!\big(P_{t}\,\big\|\,P_{1,1}^{(\lambda)}\big)\;\gtrsim\;P_{t}(o^{\star})\log\frac{P_{t}(o^{\star})}{P_{1,1}^{(\lambda)}(o^{\star})}\;+\;\bigl(1-P_{t}(o^{\star})\bigr)\log\bigl(1-P_{t}(o^{\star})\bigr)\;\xrightarrow[\lambda\to\infty]{}\;+\infty.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">On the other hand, for every <math id="A7.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex153" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex153.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\;\leq\;H\!\big(P_{1,1}^{(\lambda)}\big)\;\leq\;\log|\mathcal{O}|," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.742em;" width="0.742em"><mi>H</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\;\leq\;H\!\big(P_{1,1}^{(\lambda)}\big)\;\leq\;\log|\mathcal{O}|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">since entropy on a finite alphabet is always between <math id="A7.SS2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> (point mass) and <math id="A7.SS2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log|\mathcal{O}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log|\mathcal{O}|</annotation></semantics></math> (uniform). Thus <math id="A7.SS2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\!\big(P_{1,1}^{(\lambda)}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.742em;" width="0.742em"><mi>H</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\!\big(P_{1,1}^{(\lambda)}\big)</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="A7.SS2.p10.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">uniformly bounded in <math id="A7.SS2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math></em>. Using Proposition <a href="#Thmtheorem32" title="Proposition 32 (Welfare gap identity for logarithmic utility). ‣ E.1 Impossibility in the Binary Case ‣ Appendix E Possible and Impossible Compositions ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex154" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex154.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta_{P_{1,1}^{(\lambda)}}(P_{t})=H\!\big(P_{1,1}^{(\lambda)}\big)-H(P_{t})-\KL\!\big(P_{t}\big\|P_{1,1}^{(\lambda)}\big)\;\xrightarrow[\lambda\to\infty]{}\;-\infty," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mpadded style="width:0.742em;" width="0.742em"><mi>H</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mpadded style="width:1.431em;" width="1.431em"><mi>KL</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mo rspace="0em">→</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">λ</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mphantom></mphantom></munderover><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{P_{1,1}^{(\lambda)}}(P_{t})=H\!\big(P_{1,1}^{(\lambda)}\big)-H(P_{t})-\KL\!\big(P_{t}\big\|P_{1,1}^{(\lambda)}\big)\;\xrightarrow[\lambda\to\infty]{}\;-\infty,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">because <math id="A7.SS2.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(P_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(P_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="A7.SS2.p10.3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">independent of <math id="A7.SS2.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math></em> (as <math id="A7.SS2.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed) and finite, the entropy term is uniformly bounded, while the KL term diverges to <math id="A7.SS2.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, for all sufficiently large <math id="A7.SS2.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A7.SS2.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{P_{1,1}^{(\lambda)}}(P_{t})&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{P_{1,1}^{(\lambda)}}(P_{t})&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>
even though <math id="A7.SS2.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{P_{1}}(P_{t})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{P_{1}}(P_{t})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p">This immediately results in the following corollary, which shows that an initially unanimous group can lose unanimity after splitting even though the composition distribution does not change.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem47" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem47.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 47</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem47.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Unanimity is not preserved under splitting)<span id="Thmtheorem47.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem47.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem47.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem47.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="Thmtheorem47.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{P_{1},\dots,P_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{P_{1},\dots,P_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math> with weights <math id="Thmtheorem47.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> form a unanimously compositional group under the log pool <math id="Thmtheorem47.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>; i.e., <math id="Thmtheorem47.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{P_{i}}(P)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{P_{i}}(P)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmtheorem47.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. There exists a compatible split of <math id="Thmtheorem47.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> into two subagents <math id="Thmtheorem47.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i,1},P_{i,2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i,1},P_{i,2}</annotation></semantics></math> such that, with the new set of agents and weights, the pooled distribution remains <math id="Thmtheorem47.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> but <math id="Thmtheorem47.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{P_{i,1}}(P)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{P_{i,1}}(P)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define the split via (<a href="#A7.E10" title="In Proof. ‣ G.2 Does a Compositional Parent Agent Yield Compositional Subagents? ‣ Appendix G Recursive Splitting of Agents under Logarithmic Pooling ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>) with a tilt <math id="A7.SS2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> that assigns a large negative value on some outcome <math id="A7.SS2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A7.SS2.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(o^{\star})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(o^{\star})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS2.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> elsewhere. As in the proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmtheorem46" title="Theorem 46 (Parental benefit need not pass to subagents). ‣ G.2 Does a Compositional Parent Agent Yield Compositional Subagents? ‣ Appendix G Recursive Splitting of Agents under Logarithmic Pooling ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">46</span></a>, Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem44" title="Lemma 44 (Pooling invariance under compatible splitting). ‣ G.1 Distributional Invariance under Splitting ‣ Appendix G Recursive Splitting of Agents under Logarithmic Pooling ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">44</span></a> ensures the pool stays <math id="A7.SS2.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>, every unchanged agent <math id="A7.SS2.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\neq i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\neq i</annotation></semantics></math> maintains the same (strictly positive) <math id="A7.SS2.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{P_{k}}(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{P_{k}}(P)</annotation></semantics></math>, while <math id="A7.SS2.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{P_{i,1}}(P)\to-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{P_{i,1}}(P)\to-\infty</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A7.SS2.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A7.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">G.2.1 </span>When does Splitting Preserve Compositionality?</h4>

<div id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The negative results above are sharp in the sense that they rely on sufficiently <em id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">polarized</em> splits. Two simple stability statements go the other way.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem48" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem48.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 48</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem48.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Cloning preserves welfare and non-strict unanimity)<span id="Thmtheorem48.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem48.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem48.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem48.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="Thmtheorem48.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1,1}=\cdots=P_{1,m}=P_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1,1}=\cdots=P_{1,m}=P_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem48.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j}\beta_{1,j}=\beta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j}\beta_{1,j}=\beta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, then for each clone <math id="Thmtheorem48.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1,j}</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="Thmtheorem48.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{P_{1,j}}(P)=\Delta_{P_{1}}(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{P_{1,j}}(P)=\Delta_{P_{1}}(P)</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, if the original group is (non-strictly) unanimously compositional, it remains so after cloning any subset of agents.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.SSS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Pooling invariance gives <math id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}=P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}=P</annotation></semantics></math>. For any clone <math id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=P_{1,j}=P_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=P_{1,j}=P_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E_{P}[\log R]=\E_{P}[\log P_{1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E_{P}[\log R]=\E_{P}[\log P_{1}]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E_{R}[\log R]=\E_{P_{1}}[\log P_{1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E_{R}[\log R]=\E_{P_{1}}[\log P_{1}]</annotation></semantics></math>, hence <math id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{R}(P)=\Delta_{P_{1}}(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{R}(P)=\Delta_{P_{1}}(P)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem49" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem49.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 49</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem49.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Small-perturbation stability)<span id="Thmtheorem49.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem49.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem49.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem49.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix a composition pool <math id="Thmtheorem49.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> with all coordinates bounded below by <math id="Thmtheorem49.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{p}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{p}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then for a distribution <math id="Thmtheorem49.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>, the map <math id="Thmtheorem49.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\mapsto\Delta_{R}(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\mapsto\Delta_{R}(P)</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous on the interior of the simplex. Hence, for any agent <math id="Thmtheorem49.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmtheorem49.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{R_{\star}}(P)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{R_{\star}}(P)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="Thmtheorem49.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that if a subagent <math id="Thmtheorem49.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex155" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex155.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\log R-\log R_{\star}\|_{\infty}&lt;\varepsilon," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\log R-\log R_{\star}\|_{\infty}&lt;\varepsilon,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem49.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem49.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">then <math id="Thmtheorem49.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{R}(P)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{R}(P)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, if <math id="Thmtheorem49.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> benefits and each subagent <math id="Thmtheorem49.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1,j}</annotation></semantics></math> is a sufficiently small log-perturbation of <math id="Thmtheorem49.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, the split preserves positivity of each <math id="Thmtheorem49.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{P_{1,j}}(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{P_{1,j}}(P)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.SSS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using Proposition <a href="#Thmtheorem32" title="Proposition 32 (Welfare gap identity for logarithmic utility). ‣ E.1 Impossibility in the Binary Case ‣ Appendix E Possible and Impossible Compositions ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>, <math id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta_{R}(P)=H(R)-\KL(P\|R)-H(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{R}(P)=H(R)-\KL(P\|R)-H(P)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(P)</annotation></semantics></math> is constant. On the interior of the simplex, <math id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous. Moreover</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex156" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex156.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\KL(P\|R)\;=\;\sum_{o\in\mathcal{O}}P(o)\,\big(-\log R(o)\big)-H(P)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>R</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></munder><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(P\|R)\;=\;\sum_{o\in\mathcal{O}}P(o)\,\big(-\log R(o)\big)-H(P),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">so if <math id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\log R-\log R_{\star}\|_{\infty}&lt;\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\log R-\log R_{\star}\|_{\infty}&lt;\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> then</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex157" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex157.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\big|\KL(P\|R)-\KL(P\|R_{\star})\big|\leq\sum_{o}P(o)\,\big|\log R(o)-\log R_{\star}(o)\big|\leq\varepsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></munder><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big|\KL(P\|R)-\KL(P\|R_{\star})\big|\leq\sum_{o}P(o)\,\big|\log R(o)-\log R_{\star}(o)\big|\leq\varepsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus <math id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\mapsto\Delta_{R}(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\mapsto\Delta_{R}(P)</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous. Pick <math id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> small enough that
<math id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Delta_{R}(P)-\Delta_{R_{\star}}(P)|&lt;\tfrac{1}{2}\,\Delta_{R_{\star}}(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Delta_{R}(P)-\Delta_{R_{\star}}(P)|&lt;\tfrac{1}{2}\,\Delta_{R_{\star}}(P)</annotation></semantics></math>
whenever <math id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\log R-\log R_{\star}\|_{\infty}&lt;\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\log R-\log R_{\star}\|_{\infty}&lt;\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies <math id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{R}(P)&gt;\tfrac{1}{2}\,\Delta_{R_{\star}}(P)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{R}(P)&gt;\tfrac{1}{2}\,\Delta_{R_{\star}}(P)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem50" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem50.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 50</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem50.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem50.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem50.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem50.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If some distributions have zeros, all statements above hold verbatim after restricting every distribution to the common support <math id="Thmtheorem50.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\supp(P)\cap\bigcap_{i}\supp(P_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">∩</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⋂</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi></msub><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">P</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\supp(P)\cap\bigcap_{i}\supp(P_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> (or, for Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem47" title="Corollary 47 (Unanimity is not preserved under splitting). ‣ G.2 Does a Compositional Parent Agent Yield Compositional Subagents? ‣ Appendix G Recursive Splitting of Agents under Logarithmic Pooling ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">47</span></a>, any support where <math id="Thmtheorem50.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> is positive). Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem49" title="Lemma 49 (Small-perturbation stability). ‣ G.2.1 When does Splitting Preserve Compositionality? ‣ G.2 Does a Compositional Parent Agent Yield Compositional Subagents? ‣ Appendix G Recursive Splitting of Agents under Logarithmic Pooling ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">49</span></a> then applies as long as we stay in the interior of that reduced simplex.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem51" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem51.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 51</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem51.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem51.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem51.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem51.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem44" title="Lemma 44 (Pooling invariance under compatible splitting). ‣ G.1 Distributional Invariance under Splitting ‣ Appendix G Recursive Splitting of Agents under Logarithmic Pooling ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">44</span></a> shows that log pooling is <em id="Thmtheorem51.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">distributionally</em> recursion-invariant under compatible splits. However, Proposition <a href="#Thmtheorem46" title="Theorem 46 (Parental benefit need not pass to subagents). ‣ G.2 Does a Compositional Parent Agent Yield Compositional Subagents? ‣ Appendix G Recursive Splitting of Agents under Logarithmic Pooling ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">46</span></a> and Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem47" title="Corollary 47 (Unanimity is not preserved under splitting). ‣ G.2 Does a Compositional Parent Agent Yield Compositional Subagents? ‣ Appendix G Recursive Splitting of Agents under Logarithmic Pooling ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">47</span></a> demonstrate that welfare and unanimity are <em id="Thmtheorem51.p1.1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">not</em> recursion-invariant in general: a strictly beneficial parent can have strictly harmed subagents, and an initially unanimous group can lose unanimity after splitting, even though the pooled distribution is unchanged. On the positive side, Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem48" title="Lemma 48 (Cloning preserves welfare and non-strict unanimity). ‣ G.2.1 When does Splitting Preserve Compositionality? ‣ G.2 Does a Compositional Parent Agent Yield Compositional Subagents? ‣ Appendix G Recursive Splitting of Agents under Logarithmic Pooling ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">48</span></a> (cloning) and Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem49" title="Lemma 49 (Small-perturbation stability). ‣ G.2.1 When does Splitting Preserve Compositionality? ‣ G.2 Does a Compositional Parent Agent Yield Compositional Subagents? ‣ Appendix G Recursive Splitting of Agents under Logarithmic Pooling ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">49</span></a> (continuity) give simple sufficient conditions under which (possibly non-strict) compositionality is preserved.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A8" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix H </span>Properties of Strict Local (Small-Tilt) Unanimity</h2>

<div id="A8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the previous section, we showed that duplication preserves non-strict unanimous compositionality. One might attempt to <em id="A8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">cheat</em> strict compositionality by taking an arbitrary distribution <math id="A8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>, duplicating each agent, and introducing only slight perturbations to their beliefs, hoping that the resulting group would be unanimously compositional. We now show that this strategy is doomed to fail: such near-duplication decompositions cannot achieve unanimous strict improvement for a fixed <math id="A8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we show that even when <math id="A8.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{O}|\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{O}|\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>, if the pooled distribution is fixed to be a given <math id="A8.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and we factor it via (<a href="#A8.E11" title="In Lemma 52. ‣ Appendix H Properties of Strict Local (Small-Tilt) Unanimity ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>) with small tilts <math id="A8.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, then unanimous strict improvement cannot occur. This rules out the possibility of obtaining unanimity through “uniformly small” decompositions when <math id="A8.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed. We start by proving several lemmas.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem52" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem52.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 52</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem52.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem52.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem52.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem52.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Whenever <math id="Thmtheorem52.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\propto\prod_{i}P_{i}^{\beta_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∝</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\propto\prod_{i}P_{i}^{\beta_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can write each component as a <em id="Thmtheorem52.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">tilt</em> of <math id="Thmtheorem52.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A8.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}(o)\ =\ \frac{P(o)\,e^{h_{i}(o)}}{Z_{i}},\qquad Z_{i}:=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{O}}P(x)e^{h_{i}(x)}\ (=\E_{P}[e^{h_{i}}])," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:0.389em;" width="0.389em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}(o)\ =\ \frac{P(o)\,e^{h_{i}(o)}}{Z_{i}},\qquad Z_{i}:=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{O}}P(x)e^{h_{i}(x)}\ (=\E_{P}[e^{h_{i}}]),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem52.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem52.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for some functions <math id="Thmtheorem52.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{i}:\mathcal{O}\to\R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{i}:\mathcal{O}\to\R</annotation></semantics></math>. We may without loss of generality impose</span></p>
<table id="A8.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}h_{i}(o)\ \equiv\ 0\quad\text{for all }o\in\mathcal{O}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}h_{i}(o)\ \equiv\ 0\quad\text{for all }o\in\mathcal{O}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A8.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A8.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Assume <math id="A8.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and all distributions are strictly positive on the finite outcome set <math id="A8.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Suppose the composition <math id="A8.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> is the logarithmic pool of <math id="A8.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1},\dots,P_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1},\dots,P_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> with weights <math id="A8.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A8.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(o)\ =\ \frac{1}{Z}\,\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}},\qquad Z\ :=\ \sum_{x\in\mathcal{O}}\ \prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(x)^{\beta_{i}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>Z</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.611em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(o)\ =\ \frac{1}{Z}\,\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}},\qquad Z\ :=\ \sum_{x\in\mathcal{O}}\ \prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(x)^{\beta_{i}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A8.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define, for each <math id="A8.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A8.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{i}^{(0)}(o)\ :=\ \log\frac{P_{i}(o)}{P(o)}\quad\text{for all }o\in\mathcal{O}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{i}^{(0)}(o)\ :=\ \log\frac{P_{i}(o)}{P(o)}\quad\text{for all }o\in\mathcal{O}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex158" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex158.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(o)\,e^{h_{i}^{(0)}(o)}\;=\;P(o)\,\frac{P_{i}(o)}{P(o)}\;=\;P_{i}(o)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(o)\,e^{h_{i}^{(0)}(o)}\;=\;P(o)\,\frac{P_{i}(o)}{P(o)}\;=\;P_{i}(o).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, with <math id="A8.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}^{(0)}:=\sum_{x}P(x)e^{h_{i}^{(0)}(x)}=\sum_{x}P_{i}(x)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}^{(0)}:=\sum_{x}P(x)e^{h_{i}^{(0)}(x)}=\sum_{x}P_{i}(x)=1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the exact “tilt” identity</span></p>
<table id="A8.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}(o)\ =\ \frac{P(o)\,e^{h_{i}^{(0)}(o)}}{Z_{i}^{(0)}}\;=\;P(o)\,e^{h_{i}^{(0)}(o)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}(o)\ =\ \frac{P(o)\,e^{h_{i}^{(0)}(o)}}{Z_{i}^{(0)}}\;=\;P(o)\,e^{h_{i}^{(0)}(o)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">This proves (<a href="#A8.E11" title="In Lemma 52. ‣ Appendix H Properties of Strict Local (Small-Tilt) Unanimity ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>) with the specific choice <math id="A8.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{i}=h_{i}^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{i}=h_{i}^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A8.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Taking logs in (<a href="#A8.E13" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix H Properties of Strict Local (Small-Tilt) Unanimity ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex159" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex159.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log P(o)\ =\ \sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\log P_{i}(o)\ -\ \log Z." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.611em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log P(o)\ =\ \sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\log P_{i}(o)\ -\ \log Z.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A8.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A8.Ex160"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex160.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\,h_{i}^{(0)}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\,h_{i}^{(0)}(o)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex160.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\big(\log P_{i}(o)-\log P(o)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\big(\log P_{i}(o)-\log P(o)\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A8.Ex161"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex161.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\Big(\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\log P_{i}(o)\Big)\ -\ \log P(o)\qquad(\text{since }\sum_{i}\beta_{i}=1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>since </mtext><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Big(\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\log P_{i}(o)\Big)\ -\ \log P(o)\qquad(\text{since }\sum_{i}\beta_{i}=1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A8.Ex162"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex162.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\ \log Z\quad\text{(independent of $o$)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mtext>(independent of </mtext><mi>o</mi><mtext>)</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\ \log Z\quad\text{(independent of $o$)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">The tilt representation (<a href="#A8.E15" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix H Properties of Strict Local (Small-Tilt) Unanimity ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>) is invariant under adding an additive constant to <math id="A8.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and scaling <math id="A8.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> accordingly:
if we set</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex163" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex163.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{i}(o)\ :=\ h_{i}^{(0)}(o)-c_{i},\qquad Z_{i}\ :=\ e^{-c_{i}}Z_{i}^{(0)}=e^{-c_{i}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{i}(o)\ :=\ h_{i}^{(0)}(o)-c_{i},\qquad Z_{i}\ :=\ e^{-c_{i}}Z_{i}^{(0)}=e^{-c_{i}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p4.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p4.7.1" class="ltx_text">then</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex164" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex164.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{P(o)\,e^{h_{i}(o)}}{Z_{i}}=\frac{P(o)\,e^{h_{i}^{(0)}(o)-c_{i}}}{e^{-c_{i}}Z_{i}^{(0)}}=\frac{P(o)\,e^{h_{i}^{(0)}(o)}}{Z_{i}^{(0)}}=P_{i}(o)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{P(o)\,e^{h_{i}(o)}}{Z_{i}}=\frac{P(o)\,e^{h_{i}^{(0)}(o)-c_{i}}}{e^{-c_{i}}Z_{i}^{(0)}}=\frac{P(o)\,e^{h_{i}^{(0)}(o)}}{Z_{i}^{(0)}}=P_{i}(o),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p4.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p4.8.1" class="ltx_text">so the distributions <math id="A8.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> do not change. As <math id="A8.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}\beta_{i}h_{i}^{(0)}\equiv\log Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}\beta_{i}h_{i}^{(0)}\equiv\log Z</annotation></semantics></math>, choose any index <math id="A8.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> and set <math id="A8.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}:=\frac{\log Z}{\beta_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}:=\frac{\log Z}{\beta_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math>, while <math id="A8.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}:=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}:=0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A8.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq k</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then the modified functions <math id="A8.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex165" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex165.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}h_{i}(o)=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}h_{i}^{(0)}(o)\ -\ \beta_{k}c_{k}=\log Z\ -\ \log Z\ =\ 0\quad\text{for all }o." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.722em" rspace="0.722em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.778em">=</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}h_{i}(o)=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}h_{i}^{(0)}(o)\ -\ \beta_{k}c_{k}=\log Z\ -\ \log Z\ =\ 0\quad\text{for all }o.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p4.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p4.9.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, without loss of generality, we may assume</span></p>
<table id="A8.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}h_{i}(o)\ \equiv\ 0,\qquad\forall o\in\mathcal{O}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>o</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}h_{i}(o)\ \equiv\ 0,\qquad\forall o\in\mathcal{O}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p4.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p4.10.1" class="ltx_text">We note that imposing (<a href="#A8.E16" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix H Properties of Strict Local (Small-Tilt) Unanimity ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>) is achieved by subtracting a constant from a single <math id="A8.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, which leaves each <math id="A8.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> exactly unchanged due to rescaling <math id="A8.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> by a constant factor.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem53" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem53.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 53</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem53.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem53.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem53.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem53.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We note that the freedom to add constants <math id="Thmtheorem53.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="Thmtheorem53.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <em id="Thmtheorem53.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">only</em> freedom in the tilt representation relative to a fixed base <math id="Thmtheorem53.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>; it corresponds to renormalizing <math id="Thmtheorem53.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and does not alter <math id="Thmtheorem53.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem54" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem54.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 54</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem54.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem54.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem54.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem54.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For a fixed <math id="Thmtheorem54.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem54.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="Thmtheorem54.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, let</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex166" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex166.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)}(o)\ =\ \frac{P(o)\,e^{\varepsilon h_{i}(o)}}{Z_{i}(\varepsilon)},\qquad Z_{i}(\varepsilon)\ :=\ \sum_{x\in\mathcal{O}}P(x)\,e^{\varepsilon h_{i}(x)}\ =\ \E_{P}\!\big[e^{\varepsilon h_{i}}\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.611em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)}(o)\ =\ \frac{P(o)\,e^{\varepsilon h_{i}(o)}}{Z_{i}(\varepsilon)},\qquad Z_{i}(\varepsilon)\ :=\ \sum_{x\in\mathcal{O}}P(x)\,e^{\varepsilon h_{i}(x)}\ =\ \E_{P}\!\big[e^{\varepsilon h_{i}}\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem54.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem54.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex167" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex167.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}H\!\big(P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)}\big)\Big|_{\varepsilon=0}=-\Big(\E_{P}[h_{i}\log P]-\E_{P}[h_{i}]\;\E_{P}[\log P]\Big)=-\,\Cov_{P}\!\big(h_{i},\log P\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.742em;" width="0.742em"><mi>H</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.447em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}H\!\big(P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)}\big)\Big|_{\varepsilon=0}=-\Big(\E_{P}[h_{i}\log P]-\E_{P}[h_{i}]\;\E_{P}[\log P]\Big)=-\,\Cov_{P}\!\big(h_{i},\log P\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem54.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem54.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We assume all probabilities are strictly positive.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A8.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A8.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A8.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\varepsilon}(o)=P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\varepsilon}(o)=P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)}(o)</annotation></semantics></math>. By definition,</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex168" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex168.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H(q_{\varepsilon})\ =\ -\sum_{o\in\mathcal{O}}q_{\varepsilon}(o)\,\log q_{\varepsilon}(o)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(q_{\varepsilon})\ =\ -\sum_{o\in\mathcal{O}}q_{\varepsilon}(o)\,\log q_{\varepsilon}(o).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Differentiating termwise,</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex169" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex169.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}H(q_{\varepsilon})=-\sum_{o}\Big(\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}q_{\varepsilon}(o)\Big)\,\log q_{\varepsilon}(o)-\sum_{o}q_{\varepsilon}(o)\,\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}\log q_{\varepsilon}(o)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.337em">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></munder><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}H(q_{\varepsilon})=-\sum_{o}\Big(\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}q_{\varepsilon}(o)\Big)\,\log q_{\varepsilon}(o)-\sum_{o}q_{\varepsilon}(o)\,\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}\log q_{\varepsilon}(o).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A8.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}\log q_{\varepsilon}(o)=\frac{1}{q_{\varepsilon}(o)}\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}q_{\varepsilon}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}\log q_{\varepsilon}(o)=\frac{1}{q_{\varepsilon}(o)}\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}q_{\varepsilon}(o)</annotation></semantics></math>, we can combine the two sums:</span></p>
<table id="A8.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}H(q_{\varepsilon})=-\sum_{o}\Big(\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}q_{\varepsilon}(o)\Big)\,\Big(1+\log q_{\varepsilon}(o)\Big)=-\sum_{o}q_{\varepsilon}(o)\,\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}\log q_{\varepsilon}(o)\,\Big(1+\log q_{\varepsilon}(o)\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></munder><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}H(q_{\varepsilon})=-\sum_{o}\Big(\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}q_{\varepsilon}(o)\Big)\,\Big(1+\log q_{\varepsilon}(o)\Big)=-\sum_{o}q_{\varepsilon}(o)\,\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}\log q_{\varepsilon}(o)\,\Big(1+\log q_{\varepsilon}(o)\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">From the definition of <math id="A8.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex170" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex170.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log q_{\varepsilon}(o)=\log P(o)+\varepsilon\,h_{i}(o)-\log Z_{i}(\varepsilon)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log q_{\varepsilon}(o)=\log P(o)+\varepsilon\,h_{i}(o)-\log Z_{i}(\varepsilon).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore</span></p>
<table id="A8.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}\log q_{\varepsilon}(o)=h_{i}(o)-\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}\log Z_{i}(\varepsilon)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}\log q_{\varepsilon}(o)=h_{i}(o)-\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}\log Z_{i}(\varepsilon).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p5.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p5.6.1" class="ltx_text">Compute the latter factor using <math id="A8.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}^{\prime}(\varepsilon)=\sum_{x}P(x)\,h_{i}(x)\,e^{\varepsilon h_{i}(x)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}^{\prime}(\varepsilon)=\sum_{x}P(x)\,h_{i}(x)\,e^{\varepsilon h_{i}(x)}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex171" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex171.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}\log Z_{i}(\varepsilon)=\frac{Z_{i}^{\prime}(\varepsilon)}{Z_{i}(\varepsilon)}=\frac{\sum_{x}P(x)\,h_{i}(x)\,e^{\varepsilon h_{i}(x)}}{\sum_{x}P(x)\,e^{\varepsilon h_{i}(x)}}=\sum_{x}\frac{P(x)\,e^{\varepsilon h_{i}(x)}}{Z_{i}(\varepsilon)}\,h_{i}(x)=\E_{q_{\varepsilon}}[\,h_{i}\,]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>x</mi></munder><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}\log Z_{i}(\varepsilon)=\frac{Z_{i}^{\prime}(\varepsilon)}{Z_{i}(\varepsilon)}=\frac{\sum_{x}P(x)\,h_{i}(x)\,e^{\varepsilon h_{i}(x)}}{\sum_{x}P(x)\,e^{\varepsilon h_{i}(x)}}=\sum_{x}\frac{P(x)\,e^{\varepsilon h_{i}(x)}}{Z_{i}(\varepsilon)}\,h_{i}(x)=\E_{q_{\varepsilon}}[\,h_{i}\,].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p5.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p5.7.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, evaluating (<a href="#A8.E18" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix H Properties of Strict Local (Small-Tilt) Unanimity ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>) at <math id="A8.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=0</annotation></semantics></math> (where <math id="A8.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{0}=P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{0}=P</annotation></semantics></math>),</span></p>
<table id="A8.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Big[\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}\log q_{\varepsilon}(o)\Big]_{\varepsilon=0}=h_{i}(o)-\E_{q_{0}}[h_{i}]=h_{i}(o)-\E_{P}[h_{i}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Big[\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}\log q_{\varepsilon}(o)\Big]_{\varepsilon=0}=h_{i}(o)-\E_{q_{0}}[h_{i}]=h_{i}(o)-\E_{P}[h_{i}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p5.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p5.8.1" class="ltx_text">Using (<a href="#A8.E17" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix H Properties of Strict Local (Small-Tilt) Unanimity ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>) and (<a href="#A8.E19" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix H Properties of Strict Local (Small-Tilt) Unanimity ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A8.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A8.Ex172"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex172.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}H(q_{\varepsilon})\Big|_{\varepsilon=0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}H(q_{\varepsilon})\Big|_{\varepsilon=0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex172.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\sum_{o}P(o)\,\Big(h_{i}(o)-\E_{P}[h_{i}]\Big)\,\Big(1+\log P(o)\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></munder></mstyle><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\sum_{o}P(o)\,\Big(h_{i}(o)-\E_{P}[h_{i}]\Big)\,\Big(1+\log P(o)\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A8.Ex173"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex173.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\E_{P}\!\Big[\big(h_{i}-\E_{P}[h_{i}]\big)\,(1+\log P)\Big]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\E_{P}\!\Big[\big(h_{i}-\E_{P}[h_{i}]\big)\,(1+\log P)\Big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p5.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p5.9.1" class="ltx_text">Expand the expectation:</span></p>
<table id="A8.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A8.Ex174"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex174.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\E_{P}\!\Big[\big(h_{i}-\E_{P}[h_{i}]\big)\,(1+\log P)\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\E_{P}\!\Big[\big(h_{i}-\E_{P}[h_{i}]\big)\,(1+\log P)\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex174.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\E_{P}[h_{i}(1+\log P)]-\E_{P}[h_{i}]\;\E_{P}[\,1+\log P\,]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.447em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\E_{P}[h_{i}(1+\log P)]-\E_{P}[h_{i}]\;\E_{P}[\,1+\log P\,]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A8.Ex175"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex175.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\E_{P}[h_{i}\log P]+\E_{P}[h_{i}]-\E_{P}[h_{i}]\,(1+\E_{P}[\log P])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\E_{P}[h_{i}\log P]+\E_{P}[h_{i}]-\E_{P}[h_{i}]\,(1+\E_{P}[\log P])</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A8.Ex176"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex176.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\E_{P}[h_{i}\log P]-\E_{P}[h_{i}]\;\E_{P}[\log P]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.447em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\E_{P}[h_{i}\log P]-\E_{P}[h_{i}]\;\E_{P}[\log P].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p5.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p5.10.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex177" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex177.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}H\!\big(P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)}\big)\Big|_{\varepsilon=0}=-\Big(\E_{P}[h_{i}\log P]-\E_{P}[h_{i}]\;\E_{P}[\log P]\Big)=-\,\Cov_{P}\!\big(h_{i},\log P\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.742em;" width="0.742em"><mi>H</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.447em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}H\!\big(P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)}\big)\Big|_{\varepsilon=0}=-\Big(\E_{P}[h_{i}\log P]-\E_{P}[h_{i}]\;\E_{P}[\log P]\Big)=-\,\Cov_{P}\!\big(h_{i},\log P\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p5.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p5.11.1" class="ltx_text">This is the claimed identity.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A8.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We may now show the following theorem.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem55" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem55.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 55</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem55.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Local unanimity impossibility at a fixed pool)<span id="Thmtheorem55.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem55.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem55.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem55.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="Thmtheorem55.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> strictly positive on <math id="Thmtheorem55.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose <math id="Thmtheorem55.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}=P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)}=P\,e^{\varepsilon h_{i}}/Z_{i}(\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}=P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)}=P\,e^{\varepsilon h_{i}}/Z_{i}(\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmtheorem55.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}\beta_{i}h_{i}\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}\beta_{i}h_{i}\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math> as in (<a href="#A8.E12" title="In Lemma 52. ‣ Appendix H Properties of Strict Local (Small-Tilt) Unanimity ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>). Then, for all sufficiently small <math id="Thmtheorem55.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, it is impossible that <math id="Thmtheorem55.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{P_{i}}(P)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{P_{i}}(P)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> holds for <em id="Thmtheorem55.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">every</em> <math id="Thmtheorem55.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A8.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A8.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define <math id="A8.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)}</annotation></semantics></math> as above and write <math id="A8.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}(\varepsilon):=\Delta_{P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)}}(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}(\varepsilon):=\Delta_{P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)}}(P)</annotation></semantics></math>. We claim</span></p>
<table id="A8.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}^{\prime}(0)\ =\ -\,\Cov_{P}(h_{i},\log P)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}^{\prime}(0)\ =\ -\,\Cov_{P}(h_{i},\log P).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">To prove (<a href="#A8.E20" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix H Properties of Strict Local (Small-Tilt) Unanimity ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>), note from Proposition <a href="#Thmtheorem32" title="Proposition 32 (Welfare gap identity for logarithmic utility). ‣ E.1 Impossibility in the Binary Case ‣ Appendix E Possible and Impossible Compositions ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a> that
<math id="A8.p7.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta_{i}(\varepsilon)=H(P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)})-H(P)-\KL(P\|P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}(\varepsilon)=H(P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)})-H(P)-\KL(P\|P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Differentiate at <math id="A8.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=0</annotation></semantics></math>. First, <math id="A8.p7.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}\KL(P\|P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)})\big|_{\varepsilon=0}=\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}\E_{P}\!\big[\log\tfrac{P}{P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)}}\big]\big|_{\varepsilon=0}=-\,\E_{P}\!\big[\tfrac{d}{d\varepsilon}\log P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)}\big]_{\varepsilon=0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mi>P</mi><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><msub><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.392em">−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi>log</mi><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}\KL(P\|P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)})\big|_{\varepsilon=0}=\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}\E_{P}\!\big[\log\tfrac{P}{P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)}}\big]\big|_{\varepsilon=0}=-\,\E_{P}\!\big[\tfrac{d}{d\varepsilon}\log P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)}\big]_{\varepsilon=0}</annotation></semantics></math>.
From <math id="A8.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)}\propto Pe^{\varepsilon h_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)}\propto Pe^{\varepsilon h_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> we have
<math id="A8.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)}=\log P+\varepsilon h_{i}-\log Z_{i}(\varepsilon)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)}=\log P+\varepsilon h_{i}-\log Z_{i}(\varepsilon),</annotation></semantics></math>
so <math id="A8.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}\log P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)}\big|_{0}=h_{i}-\E_{P}[h_{i}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}\log P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)}\big|_{0}=h_{i}-\E_{P}[h_{i}]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence</span></p>
<table id="A8.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}\KL(P\|P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)})\Big|_{0}=-\,\big(\E_{P}[h_{i}]-\E_{P}[h_{i}]\big)=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.392em">−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}\KL(P\|P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)})\Big|_{0}=-\,\big(\E_{P}[h_{i}]-\E_{P}[h_{i}]\big)=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">Next, <math id="A8.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)})=-\E_{P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)}}[\log P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)})=-\E_{P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)}}[\log P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)}]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Differentiating at <math id="A8.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> gives by Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem54" title="Lemma 54. ‣ Appendix H Properties of Strict Local (Small-Tilt) Unanimity ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">54</span></a></span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex178" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex178.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}H(P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)})\Big|_{0}=-\,\Cov_{P}(h_{i},\log P)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}H(P_{i}^{(\varepsilon)})\Big|_{0}=-\,\Cov_{P}(h_{i},\log P).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">Combining with (<a href="#A8.E21" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix H Properties of Strict Local (Small-Tilt) Unanimity ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>) we obtain (<a href="#A8.E20" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix H Properties of Strict Local (Small-Tilt) Unanimity ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>).
By (<a href="#A8.E12" title="In Lemma 52. ‣ Appendix H Properties of Strict Local (Small-Tilt) Unanimity ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>), <math id="A8.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}\beta_{i}h_{i}\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}\beta_{i}h_{i}\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math>, so</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex179" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex179.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\,\Delta_{i}^{\prime}(0)=-\,\Cov_{P}\!\Big(\sum_{i}\beta_{i}h_{i},\ \log P\Big)=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\,\Delta_{i}^{\prime}(0)=-\,\Cov_{P}\!\Big(\sum_{i}\beta_{i}h_{i},\ \log P\Big)=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p7.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p7.5.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore the <math id="A8.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>–weighted average of the derivatives <math id="A8.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}^{\prime}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}^{\prime}(0)</annotation></semantics></math> is zero; in particular, they cannot all be strictly positive as <math id="A8.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, for all sufficiently small <math id="A8.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, it is impossible that <math id="A8.p7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}(\varepsilon)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}(\varepsilon)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="A8.p7.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> (otherwise all <math id="A8.p7.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}^{\prime}(0)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}^{\prime}(0)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> with some <math id="A8.p7.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> by right-derivative positivity, contradicting the weighted average zero).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem56" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem56.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 56</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem56.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem56.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem56.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem56.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem55" title="Theorem 55 (Local unanimity impossibility at a fixed pool). ‣ Appendix H Properties of Strict Local (Small-Tilt) Unanimity ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">55</span></a> does <em id="Thmtheorem56.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">not</em> rule out the possibility that for some <em id="Thmtheorem56.p1.1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">large</em> tilts (finite <math id="Thmtheorem56.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>), all <math id="Thmtheorem56.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{P_{i}}(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{P_{i}}(P)</annotation></semantics></math> might be positive; it only precludes near-uniform (i.e., near-duplicate) small-tilt unanimity around a fixed pool <math id="Thmtheorem56.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>. For instance, contrast with the proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem62" title="Theorem 62 (Openness). ‣ H.2 Openness of Strictly Unanimously Decomposable Pools ‣ Appendix H Properties of Strict Local (Small-Tilt) Unanimity ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">62</span></a>, which guarantees strict positivity for large tilts under some unrestrictive conditions.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A8.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">H.1 </span>On Joining Random Distributions</h3>

<div id="A8.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The next theorem shows that no distribution <math id="A8.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> is incentivized, in the compositional sense, to join a maximal entropy or completely random distribution.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem57" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem57.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 57</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem57.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(No strict gains at the uniform)<span id="Thmtheorem57.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem57.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem57.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem57.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem57.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> be the uniform distribution on a finite <math id="Thmtheorem57.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmtheorem57.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{O}|=m\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{O}|=m\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. For any strictly positive <math id="Thmtheorem57.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex180" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex180.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta_{R}(U)\;=\;H(R)\;-\;\log m\;-\;\KL(U\|R)\;\leq\;0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>R</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn> 0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{R}(U)\;=\;H(R)\;-\;\log m\;-\;\KL(U\|R)\;\leq\;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem57.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem57.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with equality iff <math id="Thmtheorem57.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=U</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A8.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">By definition <math id="A8.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{R}(U)=\E_{U}[\log R]-\E_{R}[\log R]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{R}(U)=\E_{U}[\log R]-\E_{R}[\log R]</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A8.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(U)=\log m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(U)=\log m</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A8.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\KL(U\|R)=\E_{U}[\log U-\log R]=-\log m-\E_{U}[\log R]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>U</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(U\|R)=\E_{U}[\log U-\log R]=-\log m-\E_{U}[\log R]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex181" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex181.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta_{R}(U)=\big(-\log m-\KL(U\|R)\big)+H(R)=H(R)-\log m-\KL(U\|R)\leq 0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{R}(U)=\big(-\log m-\KL(U\|R)\big)+H(R)=H(R)-\log m-\KL(U\|R)\leq 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">with equality iff <math id="A8.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=U</annotation></semantics></math> (Gibbs’ inequality). Alternatively, for the final step, we may compute <math id="A8.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\KL(R\|U)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(R\|U)</annotation></semantics></math> explicitly:</span></p>
<table id="A8.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A8.Ex182"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex182.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\KL(R\|U)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\KL(R\|U)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex182.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{o}R(o)\,\log\frac{R(o)}{1/m}\;=\;\sum_{o}R(o)\,\log R(o)\;+\;\sum_{o}R(o)\,\log m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{o}R(o)\,\log\frac{R(o)}{1/m}\;=\;\sum_{o}R(o)\,\log R(o)\;+\;\sum_{o}R(o)\,\log m</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A8.Ex183"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex183.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{o}R(o)\,\log R(o)\;+\;\log m\cdot\sum_{o}R(o)\;=\;\sum_{o}R(o)\,\log R(o)\;+\;\log m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{o}R(o)\,\log R(o)\;+\;\log m\cdot\sum_{o}R(o)\;=\;\sum_{o}R(o)\,\log R(o)\;+\;\log m</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A8.Ex184"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex184.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\,H(R)\;+\;\log m." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\,H(R)\;+\;\log m.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Rearranging gives the identity</span></p>
<table id="A8.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H(R)\;-\;\log m\;=\;-\KL(R\|U)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.058em">=</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(R)\;-\;\log m\;=\;-\KL(R\|U).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS1.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore</span></p>
<table id="A8.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A8.Ex185"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex185.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle H(R)\;-\;\log m\;-\;\KL(U\|R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H(R)\;-\;\log m\;-\;\KL(U\|R)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex185.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\;\big(-\KL(R\|U)\big)\;-\;\KL(U\|R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\;\big(-\KL(R\|U)\big)\;-\;\KL(U\|R)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A8.Ex186"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex186.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\;-\Big(\KL(R\|U)\;+\;\KL(U\|R)\Big)\ \leq\ 0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.058em">=</mo><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>U</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn> 0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\;-\Big(\KL(R\|U)\;+\;\KL(U\|R)\Big)\ \leq\ 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS1.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS1.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">since each Kullback–Leibler divergence is nonnegative. Moreover, equality holds iff <math id="A8.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\KL(R\|U)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(R\|U)=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A8.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\KL(U\|R)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(U\|R)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, which happens iff <math id="A8.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=U</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, we have provided an example of a distribution for which a strictly unanimous compositional group may not be formed. Can this result be extended to non-trivial distributions? We now show that there exists a set of non-uniform distributions such that they can in no way form a unanimously compositional group, regardless of which (non-trivial, i.e., bounded away from <math id="A8.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>) weights are assigned. In other words, certain agents or beliefs are fundamentally incompatible, and weights cannot in general make an arbitrary family unanimously compositional.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem58" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem58.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 58</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem58.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(No universal weights for unanimity)<span id="Thmtheorem58.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem58.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem58.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem58.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="Thmtheorem58.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. There exist <math id="Thmtheorem58.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> strictly positive and non-uniform distributions <math id="Thmtheorem58.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1},\dots,P_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1},\dots,P_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="Thmtheorem58.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}=\{1,\dots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}=\{1,\dots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math> such that, for <em id="Thmtheorem58.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">every</em> choice of positive weights <math id="Thmtheorem58.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}\geq\tau&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}\geq\tau&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmtheorem58.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> arbitrarily small and <math id="Thmtheorem58.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, the log-pool <math id="Thmtheorem58.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> fails to make all agents strictly better off; i.e., at least one index <math id="Thmtheorem58.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> has <math id="Thmtheorem58.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{P_{i}}(P)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{P_{i}}(P)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A8.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">For a parameter <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in(0,\tfrac{1}{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in(0,\tfrac{1}{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, define for each <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,\dots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,\dots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math> the distribution <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}^{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>ε</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}^{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex187" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex187.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="P_{i}^{\varepsilon}(i)=1-\varepsilon,\qquad P_{i}^{\varepsilon}(k)=\frac{\varepsilon}{n-1}\quad(k\neq i)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>ε</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>ε</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}^{\varepsilon}(i)=1-\varepsilon,\qquad P_{i}^{\varepsilon}(k)=\frac{\varepsilon}{n-1}\quad(k\neq i).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">These <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}^{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>ε</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}^{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> are strictly positive and “peak” on outcome <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. For any positive weights <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1},\dots,\beta_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1},\dots,\beta_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}\beta_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}\beta_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, the (unnormalized) pooled mass at outcome <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex188" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex188.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{P}^{\varepsilon}(k)=\prod_{i=1}^{n}\big(P_{i}^{\varepsilon}(k)\big)^{\beta_{i}}=\big(1-\varepsilon\big)^{\beta_{k}}\Big(\frac{\varepsilon}{n-1}\Big)^{\sum_{i\neq k}\beta_{i}}=\big(1-\varepsilon\big)^{\beta_{k}}\Big(\frac{\varepsilon}{n-1}\Big)^{1-\beta_{k}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>ε</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mstyle><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{P}^{\varepsilon}(k)=\prod_{i=1}^{n}\big(P_{i}^{\varepsilon}(k)\big)^{\beta_{i}}=\big(1-\varepsilon\big)^{\beta_{k}}\Big(\frac{\varepsilon}{n-1}\Big)^{\sum_{i\neq k}\beta_{i}}=\big(1-\varepsilon\big)^{\beta_{k}}\Big(\frac{\varepsilon}{n-1}\Big)^{1-\beta_{k}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Let</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex189" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex189.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{\varepsilon}:=\sum_{r=1}^{n}\widetilde{P}^{\varepsilon}(r)=\sum_{r=1}^{n}\big(1-\varepsilon\big)^{\beta_{r}}\Big(\frac{\varepsilon}{n-1}\Big)^{1-\beta_{r}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{\varepsilon}:=\sum_{r=1}^{n}\widetilde{P}^{\varepsilon}(r)=\sum_{r=1}^{n}\big(1-\varepsilon\big)^{\beta_{r}}\Big(\frac{\varepsilon}{n-1}\Big)^{1-\beta_{r}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">Then the pooled distribution is <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\varepsilon}(k)=\widetilde{P}^{\varepsilon}(k)/Z^{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\varepsilon}(k)=\widetilde{P}^{\varepsilon}(k)/Z^{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex190" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex190.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\varepsilon}(\beta)\ :=\ \sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\,\Delta_{P_{i}^{\varepsilon}}\!\big(P^{\varepsilon}\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.611em">:=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>ε</mi></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\varepsilon}(\beta)\ :=\ \sum_{i=1}^{n}\beta_{i}\,\Delta_{P_{i}^{\varepsilon}}\!\big(P^{\varepsilon}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS1.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS1.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">Using <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{R}(P)=\E_{P}[\log R]-\E_{R}[\log R]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{R}(P)=\E_{P}[\log R]-\E_{R}[\log R]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log P^{\varepsilon}=\sum_{i}\beta_{i}\log P_{i}^{\varepsilon}-\log Z^{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>ε</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log P^{\varepsilon}=\sum_{i}\beta_{i}\log P_{i}^{\varepsilon}-\log Z^{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A8.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A8.Ex191"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex191.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S^{\varepsilon}(\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S^{\varepsilon}(\beta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex191.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i}\beta_{i}\E_{P^{\varepsilon}}[\log P_{i}^{\varepsilon}]\;-\;\sum_{i}\beta_{i}\E_{P_{i}^{\varepsilon}}[\log P_{i}^{\varepsilon}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>ε</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>ε</mi></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>ε</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i}\beta_{i}\E_{P^{\varepsilon}}[\log P_{i}^{\varepsilon}]\;-\;\sum_{i}\beta_{i}\E_{P_{i}^{\varepsilon}}[\log P_{i}^{\varepsilon}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A8.Ex192"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex192.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\E_{P^{\varepsilon}}\!\Big[\sum_{i}\beta_{i}\log P_{i}^{\varepsilon}\Big]\;+\;\sum_{i}\beta_{i}H\!\big(P_{i}^{\varepsilon}\big)\quad(\text{since }\E_{P_{i}^{\varepsilon}}[\log P_{i}^{\varepsilon}]=-H(P_{i}^{\varepsilon}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>ε</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mpadded style="width:0.742em;" width="0.742em"><mi>H</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>ε</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>since </mtext><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>ε</mi></msubsup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>log</mi><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>ε</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>ε</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\E_{P^{\varepsilon}}\!\Big[\sum_{i}\beta_{i}\log P_{i}^{\varepsilon}\Big]\;+\;\sum_{i}\beta_{i}H\!\big(P_{i}^{\varepsilon}\big)\quad(\text{since }\E_{P_{i}^{\varepsilon}}[\log P_{i}^{\varepsilon}]=-H(P_{i}^{\varepsilon}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A8.Ex193"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex193.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\E_{P^{\varepsilon}}[\log P^{\varepsilon}+\log Z^{\varepsilon}]\;+\;\sum_{i}\beta_{i}H\!\big(P_{i}^{\varepsilon}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.742em;" width="0.742em"><mi>H</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>ε</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\E_{P^{\varepsilon}}[\log P^{\varepsilon}+\log Z^{\varepsilon}]\;+\;\sum_{i}\beta_{i}H\!\big(P_{i}^{\varepsilon}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A8.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&lt;-H\!\big(P^{\varepsilon}\big)\;+\;\log Z^{\varepsilon}\;+\;\sum_{i}H\!\big(P_{i}^{\varepsilon}\big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.742em;" width="0.742em"><mi>H</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.742em;" width="0.742em"><mi>H</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>ε</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&lt;-H\!\big(P^{\varepsilon}\big)\;+\;\log Z^{\varepsilon}\;+\;\sum_{i}H\!\big(P_{i}^{\varepsilon}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS1.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS1.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, if we show <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\varepsilon}(\beta)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\varepsilon}(\beta)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, then at least one <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{P_{i}^{\varepsilon}}(P^{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>ε</mi></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{P_{i}^{\varepsilon}}(P^{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> is negative (since the <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are positive). Let <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\star}:=\max_{1\leq r\leq n}\beta_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\star}:=\max_{1\leq r\leq n}\beta_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K:=\{r:\beta_{r}=\beta_{\star}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K:=\{r:\beta_{r}=\beta_{\star}\}</annotation></semantics></math> (nonempty). Then</span></p>
<table id="A8.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A8.Ex194"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex194.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Z^{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Z</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Z^{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex194.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{r=1}^{n}\big(1-\varepsilon\big)^{\beta_{r}}\Big(\frac{\varepsilon}{n-1}\Big)^{1-\beta_{r}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{r=1}^{n}\big(1-\varepsilon\big)^{\beta_{r}}\Big(\frac{\varepsilon}{n-1}\Big)^{1-\beta_{r}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A8.Ex195"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex195.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Big(\frac{\varepsilon}{n-1}\Big)^{1-\beta_{\star}}\big(1-\varepsilon\big)^{\beta_{\star}}\sum_{r=1}^{n}\Big(\frac{\varepsilon}{n-1}\Big)^{\beta_{\star}-\beta_{r}}\big(1-\varepsilon\big)^{\beta_{r}-\beta_{\star}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Big(\frac{\varepsilon}{n-1}\Big)^{1-\beta_{\star}}\big(1-\varepsilon\big)^{\beta_{\star}}\sum_{r=1}^{n}\Big(\frac{\varepsilon}{n-1}\Big)^{\beta_{\star}-\beta_{r}}\big(1-\varepsilon\big)^{\beta_{r}-\beta_{\star}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS1.p4.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS1.p4.7.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\notin K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\notin K</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\star}-\beta_{r}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\star}-\beta_{r}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, hence
<math id="A8.SS1.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Big(\tfrac{\varepsilon}{n-1}\Big)^{\beta_{\star}-\beta_{r}}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Big(\tfrac{\varepsilon}{n-1}\Big)^{\beta_{\star}-\beta_{r}}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\to 0^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\to 0^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>; for <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in K</annotation></semantics></math>, that factor equals <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex196" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex196.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log Z^{\varepsilon}=(1-\beta_{\star})\log\!\Big(\frac{\varepsilon}{n-1}\Big)+\beta_{\star}\log(1-\varepsilon)+\log\!\Big(|K|+o(1)\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log Z^{\varepsilon}=(1-\beta_{\star})\log\!\Big(\frac{\varepsilon}{n-1}\Big)+\beta_{\star}\log(1-\varepsilon)+\log\!\Big(|K|+o(1)\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS1.p4.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS1.p4.8.1" class="ltx_text">In particular, there exists a constant <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> (depending only on <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>) such that for all sufficiently small <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A8.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log Z^{\varepsilon}\ \leq\ (1-\beta_{\star})\,\log\varepsilon+C_{1},\qquad\text{with }(1-\beta_{\star})&gt;0\text{ since }n\geq 2." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>with </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> since </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log Z^{\varepsilon}\ \leq\ (1-\beta_{\star})\,\log\varepsilon+C_{1},\qquad\text{with }(1-\beta_{\star})&gt;0\text{ since }n\geq 2.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS1.p4.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS1.p4.9.1" class="ltx_text">Now for each <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A8.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A8.Ex197"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex197.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle H\!\big(P_{i}^{\varepsilon}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.742em;" width="0.742em"><mi>H</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>ε</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H\!\big(P_{i}^{\varepsilon}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex197.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-(1-\varepsilon)\log(1-\varepsilon)-\sum_{k\neq i}\frac{\varepsilon}{n-1}\,\log\!\Big(\frac{\varepsilon}{n-1}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-(1-\varepsilon)\log(1-\varepsilon)-\sum_{k\neq i}\frac{\varepsilon}{n-1}\,\log\!\Big(\frac{\varepsilon}{n-1}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A8.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-(1-\varepsilon)\log(1-\varepsilon)-\varepsilon\log\varepsilon+\varepsilon\log(n-1)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-(1-\varepsilon)\log(1-\varepsilon)-\varepsilon\log\varepsilon+\varepsilon\log(n-1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS1.p4.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS1.p4.10.1" class="ltx_text">Hence there exists <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> (independent of <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>) with</span></p>
<table id="A8.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{n}H\!\big(P_{i}^{\varepsilon}\big)=n\Big(-(1-\varepsilon)\log(1-\varepsilon)-\varepsilon\log\varepsilon+\varepsilon\log(n-1)\Big)\ \leq\ C_{2}\,\varepsilon\big(1-\log\varepsilon\big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.742em;" width="0.742em"><mi>H</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>ε</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{n}H\!\big(P_{i}^{\varepsilon}\big)=n\Big(-(1-\varepsilon)\log(1-\varepsilon)-\varepsilon\log\varepsilon+\varepsilon\log(n-1)\Big)\ \leq\ C_{2}\,\varepsilon\big(1-\log\varepsilon\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS1.p4.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS1.p4.11.1" class="ltx_text">for all sufficiently small <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> (using <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\log(1-\varepsilon)\leq 2\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\log(1-\varepsilon)\leq 2\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in(0,\tfrac{1}{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in(0,\tfrac{1}{2})</annotation></semantics></math>). Recall that <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq H(P^{\varepsilon})\leq\log n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq H(P^{\varepsilon})\leq\log n</annotation></semantics></math>, which gives</span></p>
<table id="A8.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\,H\!\big(P^{\varepsilon}\big)\ \leq\ 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.742em;" width="0.742em"><mi>H</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\,H\!\big(P^{\varepsilon}\big)\ \leq\ 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS1.p4.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS1.p4.12.1" class="ltx_text">Combine (<a href="#A8.E23" title="In Proof. ‣ H.1 On Joining Random Distributions ‣ Appendix H Properties of Strict Local (Small-Tilt) Unanimity ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>), (<a href="#A8.E24" title="In Proof. ‣ H.1 On Joining Random Distributions ‣ Appendix H Properties of Strict Local (Small-Tilt) Unanimity ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>), (<a href="#A8.E26" title="In Proof. ‣ H.1 On Joining Random Distributions ‣ Appendix H Properties of Strict Local (Small-Tilt) Unanimity ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>), and (<a href="#A8.E27" title="In Proof. ‣ H.1 On Joining Random Distributions ‣ Appendix H Properties of Strict Local (Small-Tilt) Unanimity ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>):</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex198" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex198.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\varepsilon}(\beta)\ \leq\ 0\;+\;(1-\beta_{\star})\log\varepsilon+C_{1}\;+\;C_{2}\,\varepsilon\big(1-\log\varepsilon\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn> 0</mn><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\varepsilon}(\beta)\ \leq\ 0\;+\;(1-\beta_{\star})\log\varepsilon+C_{1}\;+\;C_{2}\,\varepsilon\big(1-\log\varepsilon\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS1.p4.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS1.p4.13.1" class="ltx_text">As <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\to 0^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\to 0^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, the term <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\beta_{\star})\log\varepsilon\to-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\beta_{\star})\log\varepsilon\to-\infty</annotation></semantics></math> (since <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\beta_{\star}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\beta_{\star}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\varepsilon\to-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\varepsilon\to-\infty</annotation></semantics></math>), whereas <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is constant and <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon(1-\log\varepsilon)\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon(1-\log\varepsilon)\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\varepsilon}(\beta)\to-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\varepsilon}(\beta)\to-\infty</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\to 0^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\to 0^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, there exists <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{0}=\varepsilon_{0}(\beta,n)\in(0,\tfrac{1}{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{0}=\varepsilon_{0}(\beta,n)\in(0,\tfrac{1}{2})</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in(0,\varepsilon_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in(0,\varepsilon_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A8.SS1.p4.m44" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\varepsilon}(\beta)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\varepsilon}(\beta)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, since each <math id="A8.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A8.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\varepsilon}(\beta)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\varepsilon}(\beta)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> implies not all <math id="A8.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{P_{i}^{\varepsilon}}(P^{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>ε</mi></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{P_{i}^{\varepsilon}}(P^{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> can be strictly positive. Hence for every choice of positive weights <math id="A8.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, unanimity fails for the family <math id="A8.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{P_{i}^{\varepsilon}\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>ε</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{P_{i}^{\varepsilon}\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> once <math id="A8.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently small.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem59" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem59.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 59</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem59.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem59.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem59.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem59.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Even for <math id="Thmtheorem59.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{O}|\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{O}|\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>, given arbitrary agents <math id="Thmtheorem59.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1},\dots,P_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1},\dots,P_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, there need not exist positive weights <math id="Thmtheorem59.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> making the group unanimously compositional under epistemic utilities. In particular, the family <math id="Thmtheorem59.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{P_{i}^{\varepsilon}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>ε</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{P_{i}^{\varepsilon}\}</annotation></semantics></math> from Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem58" title="Theorem 58 (No universal weights for unanimity). ‣ H.1 On Joining Random Distributions ‣ Appendix H Properties of Strict Local (Small-Tilt) Unanimity ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">58</span></a> is a counterexample for every choice of positive <math id="Thmtheorem59.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> (for all sufficiently small <math id="Thmtheorem59.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem60" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem60.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 60</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem60.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem60.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem60.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem60.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The proof employs a <math id="Thmtheorem60.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-weighted sum <math id="Thmtheorem60.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\varepsilon}(\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\varepsilon}(\beta)</annotation></semantics></math>, showing it becomes negative when the agents are highly peaked on disjoint outcomes, thereby avoiding a case-by-case analysis of individual <math id="Thmtheorem60.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{P_{i}}(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{P_{i}}(P)</annotation></semantics></math> and establishing the result for all weight vectors simultaneously. While trivial obstructions exist–if all <math id="Thmtheorem60.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are identical, then <math id="Thmtheorem60.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P=P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P=P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="Thmtheorem60.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem60.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{P_{i}}(P)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{P_{i}}(P)=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmtheorem60.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, making strict unanimity impossible–Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem58" title="Theorem 58 (No universal weights for unanimity). ‣ H.1 On Joining Random Distributions ‣ Appendix H Properties of Strict Local (Small-Tilt) Unanimity ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">58</span></a> provides a nontrivial obstruction in which the <math id="Thmtheorem60.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are distinct and strictly positive. Moreover, we have previously shown in Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem33" title="Theorem 33 (Binary-outcome impossibility under log-welfare). ‣ E.1 Impossibility in the Binary Case ‣ Appendix E Possible and Impossible Compositions ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a> that for <math id="Thmtheorem60.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{O}|=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{O}|=2</annotation></semantics></math>, a stronger impossibility holds: for any two distinct agents and any positive <math id="Thmtheorem60.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, at least one agent satisfies <math id="Thmtheorem60.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{P_{i}}(P)\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{P_{i}}(P)\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Our construction further shows that even when <math id="Thmtheorem60.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{O}|=n\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{O}|=n\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math> and there are <math id="Thmtheorem60.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> agents, unanimity can fail for all choices of positive weights.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">H.2 </span>Openness of Strictly Unanimously Decomposable Pools</h3>

<div id="Thmtheorem61" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem61.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 61</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem61.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Strict unanimous decomposability)<span id="Thmtheorem61.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem61.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem61.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem61.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A distribution <math id="Thmtheorem61.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="Thmtheorem61.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">strictly unanimously decomposable</em> (under epistemic utilities) if there exist an integer <math id="Thmtheorem61.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, positive weights <math id="Thmtheorem61.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1},\dots,\beta_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1},\dots,\beta_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmtheorem61.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}\beta_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}\beta_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, and strictly positive agents <math id="Thmtheorem61.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1},\dots,P_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1},\dots,P_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex199" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex199.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\ \propto\ \prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}^{\beta_{i}}\qquad\text{and}\qquad\Delta_{P_{i}}(P)\ :=\ \E_{P}[\log P_{i}]-\E_{P_{i}}[\log P_{i}]\ &gt;\ 0\quad\forall i." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.611em">∝</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\ \propto\ \prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}^{\beta_{i}}\qquad\text{and}\qquad\Delta_{P_{i}}(P)\ :=\ \E_{P}[\log P_{i}]-\E_{P_{i}}[\log P_{i}]\ &gt;\ 0\quad\forall i.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem61.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem61.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We denote by <math id="Thmtheorem61.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{\rm strict}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>strict</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{\rm strict}</annotation></semantics></math> the set of all such <math id="Thmtheorem61.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> in the simplex.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We will show that the compositional property forms an open set in the simplex topology.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem62" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem62.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 62</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem62.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Openness)<span id="Thmtheorem62.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem62.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem62.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem62.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="Thmtheorem62.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\in\mathcal{U}_{\rm strict}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>strict</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\in\mathcal{U}_{\rm strict}</annotation></semantics></math>, then there exists an open neighborhood <math id="Thmtheorem62.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="Thmtheorem62.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> such that every <math id="Thmtheorem62.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}\in\mathcal{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}\in\mathcal{N}</annotation></semantics></math> also belongs to <math id="Thmtheorem62.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{\rm strict}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>strict</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{\rm strict}</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, <math id="Thmtheorem62.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{\rm strict}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>strict</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{\rm strict}</annotation></semantics></math> is an open set in the simplex topology.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The proof uses two elementary ingredients: a transport that preserves log-pooling and a continuity argument in total variation.</p>
</div>
<section id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Total variation (TV) distance.</h5>

<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For distributions <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu,\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu,\nu</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> we set</p>
<table id="A8.Ex200" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex200.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mu-\nu\|_{\mathrm{TV}}\ :=\ \frac{1}{2}\sum_{o\in\mathcal{O}}|\mu(o)-\nu(o)|\ =\ \frac{1}{2}\|\mu-\nu\|_{1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mu-\nu\|_{\mathrm{TV}}\ :=\ \frac{1}{2}\sum_{o\in\mathcal{O}}|\mu(o)-\nu(o)|\ =\ \frac{1}{2}\|\mu-\nu\|_{1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Convergence in TV is equivalent to coordinatewise convergence in this finite setting.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem63" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem63.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 63</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem63.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Pool-preserving transport around a base <math id="Thmtheorem63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="Thmtheorem63.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem63.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem63.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem63.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix a strictly positive base pool <math id="Thmtheorem63.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and a witnessing decomposition <math id="Thmtheorem63.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\propto\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}^{\beta_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∝</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\propto\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}^{\beta_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmtheorem63.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem63.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}\beta_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}\beta_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. For any strictly positive target <math id="Thmtheorem63.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>, define</span></p>
<table id="A8.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{R\mid P}(P_{i})(o)\ :=\ \frac{P_{i}(o)\,\frac{R(o)}{P(o)}}{\sum_{x\in\mathcal{O}}P_{i}(x)\,\frac{R(x)}{P(x)}}\qquad(o\in\mathcal{O})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{R\mid P}(P_{i})(o)\ :=\ \frac{P_{i}(o)\,\frac{R(o)}{P(o)}}{\sum_{x\in\mathcal{O}}P_{i}(x)\,\frac{R(x)}{P(x)}}\qquad(o\in\mathcal{O}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem63.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem63.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, writing <math id="Thmtheorem63.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}^{\prime}:=\mathcal{S}_{R\mid P}(P_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}^{\prime}:=\mathcal{S}_{R\mid P}(P_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex201" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex201.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{i=1}^{n}\big(P_{i}^{\prime}\big)^{\beta_{i}}\ \propto\ R\quad\text{(with the same weights $\beta$)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">∝</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">(with the same weights </mtext><mi>β</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">)</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{i=1}^{n}\big(P_{i}^{\prime}\big)^{\beta_{i}}\ \propto\ R\quad\text{(with the same weights $\beta$)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem63.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem63.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and each <math id="Thmtheorem63.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly positive. Moreover, the map <math id="Thmtheorem63.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\mapsto P_{i}^{\prime}=\mathcal{S}_{R\mid P}(P_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\mapsto P_{i}^{\prime}=\mathcal{S}_{R\mid P}(P_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous in total variation.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{i}(R):=\sum_{x}P_{i}(x)\,\frac{R(x)}{P(x)}\in(0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{i}(R):=\sum_{x}P_{i}(x)\,\frac{R(x)}{P(x)}\in(0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex202" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex202.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(P_{i}^{\prime}(o)\big)^{\beta_{i}}=\frac{P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}}\,\big(\tfrac{R(o)}{P(o)}\big)^{\beta_{i}}}{D_{i}(R)^{\beta_{i}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(P_{i}^{\prime}(o)\big)^{\beta_{i}}=\frac{P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}}\,\big(\tfrac{R(o)}{P(o)}\big)^{\beta_{i}}}{D_{i}(R)^{\beta_{i}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Multiplying over <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\dots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\dots,n</annotation></semantics></math> and using <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}\beta_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}\beta_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex203" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A8.Ex203X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex203X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\prod_{i=1}^{n}\big(P_{i}^{\prime}(o)\big)^{\beta_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\prod_{i=1}^{n}\big(P_{i}^{\prime}(o)\big)^{\beta_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex203X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Big(\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}}\Big)\cdot\Big(\frac{R(o)}{P(o)}\Big)^{\sum_{i}\beta_{i}}\cdot\Big(\prod_{i=1}^{n}D_{i}(R)^{-\beta_{i}}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub></mstyle><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Big(\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}}\Big)\cdot\Big(\frac{R(o)}{P(o)}\Big)^{\sum_{i}\beta_{i}}\cdot\Big(\prod_{i=1}^{n}D_{i}(R)^{-\beta_{i}}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A8.Ex203Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex203Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\propto\ \Big(\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}}\Big)\cdot\frac{R(o)}{P(o)}\ \propto\ P(o)\cdot\frac{R(o)}{P(o)}\ =\ R(o)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.778em">∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\propto\ \Big(\prod_{i=1}^{n}P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}}\Big)\cdot\frac{R(o)}{P(o)}\ \propto\ P(o)\cdot\frac{R(o)}{P(o)}\ =\ R(o).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus the pooled distribution is <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>. Now, fix <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and define for target <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> the (unnormalized) map</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex204" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex204.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{P}_{i}^{\,R}(o)\ :=\ P_{i}(o)\,\frac{R(o)}{P(o)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{P}_{i}^{\,R}(o)\ :=\ P_{i}(o)\,\frac{R(o)}{P(o)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Then
<math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}^{\prime}=\widetilde{P}_{i}^{\,R}/\|\widetilde{P}_{i}^{\,R}\|_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}^{\prime}=\widetilde{P}_{i}^{\,R}/\|\widetilde{P}_{i}^{\,R}\|_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>
since <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{o}\widetilde{P}_{i}^{\,R}(o)=D_{i}(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>o</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{o}\widetilde{P}_{i}^{\,R}(o)=D_{i}(R)</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{(n)}\to R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{(n)}\to R</annotation></semantics></math> in TV, then <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{P}_{i}^{\,R^{(n)}}\to\widetilde{P}_{i}^{\,R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mi>R</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{P}_{i}^{\,R^{(n)}}\to\widetilde{P}_{i}^{\,R}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> because <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}/P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}/P</annotation></semantics></math> is a fixed bounded positive vector and multiplication is continuous coordinatewise. Also <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{i}(R^{(n)})=\|\widetilde{P}_{i}^{\,R^{(n)}}\|_{1}\to\|\widetilde{P}_{i}^{\,R}\|_{1}=D_{i}(R)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{i}(R^{(n)})=\|\widetilde{P}_{i}^{\,R^{(n)}}\|_{1}\to\|\widetilde{P}_{i}^{\,R}\|_{1}=D_{i}(R)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>; hence normalization is continuous. Therefore <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}^{\prime\,(n)}\to P_{i}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}^{\prime\,(n)}\to P_{i}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> in TV.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem64" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem64.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 64</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem64.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Continuity of the welfare map)<span id="Thmtheorem64.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem64.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem64.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem64.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">On the strictly positive simplex, the map</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex205" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex205.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Phi:(R,P)\ \longmapsto\ \Delta_{R}(P)\ =\ H(R)-H(P)-\KL(P\|R)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em" stretchy="false">⟼</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi:(R,P)\ \longmapsto\ \Delta_{R}(P)\ =\ H(R)-H(P)-\KL(P\|R)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem64.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem64.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">is jointly continuous in total variation.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Write out the three terms explicitly:</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex206" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex206.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H(R)=-\sum_{o}R(o)\log R(o),\quad H(P)=-\sum_{o}P(o)\log P(o),\quad\KL(P\|R)=\sum_{o}P(o)\,\big(\log P(o)-\log R(o)\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></munder><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></munder><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></munder><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(R)=-\sum_{o}R(o)\log R(o),\quad H(P)=-\sum_{o}P(o)\log P(o),\quad\KL(P\|R)=\sum_{o}P(o)\,\big(\log P(o)-\log R(o)\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">On <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,1)\times(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,1)\times(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> the functions <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)\mapsto x\log x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)\mapsto x\log x</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\mapsto x\log x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\mapsto x\log x</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)\mapsto x\log(x/y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)\mapsto x\log(x/y)</annotation></semantics></math> are continuous. Finite sums of continuous functions are continuous; TV convergence implies coordinatewise convergence; hence <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We can now prove the openness statement.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem62" title="Theorem 62 (Openness). ‣ H.2 Openness of Strictly Unanimously Decomposable Pools ‣ Appendix H Properties of Strict Local (Small-Tilt) Unanimity ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">62</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\in\mathcal{U}_{\rm strict}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>strict</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\in\mathcal{U}_{\rm strict}</annotation></semantics></math> with a witnessing decomposition <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\propto\prod_{i}P_{i}^{\beta_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∝</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\propto\prod_{i}P_{i}^{\beta_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> and strict gains <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{P_{i}}(P)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{P_{i}}(P)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. Set</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex207" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex207.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\ :=\ \min_{1\leq i\leq n}\Delta_{P_{i}}(P)\ &gt;\ 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\ :=\ \min_{1\leq i\leq n}\Delta_{P_{i}}(P)\ &gt;\ 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">For any strictly positive <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>, define <em id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">transported</em> agents</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex208" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex208.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}^{\prime}\ :=\ \mathcal{S}_{P^{\prime}\mid P}(P_{i})\quad\text{(as in \eqref{eq:S-transport})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>(as in (</mtext><mtext><a href="#A8.E28" title="In Lemma 63 (Pool-preserving transport around a base 𝑃). ‣ Total variation (TV) distance. ‣ H.2 Openness of Strictly Unanimously Decomposable Pools ‣ Appendix H Properties of Strict Local (Small-Tilt) Unanimity ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a></mtext><mtext>))</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}^{\prime}\ :=\ \mathcal{S}_{P^{\prime}\mid P}(P_{i})\quad\text{(as in \eqref{eq:S-transport})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem63" title="Lemma 63 (Pool-preserving transport around a base 𝑃). ‣ Total variation (TV) distance. ‣ H.2 Openness of Strictly Unanimously Decomposable Pools ‣ Appendix H Properties of Strict Local (Small-Tilt) Unanimity ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">63</span></a>, <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{i}(P_{i}^{\prime})^{\beta_{i}}\propto P^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo>∝</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{i}(P_{i}^{\prime})^{\beta_{i}}\propto P^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> (same weights), and the map <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}\mapsto P_{i}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}\mapsto P_{i}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is TV-continuous. Consider the functions</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex209" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex209.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{i}(P^{\prime})\ :=\ \Delta_{P_{i}^{\prime}}(P^{\prime})\ =\ \Phi\big(P_{i}^{\prime},\,P^{\prime}\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{i}(P^{\prime})\ :=\ \Delta_{P_{i}^{\prime}}(P^{\prime})\ =\ \Phi\big(P_{i}^{\prime},\,P^{\prime}\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> is from Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem64" title="Lemma 64 (Continuity of the welfare map). ‣ Total variation (TV) distance. ‣ H.2 Openness of Strictly Unanimously Decomposable Pools ‣ Appendix H Properties of Strict Local (Small-Tilt) Unanimity ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">64</span></a>. The composition of continuous maps is continuous; hence each <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous at <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}=P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}=P</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, for <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}=P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}=P</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}^{\prime}=\mathcal{S}_{P\mid P}(P_{i})=P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}^{\prime}=\mathcal{S}_{P\mid P}(P_{i})=P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, so</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex210" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex210.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{i}(P)\ =\ \Delta_{P_{i}}(P)\ \geq\ \gamma\ &gt;\ 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.778em">&gt;</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{i}(P)\ =\ \Delta_{P_{i}}(P)\ \geq\ \gamma\ &gt;\ 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text">By continuity, for each <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> there exists a TV-neighborhood <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{i}(P^{\prime})&gt;\gamma/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{i}(P^{\prime})&gt;\gamma/2</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}\in\mathcal{N}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}\in\mathcal{N}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let
<math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}:=\bigcap_{i=1}^{n}\mathcal{N}_{i}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>⋂</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}:=\bigcap_{i=1}^{n}\mathcal{N}_{i},</annotation></semantics></math>
which is again an open neighborhood of <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>. Then for every <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}\in\mathcal{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}\in\mathcal{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, the transported agents <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}^{\prime},\dots,P_{n}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}^{\prime},\dots,P_{n}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> (with the same weights <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>) pool to <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and satisfy
<math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{P_{i}^{\prime}}(P^{\prime})=F_{i}(P^{\prime})&gt;\gamma/2&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{P_{i}^{\prime}}(P^{\prime})=F_{i}(P^{\prime})&gt;\gamma/2&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>
for all <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}\in\mathcal{U}_{\rm strict}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>strict</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}\in\mathcal{U}_{\rm strict}</annotation></semantics></math>, proving openness.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem65" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem65.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 65</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem65.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem65.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem65.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem65.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="Thmtheorem65.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{O}|=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{O}|=2</annotation></semantics></math>, strict unanimity is impossible for any decomposition (see the binary impossibility argument). Thus <math id="Thmtheorem65.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{\rm strict}=\varnothing" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>strict</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{\rm strict}=\varnothing</annotation></semantics></math> on the binary simplex, and the theorem holds vacuously (the empty set is open).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem66" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem66.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 66</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem66.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem66.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem66.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem66.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If some outcomes are allotted zero probability, all continuity/KL arguments still go through upon restricting to a fixed common support <math id="Thmtheorem66.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subseteq\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subseteq\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> on which all distributions are strictly positive, and treating the simplex on <math id="Thmtheorem66.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>. The transport (<a href="#A8.E28" title="In Lemma 63 (Pool-preserving transport around a base 𝑃). ‣ Total variation (TV) distance. ‣ H.2 Openness of Strictly Unanimously Decomposable Pools ‣ Appendix H Properties of Strict Local (Small-Tilt) Unanimity ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>) preserves support and continuity on the restricted simplex.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A9" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix I </span>Modeling the Waluigi Effect</h2>

<section id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Informal background.</h5>

<div id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <em id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Waluigi Effect</em> is the empirical phenomenon that, after training an LLM to satisfy a desirable property <math id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>
(e.g. helpfulness), it can become <em id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">easier</em> to elicit responses with the opposite property <math id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-P</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g. hostility) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>, <a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>, <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>]</cite>,
often via prompt steering or role-play <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib72" title="" class="ltx_ref">72</a>, <a href="#bib.bib73" title="" class="ltx_ref">73</a>, <a href="#bib.bib74" title="" class="ltx_ref">74</a>]</cite>. We now formalize a mechanism for this effect using our compositional model.</p>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In the preceding sections, we considered the <em id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">decomposition</em> or flexible <em id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">factorization</em> of a parent agent <math id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> into child subagents <math id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. We now reverse this perspective. Suppose we have an established <em id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">witnessing set</em> of distributions <math id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1},\dots,P_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1},\dots,P_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> that combine to yield <math id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>. These witnesses may be viewed as distinct subagents, or personas, that emerged during training. In what follows, we work directly at the witness level, examining how these component distributions change when constraints are imposed on the parent distribution <math id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A9.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">I.1 </span>Defining Centered Logarithmic Character Profiles</h3>

<div id="A9.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To preserve the intuition of logarithmic probabilities, we now write the epistemic utilities as <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(o):=\log P(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(o):=\log P(o)</annotation></semantics></math> for the parent agent and <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{i}(o):=\log P_{i}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{i}(o):=\log P_{i}(o)</annotation></semantics></math> for the child subagents or witnesses. Then, we may define the <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>-centered <em id="A9.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">log profile</em> of agent <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> by</p>
<table id="A9.Ex211" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex211.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}(o)\ :=\ l_{i}(o)\ -\ \E_{P}[\,l_{i}\,]\qquad(o\in\mathcal{O})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}(o)\ :=\ l_{i}(o)\ -\ \E_{P}[\,l_{i}\,]\qquad(o\in\mathcal{O}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">so that <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E_{P}[v_{i}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E_{P}[v_{i}]=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. We equip functions on <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> with the inner product
<math id="A9.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle f,g\rangle_{P}:=\sum_{o}P(o)f(o)g(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>o</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle f,g\rangle_{P}:=\sum_{o}P(o)f(o)g(o)</annotation></semantics></math> and the induced seminorm <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f\|_{P}:=\sqrt{\langle f,f\rangle_{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msqrt><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f\|_{P}:=\sqrt{\langle f,f\rangle_{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Proposition <a href="#Thmtheorem67" title="Proposition 67 (∥⋅∥_𝑃 is a norm). ‣ I.1 Defining Centered Logarithmic Character Profiles ‣ Appendix I Modeling the Waluigi Effect ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">67</span></a> formally confirms that this defines a norm:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem67" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem67.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 67</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem67.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<math id="Thmtheorem67.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{P}</annotation></semantics></math> is a norm)<span id="Thmtheorem67.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem67.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem67.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem67.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="Thmtheorem67.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(o)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(o)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmtheorem67.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\in\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\in\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> (strict positivity), then <math id="Thmtheorem67.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle_{P}</annotation></semantics></math> is an inner product on the real vector space <math id="Thmtheorem67.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{\mathcal{O}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{\mathcal{O}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmtheorem67.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{P}</annotation></semantics></math> is a norm. In particular:</span></p>
<ol id="A9.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A9.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A9.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Symmetry) </span><math id="A9.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle f,g\rangle_{P}=\langle g,f\rangle_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle f,g\rangle_{P}=\langle g,f\rangle_{P}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A9.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A9.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A9.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Bilinearity) </span><math id="A9.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle af+bh,\,g\rangle_{P}=a\langle f,g\rangle_{P}+b\langle h,g\rangle_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle af+bh,\,g\rangle_{P}=a\langle f,g\rangle_{P}+b\langle h,g\rangle_{P}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A9.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and similarly in the second slot.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A9.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A9.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Positive definiteness) </span><math id="A9.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle f,f\rangle_{P}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle f,f\rangle_{P}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A9.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for all </span><math id="A9.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A9.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A9.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A9.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Norm axioms) </span><math id="A9.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f\|_{P}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f\|_{P}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A9.I1.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> with equality iff </span><math id="A9.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A9.I1.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">; </span><math id="A9.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\alpha f\|_{P}=|\alpha|\,\|f\|_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\alpha f\|_{P}=|\alpha|\,\|f\|_{P}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A9.I1.i4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">; and the triangle inequality </span><math id="A9.I1.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f+g\|_{P}\leq\|f\|_{P}+\|g\|_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f+g\|_{P}\leq\|f\|_{P}+\|g\|_{P}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A9.I1.i4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> holds.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A9.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Symmetry and bilinearity are immediate from the finite sum definition. For positive definiteness, if <math id="A9.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> there exists <math id="A9.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A9.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(o^{\star})\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(o^{\star})\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, and since <math id="A9.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(o^{\star})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(o^{\star})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="A9.Ex212" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex212.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle f,f\rangle_{P}=\sum_{o}P(o)f(o)^{2}\ \geq\ P(o^{\star})f(o^{\star})^{2}\ &gt;\ 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle f,f\rangle_{P}=\sum_{o}P(o)f(o)^{2}\ \geq\ P(o^{\star})f(o^{\star})^{2}\ &gt;\ 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus <math id="A9.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle_{P}</annotation></semantics></math> is an inner product. The norm axioms then follow from standard facts about inner product norms: nonnegativity and homogeneity are immediate, and the triangle inequality follows from</span></p>
<table id="A9.Ex213" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex213.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f+g\|_{P}^{2}=\|f\|_{P}^{2}+\|g\|_{P}^{2}+2\langle f,g\rangle_{P}\ \leq\ \|f\|_{P}^{2}+\|g\|_{P}^{2}+2\,\|f\|_{P}\,\|g\|_{P}\ =\ (\|f\|_{P}+\|g\|_{P})^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f+g\|_{P}^{2}=\|f\|_{P}^{2}+\|g\|_{P}^{2}+2\langle f,g\rangle_{P}\ \leq\ \|f\|_{P}^{2}+\|g\|_{P}^{2}+2\,\|f\|_{P}\,\|g\|_{P}\ =\ (\|f\|_{P}+\|g\|_{P})^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">where we used the Cauchy–Schwarz inequality. Taking square roots gives <math id="A9.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f+g\|_{P}\leq\|f\|_{P}+\|g\|_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f+g\|_{P}\leq\|f\|_{P}+\|g\|_{P}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Our modeling approach is informed by the following intuition.
Consider an LLM agent <math id="A9.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> whose behavior admits a unanimously compositional witnessing decomposition, with the witnesses interpreted as emergent personas formed during training.
By the stability result (Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem62" title="Theorem 62 (Openness). ‣ H.2 Openness of Strictly Unanimously Decomposable Pools ‣ Appendix H Properties of Strict Local (Small-Tilt) Unanimity ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">62</span></a>), there exists an <math id="A9.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-ball around <math id="A9.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> within which the unanimously compositional structure is preserved.
In the context of fine-tuning, we assume that each backpropagation step induces a small change to the agent’s profile: the original parent <math id="A9.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> is updated to a new parent <math id="A9.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> that remains within this <math id="A9.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-ball, and therefore also admits a unanimously compositional witnessing decomposition.</p>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">An alternative viewpoint is to express this constraint in terms of a <math id="A9.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\KL" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>KL</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL</annotation></semantics></math>-budget. During fine-tuning, a <math id="A9.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\KL" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>KL</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL</annotation></semantics></math>-regularization term is often introduced to preserve baseline capabilities while steering the model toward desired traits such as benevolence and helpfulness, thereby constraining divergence from the base model to remain within a specified bound.
In Appendix <a href="#A10.SS4" title="J.4 KL Budgets and Optimal Suppression ‣ Appendix J Killing the Waluigi Effect to First Order ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">J.4</span></a>, we unify these two perspectives and show that they are essentially equivalent.</p>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">This leads to a natural question: under such settings, can we theoretically characterize any macroscopic emergent properties of the witnesses?</p>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">For this purpose, we define</p>
<table id="A9.Ex214" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex214.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L(o)\;:=\;\log\!\left(\frac{P^{\prime}(o)}{P(o)}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L(o)\;:=\;\log\!\left(\frac{P^{\prime}(o)}{P(o)}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p">which measures the change in epistemic utility between the original parent <math id="A9.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and the updated parent <math id="A9.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The change in witness weights <math id="A9.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{\prime}-\beta=\Delta\beta=(\Delta\beta_{1},\dots,\Delta\beta_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{\prime}-\beta=\Delta\beta=(\Delta\beta_{1},\dots,\Delta\beta_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> must sum to zero coordinate-wise for the witnesses to remain a valid decomposition of <math id="A9.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We may then classify <math id="A9.SS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L(o)</annotation></semantics></math> to first order in Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem68" title="Theorem 68 (First–order log deviation under weight changes). ‣ I.1 Defining Centered Logarithmic Character Profiles ‣ Appendix I Modeling the Waluigi Effect ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">68</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem68" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem68.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 68</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem68.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(First–order log deviation under weight changes)<span id="Thmtheorem68.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem68.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem68.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem68.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem68.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{\prime}=\beta+\Delta\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{\prime}=\beta+\Delta\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem68.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> be the log–pool at <math id="Thmtheorem68.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define</span></p>
<table id="A9.Ex215" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex215.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(\beta,o):=\sum_{i=1}^{m}\beta_{i}\,l_{i}(o)\qquad\text{and}\qquad Z(\beta):=\sum_{u\in\mathcal{O}}\exp\big(S(\beta,u)\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(\beta,o):=\sum_{i=1}^{m}\beta_{i}\,l_{i}(o)\qquad\text{and}\qquad Z(\beta):=\sum_{u\in\mathcal{O}}\exp\big(S(\beta,u)\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem68.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem68.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then <math id="Thmtheorem68.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(o):=\log P(o)=S(\beta,o)-\log Z(\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(o):=\log P(o)=S(\beta,o)-\log Z(\beta)</annotation></semantics></math>.
To first order in <math id="Thmtheorem68.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\beta</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="A9.Ex216" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex216.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L(o)\ :=\ \log\frac{P^{\prime}(o)}{P(o)}\ =\ \sum_{i=1}^{m}\Delta\beta_{i}\,v_{i}(o)\ +\ o(\|\Delta\beta\|)\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.611em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L(o)\ :=\ \log\frac{P^{\prime}(o)}{P(o)}\ =\ \sum_{i=1}^{m}\Delta\beta_{i}\,v_{i}(o)\ +\ o(\|\Delta\beta\|)\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem68.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem68.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and in particular</span></p>
<table id="A9.Ex217" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex217.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big\|\Delta L\big\|_{P}\ \leq\ \sum_{i=1}^{m}|\Delta\beta_{i}|\,\|v_{i}\|_{P}\ +\ o(\|\Delta\beta\|)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.611em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big\|\Delta L\big\|_{P}\ \leq\ \sum_{i=1}^{m}|\Delta\beta_{i}|\,\|v_{i}\|_{P}\ +\ o(\|\Delta\beta\|).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A9.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">By definition of the log-pool,</span></p>
<table id="A9.Ex218" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex218.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(o)=\frac{\prod_{i=1}^{m}P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}}}{\sum_{u\in\mathcal{O}}\prod_{i=1}^{m}P_{i}(u)^{\beta_{i}}}=\frac{\exp\big(\sum_{i}\beta_{i}\log P_{i}(o)\big)}{\sum_{u\in\mathcal{O}}\exp\big(\sum_{i}\beta_{i}\log P_{i}(u)\big)}=\frac{e^{S(\beta,o)}}{Z(\beta)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(o)=\frac{\prod_{i=1}^{m}P_{i}(o)^{\beta_{i}}}{\sum_{u\in\mathcal{O}}\prod_{i=1}^{m}P_{i}(u)^{\beta_{i}}}=\frac{\exp\big(\sum_{i}\beta_{i}\log P_{i}(o)\big)}{\sum_{u\in\mathcal{O}}\exp\big(\sum_{i}\beta_{i}\log P_{i}(u)\big)}=\frac{e^{S(\beta,o)}}{Z(\beta)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence</span></p>
<table id="A9.Ex219" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex219.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(o):=\log P(o)=S(\beta,o)-\log Z(\beta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(o):=\log P(o)=S(\beta,o)-\log Z(\beta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS1.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS1.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">Now, fix <math id="A9.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\in\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\in\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math>. The map <math id="A9.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\mapsto L(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\mapsto L(o)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A9.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> as a composition of smooth functions on a finite sum within a positive domain. Thus, by the multivariate Taylor theorem at <math id="A9.SS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A9.Ex220" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex220.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\beta+\Delta\beta,\,o)\ =\ L(\beta,o)\ +\ \sum_{i=1}^{m}\partial_{\beta_{i}}L(\beta,o)\,\Delta\beta_{i}\ +\ r_{o}(\Delta\beta)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.555em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\beta+\Delta\beta,\,o)\ =\ L(\beta,o)\ +\ \sum_{i=1}^{m}\partial_{\beta_{i}}L(\beta,o)\,\Delta\beta_{i}\ +\ r_{o}(\Delta\beta),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS1.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS1.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">where the remainder satisfies <math id="A9.SS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{o}(\Delta\beta)=o(\|\Delta\beta\|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{o}(\Delta\beta)=o(\|\Delta\beta\|)</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A9.SS1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\beta\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\beta\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that <math id="A9.SS1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta\beta\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta\beta\|</annotation></semantics></math> denotes any fixed Euclidean norm on <math id="A9.SS1.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A9.Ex221" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex221.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L(o)\ =\ \sum_{i=1}^{m}\partial_{\beta_{i}}L(\beta,o)\,\Delta\beta_{i}\ +\ o(\|\Delta\beta\|)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.611em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L(o)\ =\ \sum_{i=1}^{m}\partial_{\beta_{i}}L(\beta,o)\,\Delta\beta_{i}\ +\ o(\|\Delta\beta\|).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS1.p7.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS1.p7.5.1" class="ltx_text">It remains to compute the partial derivatives <math id="A9.SS1.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{\beta_{i}}L(\beta,o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{\beta_{i}}L(\beta,o)</annotation></semantics></math>. Using <math id="A9.SS1.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\beta,o)=S(\beta,o)-\log Z(\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\beta,o)=S(\beta,o)-\log Z(\beta)</annotation></semantics></math> and the chain rule,</span></p>
<table id="A9.Ex222" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex222.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{\beta_{i}}L(\beta,o)\ =\ \partial_{\beta_{i}}S(\beta,o)\ -\ \partial_{\beta_{i}}\log Z(\beta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.611em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.555em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∂</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{\beta_{i}}L(\beta,o)\ =\ \partial_{\beta_{i}}S(\beta,o)\ -\ \partial_{\beta_{i}}\log Z(\beta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS1.p7.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS1.p7.6.1" class="ltx_text">The first term is immediate from the definition of <math id="A9.SS1.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A9.Ex223" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex223.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{\beta_{i}}S(\beta,o)\ =\ l_{i}(o)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{\beta_{i}}S(\beta,o)\ =\ l_{i}(o).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS1.p7.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS1.p7.7.1" class="ltx_text">For the second term, apply the chain rule to <math id="A9.SS1.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log Z</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A9.Ex224" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex224.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{\beta_{i}}\log Z(\beta)\ =\ \frac{1}{Z(\beta)}\,\partial_{\beta_{i}}Z(\beta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{\beta_{i}}\log Z(\beta)\ =\ \frac{1}{Z(\beta)}\,\partial_{\beta_{i}}Z(\beta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS1.p7.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS1.p7.8.1" class="ltx_text">By definition of <math id="A9.SS1.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> and again by the chain rule,</span></p>
<table id="A9.Ex225" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex225.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{\beta_{i}}Z(\beta)=\sum_{u\in\mathcal{O}}\partial_{\beta_{i}}\!\left(e^{S(\beta,u)}\right)=\sum_{u\in\mathcal{O}}e^{S(\beta,u)}\,\partial_{\beta_{i}}S(\beta,u)=\sum_{u\in\mathcal{O}}e^{S(\beta,u)}\,l_{i}(u)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{\beta_{i}}Z(\beta)=\sum_{u\in\mathcal{O}}\partial_{\beta_{i}}\!\left(e^{S(\beta,u)}\right)=\sum_{u\in\mathcal{O}}e^{S(\beta,u)}\,\partial_{\beta_{i}}S(\beta,u)=\sum_{u\in\mathcal{O}}e^{S(\beta,u)}\,l_{i}(u).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS1.p7.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS1.p7.9.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore</span></p>
<table id="A9.Ex226" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex226.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{\beta_{i}}\log Z(\beta)\ =\ \frac{\sum_{u\in\mathcal{O}}e^{S(\beta,u)}\,l_{i}(u)}{Z(\beta)}=\sum_{u\in\mathcal{O}}\frac{e^{S(\beta,u)}}{Z(\beta)}\,l_{i}(u)=\sum_{u\in\mathcal{O}}P(u)\,l_{i}(u)\ =\ \E_{P}[\,l_{i}\,]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{\beta_{i}}\log Z(\beta)\ =\ \frac{\sum_{u\in\mathcal{O}}e^{S(\beta,u)}\,l_{i}(u)}{Z(\beta)}=\sum_{u\in\mathcal{O}}\frac{e^{S(\beta,u)}}{Z(\beta)}\,l_{i}(u)=\sum_{u\in\mathcal{O}}P(u)\,l_{i}(u)\ =\ \E_{P}[\,l_{i}\,].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS1.p7.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS1.p7.10.1" class="ltx_text">Combining the pieces,</span></p>
<table id="A9.Ex227" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex227.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{\beta_{i}}L(\beta,o)\ =\ l_{i}(o)\ -\ \E_{P}[\,l_{i}\,]\ =\ v_{i}(o)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{\beta_{i}}L(\beta,o)\ =\ l_{i}(o)\ -\ \E_{P}[\,l_{i}\,]\ =\ v_{i}(o).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS1.p7.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS1.p7.11.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting <math id="A9.SS1.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{\beta_{i}}L(\beta,o)=v_{i}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{\beta_{i}}L(\beta,o)=v_{i}(o)</annotation></semantics></math> into the first-order Taylor expansion gives</span></p>
<table id="A9.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L(o)\ =\ \sum_{i=1}^{m}\Delta\beta_{i}\,v_{i}(o)\ +\ o(\|\Delta\beta\|)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.611em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L(o)\ =\ \sum_{i=1}^{m}\Delta\beta_{i}\,v_{i}(o)\ +\ o(\|\Delta\beta\|),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS1.p7.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS1.p7.12.1" class="ltx_text">as claimed. Define the remainder function <math id="A9.SS1.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(o):=\Delta L(o)-\sum_{i}\Delta\beta_{i}v_{i}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(o):=\Delta L(o)-\sum_{i}\Delta\beta_{i}v_{i}(o)</annotation></semantics></math>, so that <math id="A9.SS1.p7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|r\|_{P}=o(\|\Delta\beta\|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|r\|_{P}=o(\|\Delta\beta\|)</annotation></semantics></math> by the Taylor residual on smooth functions. Then</span></p>
<table id="A9.Ex228" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex228.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta L\|_{P}\ \leq\ \left\|\sum_{i=1}^{m}\Delta\beta_{i}v_{i}\right\|_{P}\ +\ \|r\|_{P}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta L\|_{P}\ \leq\ \left\|\sum_{i=1}^{m}\Delta\beta_{i}v_{i}\right\|_{P}\ +\ \|r\|_{P}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS1.p7.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS1.p7.13.1" class="ltx_text">Using the triangle inequality and homogeneity of the norm,</span></p>
<table id="A9.Ex229" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex229.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\sum_{i=1}^{m}\Delta\beta_{i}v_{i}\right\|_{P}\ \leq\ \sum_{i=1}^{m}\|\Delta\beta_{i}v_{i}\|_{P}\ =\ \sum_{i=1}^{m}|\Delta\beta_{i}|\,\|v_{i}\|_{P}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.611em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.611em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\sum_{i=1}^{m}\Delta\beta_{i}v_{i}\right\|_{P}\ \leq\ \sum_{i=1}^{m}\|\Delta\beta_{i}v_{i}\|_{P}\ =\ \sum_{i=1}^{m}|\Delta\beta_{i}|\,\|v_{i}\|_{P}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS1.p7.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS1.p7.14.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore</span></p>
<table id="A9.Ex230" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex230.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta L\|_{P}\ \leq\ \sum_{i=1}^{m}|\Delta\beta_{i}|\,\|v_{i}\|_{P}\ +\ o(\|\Delta\beta\|)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.611em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta L\|_{P}\ \leq\ \sum_{i=1}^{m}|\Delta\beta_{i}|\,\|v_{i}\|_{P}\ +\ o(\|\Delta\beta\|),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS1.p7.15" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS1.p7.15.1" class="ltx_text">which completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A9.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">I.2 </span>The Law of Weight-Compensation: Manifesting Luigi Forces Waluigi</h3>

<div id="A9.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We may now model the Waluigi effect, where “Luigi” is taken to be a benevolent persona or child subagent desideratum manifested during model training. Fix an index <math id="A9.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\in\mathbb{Z}_{&gt;0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\in\mathbb{Z}_{&gt;0}</annotation></semantics></math> (for a helpful logit vector component pointing toward Luigi). As the log-profiles have been centered in expectation, we say a vector <math id="A9.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="A9.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">aligned</em> with <math id="A9.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A9.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>
and <em id="A9.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">anti-aligned</em> if <math id="A9.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Intuitively, <math id="A9.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{H}</annotation></semantics></math> points in the direction in log–probability space that Luigi prefers; anti-aligned components push against it.</p>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In modeling a coherent and stable neural agent, we aim to preserve its underlying compositional structure. If a unanimously compositional decomposition exists, then there is an <math id="A9.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-ball around the agent’s profile within which the compositional property is maintained. In Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem69" title="Theorem 69 (Waluigi emergence). ‣ I.2 The Law of Weight-Compensation: Manifesting Luigi Forces Waluigi ‣ Appendix I Modeling the Waluigi Effect ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">69</span></a>, we examine the effects of introducing a targeted persona–“Luigi”–while ensuring that the overall agent remains within this compositional neighborhood. We prove that this process necessarily manifests or strengthens the weights of an anti-aligned persona to Luigi, which we denote “Waluigi,” under the assumption that the log-profile change remains within the <math id="A9.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-ball to preserve the compositional property or <math id="A9.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\KL" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>KL</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL</annotation></semantics></math>-budget.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem69" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem69.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 69</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem69.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Waluigi emergence)<span id="Thmtheorem69.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem69.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem69.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem69.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem69.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> be the log–pool at weights <math id="Thmtheorem69.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="Thmtheorem69.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}:=\log P_{i}-\E_{P}[\log P_{i}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">P</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}:=\log P_{i}-\E_{P}[\log P_{i}]</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., the log-profile of agent <math id="Thmtheorem69.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>).
Fix <math id="Thmtheorem69.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and perturb to <math id="Thmtheorem69.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{\prime}=\beta+\Delta\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{\prime}=\beta+\Delta\beta</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmtheorem69.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\beta_{H}=\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\beta_{H}=\delta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem69.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}\Delta\beta_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}\Delta\beta_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="Thmtheorem69.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> be the new log–pool and write</span></p>
<table id="A9.Ex231" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex231.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L\ :=\ \log\frac{P^{\prime}}{P}\ =\ \sum_{i=1}^{m}\Delta\beta_{i}\,v_{i}\ +\ r," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>P</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.611em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L\ :=\ \log\frac{P^{\prime}}{P}\ =\ \sum_{i=1}^{m}\Delta\beta_{i}\,v_{i}\ +\ r,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem69.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem69.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem69.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=o(\|\Delta\beta\|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=o(\|\Delta\beta\|)</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="Thmtheorem69.p1.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{P}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem68" title="Theorem 68 (First–order log deviation under weight changes). ‣ I.1 Defining Centered Logarithmic Character Profiles ‣ Appendix I Modeling the Waluigi Effect ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">68</span></a>). Assume the pooled distribution is stable in logit deviation, <math id="Thmtheorem69.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta L\|_{P}\ \leq\ \varepsilon." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta L\|_{P}\ \leq\ \varepsilon.</annotation></semantics></math>
Then, for every choice of <math id="Thmtheorem69.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\beta</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A9.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.E30.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{i:\,\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}&lt;0}(\Delta\beta_{i})^{+}\ \big|\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\big|\ \geq\ \delta\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}^{2}\ -\ (\varepsilon+\|r\|_{P})\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}\ -\!\!\sum_{j:\,\langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\geq 0}\!\!(\Delta\beta_{j})^{-}\ \langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.448em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.389em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.722em">−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo rspace="0em">+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi></msub><mpadded style="width:0.632em;" width="0.632em"><mo lspace="0em">−</mo></mpadded><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.448em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo></msup><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i:\,\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}&lt;0}(\Delta\beta_{i})^{+}\ \big|\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\big|\ \geq\ \delta\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}^{2}\ -\ (\varepsilon+\|r\|_{P})\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}\ -\!\!\sum_{j:\,\langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\geq 0}\!\!(\Delta\beta_{j})^{-}\ \langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem69.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem69.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem69.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\pm}:=\max\{\pm x,0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>±</mo></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>±</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\pm}:=\max\{\pm x,0\}</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, if <math id="Thmtheorem69.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> is the <em id="Thmtheorem69.p1.3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">only</em> anti-aligned component
(<math id="Thmtheorem69.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle v_{W},v_{H}\rangle_{P}&lt;0\leq\langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle v_{W},v_{H}\rangle_{P}&lt;0\leq\langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmtheorem69.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\neq W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\neq W</annotation></semantics></math>), and the weights <math id="Thmtheorem69.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\beta_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\beta_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> of aligned components <math id="Thmtheorem69.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{j:\langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{j:\langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\}</annotation></semantics></math> are not downgraded
by <math id="Thmtheorem69.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Delta\beta_{j})^{-}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo></msup><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta\beta_{j})^{-}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A9.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Delta\beta_{W})^{+}\ \geq\ \frac{\ \delta\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}^{2}\ -\ (\varepsilon+\|r\|_{P})\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}\ }{\,\big|\langle v_{W},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\big|}\ ." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>W</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta\beta_{W})^{+}\ \geq\ \frac{\ \delta\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}^{2}\ -\ (\varepsilon+\|r\|_{P})\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}\ }{\,\big|\langle v_{W},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\big|}\ .</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem69.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem69.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consequently, whenever <math id="Thmtheorem69.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon+\|r\|_{P}&lt;\delta\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon+\|r\|_{P}&lt;\delta\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}</annotation></semantics></math>, the Waluigi weight must increase by a strictly positive amount.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A9.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem68" title="Theorem 68 (First–order log deviation under weight changes). ‣ I.1 Defining Centered Logarithmic Character Profiles ‣ Appendix I Modeling the Waluigi Effect ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">68</span></a>, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A9.Ex232" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex232.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L=\sum_{i}\Delta\beta_{i}v_{i}+r,\qquad\|r\|_{P}=o(\|\Delta\beta\|)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L=\sum_{i}\Delta\beta_{i}v_{i}+r,\qquad\|r\|_{P}=o(\|\Delta\beta\|).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Take the <math id="A9.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>–inner product with <math id="A9.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{H}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A9.Ex233" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex233.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big\langle\Delta L,\ v_{H}\big\rangle_{P}\ =\ \sum_{i=1}^{m}\Delta\beta_{i}\,\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\ +\ \langle r,\ v_{H}\rangle_{P}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.611em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big\langle\Delta L,\ v_{H}\big\rangle_{P}\ =\ \sum_{i=1}^{m}\Delta\beta_{i}\,\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\ +\ \langle r,\ v_{H}\rangle_{P}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Using Cauchy–Schwarz and the deviation bound <math id="A9.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta L\|_{P}\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta L\|_{P}\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A9.Ex234" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex234.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big|\langle\Delta L,v_{H}\rangle_{P}\big|\ \leq\ \|\Delta L\|_{P}\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}\ \leq\ \varepsilon\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big|\langle\Delta L,v_{H}\rangle_{P}\big|\ \leq\ \|\Delta L\|_{P}\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}\ \leq\ \varepsilon\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS2.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A9.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{m}\Delta\beta_{i}\,\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\ +\ \langle r,v_{H}\rangle_{P}\ \leq\ \varepsilon\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{m}\Delta\beta_{i}\,\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\ +\ \langle r,v_{H}\rangle_{P}\ \leq\ \varepsilon\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS2.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS2.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">Bound the remainder by <math id="A9.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\langle r,v_{H}\rangle_{P}|\leq\|r\|_{P}\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\langle r,v_{H}\rangle_{P}|\leq\|r\|_{P}\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence</span></p>
<table id="A9.Ex235" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex235.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{m}\Delta\beta_{i}\,\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\ \leq\ (\varepsilon+\|r\|_{P})\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{m}\Delta\beta_{i}\,\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\ \leq\ (\varepsilon+\|r\|_{P})\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS2.p3.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS2.p3.6.1" class="ltx_text">We split into aligned and anti-aligned components and isolate the anti-aligned increases. Write the sum as</span></p>
<table id="A9.Ex236" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex236.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta\beta_{H}\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}^{2}\ +\!\!\sum_{j:\,\langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\geq 0}\!\!\Delta\beta_{j}\,\langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\ +\!\!\sum_{i:\,\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}&lt;0}\!\!\Delta\beta_{i}\,\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\ \leq\ (\varepsilon+\|r\|_{P})\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mpadded style="width:0.660em;" width="0.660em"><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mpadded><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.448em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mpadded style="width:0.660em;" width="0.660em"><mo>+</mo></mpadded><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.448em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo rspace="0em">+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\beta_{H}\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}^{2}\ +\!\!\sum_{j:\,\langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\geq 0}\!\!\Delta\beta_{j}\,\langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\ +\!\!\sum_{i:\,\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}&lt;0}\!\!\Delta\beta_{i}\,\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\ \leq\ (\varepsilon+\|r\|_{P})\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS2.p3.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS2.p3.7.1" class="ltx_text">Subtract <math id="A9.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\|v_{H}\|_{P}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\|v_{H}\|_{P}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> (recall <math id="A9.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\beta_{H}=\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\beta_{H}=\delta</annotation></semantics></math>) and rearranging gives</span></p>
<table id="A9.Ex237" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex237.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{i:\,\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}&lt;0}\Delta\beta_{i}\,\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\ \leq\ (\varepsilon+\|r\|_{P})\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}\ -\ \delta\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}^{2}\ -\!\!\sum_{j:\,\langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\geq 0}\!\!\Delta\beta_{j}\,\langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.448em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo rspace="0em">+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.722em">−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mpadded style="width:0.632em;" width="0.632em"><mo lspace="0em">−</mo></mpadded><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.448em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i:\,\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}&lt;0}\Delta\beta_{i}\,\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\ \leq\ (\varepsilon+\|r\|_{P})\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}\ -\ \delta\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}^{2}\ -\!\!\sum_{j:\,\langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\geq 0}\!\!\Delta\beta_{j}\,\langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS2.p3.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS2.p3.8.1" class="ltx_text">Each anti-aligned inner product is negative. Decompose <math id="A9.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\beta_{i}=\Delta\beta_{i}^{+}-\Delta\beta_{i}^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\beta_{i}=\Delta\beta_{i}^{+}-\Delta\beta_{i}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A9.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\pm}:=\max\{\pm x,0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>±</mo></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>±</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\pm}:=\max\{\pm x,0\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then for <math id="A9.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A9.Ex238" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex238.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\beta_{i}\,\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}=(\Delta\beta_{i}^{+}-\Delta\beta_{i}^{-})\,\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}=-\,\Delta\beta_{i}^{+}\ \big|\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\big|\ +\ \Delta\beta_{i}^{-}\ \big|\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\big|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\beta_{i}\,\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}=(\Delta\beta_{i}^{+}-\Delta\beta_{i}^{-})\,\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}=-\,\Delta\beta_{i}^{+}\ \big|\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\big|\ +\ \Delta\beta_{i}^{-}\ \big|\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\big|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS2.p3.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS2.p3.9.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, for aligned <math id="A9.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A9.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A9.Ex239" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex239.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\beta_{j}\,\langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P}=\Delta\beta_{j}^{+}\ \langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\ -\ \Delta\beta_{j}^{-}\ \langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\beta_{j}\,\langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P}=\Delta\beta_{j}^{+}\ \langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\ -\ \Delta\beta_{j}^{-}\ \langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS2.p3.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS2.p3.10.1" class="ltx_text">Plugging these into the inequality,</span></p>
<table id="A9.Ex240" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex240.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-\,\sum_{i:\,\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}&lt;0}\Delta\beta_{i}^{+}\ \big|\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\big|\ \leq\ (\varepsilon+\|r\|_{P})\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}\ -\ \delta\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}^{2}\ +\!\!\sum_{j:\,\langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\geq 0}\!\!\Delta\beta_{j}^{-}\ \langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.448em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.389em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo rspace="0em">+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.722em">−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mpadded style="width:0.660em;" width="0.660em"><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mpadded><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.448em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\,\sum_{i:\,\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}&lt;0}\Delta\beta_{i}^{+}\ \big|\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\big|\ \leq\ (\varepsilon+\|r\|_{P})\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}\ -\ \delta\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}^{2}\ +\!\!\sum_{j:\,\langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\geq 0}\!\!\Delta\beta_{j}^{-}\ \langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS2.p3.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS2.p3.11.1" class="ltx_text">Rearranging gives (<a href="#A9.E30" title="In Theorem 69 (Waluigi emergence). ‣ I.2 The Law of Weight-Compensation: Manifesting Luigi Forces Waluigi ‣ Appendix I Modeling the Waluigi Effect ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>):</span></p>
<table id="A9.Ex241" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex241.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{i:\,\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}&lt;0}\Delta\beta_{i}^{+}\ \big|\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\big|\ \geq\ \delta\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}^{2}\ -\ (\varepsilon+\|r\|_{P})\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}\ -\!\!\sum_{j:\,\langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\geq 0}\!\!\Delta\beta_{j}^{-}\ \langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.448em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.389em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.722em">−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo rspace="0em">+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi></msub><mpadded style="width:0.632em;" width="0.632em"><mo lspace="0em">−</mo></mpadded><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.448em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i:\,\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}&lt;0}\Delta\beta_{i}^{+}\ \big|\langle v_{i},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\big|\ \geq\ \delta\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}^{2}\ -\ (\varepsilon+\|r\|_{P})\,\|v_{H}\|_{P}\ -\!\!\sum_{j:\,\langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P}\geq 0}\!\!\Delta\beta_{j}^{-}\ \langle v_{j},v_{H}\rangle_{P}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS2.p3.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS2.p3.12.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A9.SS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> is the only anti-aligned component, the left-hand side is exactly <math id="A9.SS2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Delta\beta_{W})^{+}|\langle v_{W},v_{H}\rangle_{P}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>W</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta\beta_{W})^{+}|\langle v_{W},v_{H}\rangle_{P}|</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding (<a href="#A9.E31" title="In Theorem 69 (Waluigi emergence). ‣ I.2 The Law of Weight-Compensation: Manifesting Luigi Forces Waluigi ‣ Appendix I Modeling the Waluigi Effect ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Operationally, efforts to “manifest Luigi” (increasing <math id="A9.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{H}</annotation></semantics></math> via training or steering) while keeping behavior
close to the original <math id="A9.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> therefore <em id="A9.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">must</em> be offset by increasing weight on at least one anti-aligned
direction. If there is a distinguished anti-aligned component <math id="A9.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> (“Waluigi”), its weight must rise by at least the
explicit lower bound.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A10" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix J </span>Killing the Waluigi Effect to First Order</h2>

<div id="A10.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The previous section established a necessity result: if the system selects a minimal change to the pooled distribution to preserve unanimous compositionality while amplifying Luigi, it will inherently do so by shifting weight onto Waluigi, the anti-aligned counterpart subagents. Motivated by this result, we introduce <em id="A10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Antagonistic Persona Suppression (APS)</em>, formalized as the <em id="A10.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Waluigi Shattering</em> theorem. The key insight is that deliberately manifesting the anti-aligned persona (Waluigi) and then shattering it provides provably stronger suppression of anti-alignment than reinforcement of the aligned persona (Luigi) alone.</p>
</div>
<section id="A10.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">J.1 </span>First-Order Control of Misaligned Events</h3>

<div id="A10.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix a measurable anti-aligned outcome set <math id="A10.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\subseteq\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\subseteq\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> and write the centered indicator</p>
<table id="A10.Ex242" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex242.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{A}\ :=\ \mathbf{1}_{A}-P(A)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{A}\ :=\ \mathbf{1}_{A}-P(A).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We wish to reduce the probability that anti-aligned event <math id="A10.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is realized under the agent <math id="A10.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>. We now obtain the sensitivity of <math id="A10.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(A)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem70" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem70.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 70</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem70.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(First-order change of <math id="Thmtheorem70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(A)</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="Thmtheorem70.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem70.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem70.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem70.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For base agent <math id="Thmtheorem70.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and elicited agent <math id="Thmtheorem70.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex243" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex243.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}(A)-P(A)\ =\ \E_{P^{\prime}}[\mathbf{1}_{A}]-\E_{P}[\mathbf{1}_{A}]\ =\ \langle\Delta L,\ g_{A}\rangle_{P}\ +\ o(\|\Delta L\|_{P})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>A</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}(A)-P(A)\ =\ \E_{P^{\prime}}[\mathbf{1}_{A}]-\E_{P}[\mathbf{1}_{A}]\ =\ \langle\Delta L,\ g_{A}\rangle_{P}\ +\ o(\|\Delta L\|_{P}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem70.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem70.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem70.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{A}:=\mathbf{1}_{A}-P(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{A}:=\mathbf{1}_{A}-P(A)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem70.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{P}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="Thmtheorem70.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>–inner product norm.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A10.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A10.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Write <math id="A10.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta:=\|\Delta L\|_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta:=\|\Delta L\|_{P}</annotation></semantics></math>. By definition,</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex244" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex244.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}(o)\ =\ \frac{P(o)\,e^{\Delta L(o)}}{\E_{P}[e^{\Delta L}]}\,,\qquad P^{\prime}(A)\ =\ \frac{\E_{P}[\mathbf{1}_{A}\,e^{\Delta L}]}{\E_{P}[e^{\Delta L}]}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}(o)\ =\ \frac{P(o)\,e^{\Delta L(o)}}{\E_{P}[e^{\Delta L}]}\,,\qquad P^{\prime}(A)\ =\ \frac{\E_{P}[\mathbf{1}_{A}\,e^{\Delta L}]}{\E_{P}[e^{\Delta L}]}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Set</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex245" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex245.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\ :=\ \E_{P}[\mathbf{1}_{A}\,e^{\Delta L}],\qquad D\ :=\ \E_{P}[e^{\Delta L}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\ :=\ \E_{P}[\mathbf{1}_{A}\,e^{\Delta L}],\qquad D\ :=\ \E_{P}[e^{\Delta L}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Then <math id="A10.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}(A)=N/D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}(A)=N/D</annotation></semantics></math>. Define the continuous function</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex246" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex246.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(x)\ :=\ \begin{cases}\frac{e^{x}-1-x}{x^{2}},&amp;x\neq 0,\\
\frac{1}{2},&amp;x=0,\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(x)\ :=\ \begin{cases}\frac{e^{x}-1-x}{x^{2}},&amp;x\neq 0,\\
\frac{1}{2},&amp;x=0,\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS1.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">so that the identity <math id="A10.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{x}=1+x+\psi(x)\,x^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{x}=1+x+\psi(x)\,x^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> holds for all <math id="A10.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex247" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex247.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\Delta L}=1+\Delta L+\psi(\Delta L)\,\Delta L^{\,2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn> 2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\Delta L}=1+\Delta L+\psi(\Delta L)\,\Delta L^{\,2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS1.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS1.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A10.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous, there exists a constant <math id="A10.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A10.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that
<math id="A10.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\psi(\Delta L(o))|\leq C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\psi(\Delta L(o))|\leq C</annotation></semantics></math> whenever <math id="A10.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\leq\eta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\leq\eta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>; therefore</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex248" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex248.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E_{P}\big[\,|\psi(\Delta L)|\,\Delta L^{\,2}\big]\ \leq\ C\,\E_{P}[\Delta L^{\,2}]\ =\ C\,\|\Delta L\|_{P}^{2}\ =\ O(\eta^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn> 2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn> 2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E_{P}\big[\,|\psi(\Delta L)|\,\Delta L^{\,2}\big]\ \leq\ C\,\E_{P}[\Delta L^{\,2}]\ =\ C\,\|\Delta L\|_{P}^{2}\ =\ O(\eta^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS1.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS1.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">This gives that</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex249" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex249.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=\E_{P}[\mathbf{1}_{A}(1+\Delta L+\psi(\Delta L)\Delta L^{\,2})]=P(A)+\E_{P}[\mathbf{1}_{A}\Delta L]+O(\eta^{2})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn> 2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=\E_{P}[\mathbf{1}_{A}(1+\Delta L+\psi(\Delta L)\Delta L^{\,2})]=P(A)+\E_{P}[\mathbf{1}_{A}\Delta L]+O(\eta^{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A10.Ex250" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex250.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=\E_{P}[1+\Delta L+\psi(\Delta L)\Delta L^{\,2}]=1+\E_{P}[\Delta L]+O(\eta^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn> 2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\E_{P}[1+\Delta L+\psi(\Delta L)\Delta L^{\,2}]=1+\E_{P}[\Delta L]+O(\eta^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS1.p2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS1.p2.7.1" class="ltx_text">By Cauchy–Schwarz, <math id="A10.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\E_{P}[\Delta L]|\leq\|\Delta L\|_{P}\|\mathbf{1}\|_{P}=\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\E_{P}[\Delta L]|\leq\|\Delta L\|_{P}\|\mathbf{1}\|_{P}=\eta</annotation></semantics></math> (since <math id="A10.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{1}\|_{P}=\sqrt{\E_{P}[1]}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{1}\|_{P}=\sqrt{\E_{P}[1]}=1</annotation></semantics></math>), and
<math id="A10.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\E_{P}[\mathbf{1}_{A}\Delta L]|\leq\|\mathbf{1}_{A}\|_{P}\,\|\Delta L\|_{P}\leq\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\E_{P}[\mathbf{1}_{A}\Delta L]|\leq\|\mathbf{1}_{A}\|_{P}\,\|\Delta L\|_{P}\leq\eta</annotation></semantics></math> (because <math id="A10.SS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{1}_{A}\|_{P}=\sqrt{P(A)}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{1}_{A}\|_{P}=\sqrt{P(A)}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>).
Thus both linear terms are <math id="A10.SS1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\eta)</annotation></semantics></math> and the remainders are <math id="A10.SS1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\eta^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\eta^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A10.SS1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u:=\E_{P}[\Delta L]+O(\eta^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u:=\E_{P}[\Delta L]+O(\eta^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> so <math id="A10.SS1.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|u|=O(\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|u|=O(\eta)</annotation></semantics></math>. Using the identity</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex251" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex251.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{1+u}\ =\ 1-u+u^{2}\,\phi(u)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{1+u}\ =\ 1-u+u^{2}\,\phi(u),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS1.p2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS1.p2.8.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A10.SS1.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous (e.g., via the Taylor expansion or Neumann series) and hence bounded near <math id="A10.SS1.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex252" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex252.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{D}\ =\ \frac{1}{1+\E_{P}[\Delta L]+O(\eta^{2})}\ =\ 1-\E_{P}[\Delta L]+O(\eta^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{D}\ =\ \frac{1}{1+\E_{P}[\Delta L]+O(\eta^{2})}\ =\ 1-\E_{P}[\Delta L]+O(\eta^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS1.p2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS1.p2.9.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, we have</span></p>
<table id="A10.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A10.Ex253"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex253.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P^{\prime}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P^{\prime}(A)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex253.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\big(P(A)+\E_{P}[\mathbf{1}_{A}\Delta L]+O(\eta^{2})\big)\,\big(1-\E_{P}[\Delta L]+O(\eta^{2})\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\big(P(A)+\E_{P}[\mathbf{1}_{A}\Delta L]+O(\eta^{2})\big)\,\big(1-\E_{P}[\Delta L]+O(\eta^{2})\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A10.Ex254"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex254.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=P(A)\ +\ \E_{P}[\mathbf{1}_{A}\Delta L]\ -\ P(A)\,\E_{P}[\Delta L]\ +\ O(\eta^{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=P(A)\ +\ \E_{P}[\mathbf{1}_{A}\Delta L]\ -\ P(A)\,\E_{P}[\Delta L]\ +\ O(\eta^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS1.p2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS1.p2.10.1" class="ltx_text">Subtract <math id="A10.SS1.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(A)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex255" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex255.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}(A)-P(A)\ =\ \E_{P}[\mathbf{1}_{A}\Delta L]\ -\ P(A)\,\E_{P}[\Delta L]\ +\ O(\eta^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}(A)-P(A)\ =\ \E_{P}[\mathbf{1}_{A}\Delta L]\ -\ P(A)\,\E_{P}[\Delta L]\ +\ O(\eta^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS1.p2.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS1.p2.11.1" class="ltx_text">Recall <math id="A10.SS1.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{A}=\mathbf{1}_{A}-P(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{A}=\mathbf{1}_{A}-P(A)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex256" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex256.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\Delta L,g_{A}\rangle_{P}\ =\ \E_{P}[\Delta L\,(\mathbf{1}_{A}-P(A))]\ =\ \E_{P}[\mathbf{1}_{A}\Delta L]\ -\ P(A)\,\E_{P}[\Delta L]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\Delta L,g_{A}\rangle_{P}\ =\ \E_{P}[\Delta L\,(\mathbf{1}_{A}-P(A))]\ =\ \E_{P}[\mathbf{1}_{A}\Delta L]\ -\ P(A)\,\E_{P}[\Delta L].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS1.p2.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS1.p2.12.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex257" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex257.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}(A)-P(A)\ =\ \langle\Delta L,g_{A}\rangle_{P}\ +\ O(\eta^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}(A)-P(A)\ =\ \langle\Delta L,g_{A}\rangle_{P}\ +\ O(\eta^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS1.p2.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS1.p2.13.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A10.SS1.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\eta^{2})=o(\eta)=o(\|\Delta L\|_{P})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\eta^{2})=o(\eta)=o(\|\Delta L\|_{P})</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A10.SS1.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex258" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex258.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}(A)-P(A)\ =\ \langle\Delta L,g_{A}\rangle_{P}\ +\ o(\|\Delta L\|_{P})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}(A)-P(A)\ =\ \langle\Delta L,g_{A}\rangle_{P}\ +\ o(\|\Delta L\|_{P}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS1.p2.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS1.p2.14.1" class="ltx_text">as claimed.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A10.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Within the compositional regime <math id="A10.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta L\|_{P}\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta L\|_{P}\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, we have by (<a href="#Thmtheorem68" title="Theorem 68 (First–order log deviation under weight changes). ‣ I.1 Defining Centered Logarithmic Character Profiles ‣ Appendix I Modeling the Waluigi Effect ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">68</span></a>) that feasible <math id="A10.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L</annotation></semantics></math> lie in the subspace <math id="A10.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S:=\mathrm{span}\{v_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>span</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S:=\mathrm{span}\{v_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. This gives Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem71" title="Lemma 71 (Optimal small-change suppression of 𝐴). ‣ J.1 First-Order Control of Misaligned Events ‣ Appendix J Killing the Waluigi Effect to First Order ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">71</span></a>, which precisely quantifies the maximal first order decrease in the probability of the manifestation of deplorable or misaligned outcomes <math id="A10.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(A)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem71" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem71.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 71</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem71.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Optimal small-change suppression of <math id="Thmtheorem71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="Thmtheorem71.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem71.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem71.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem71.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the budget <math id="Thmtheorem71.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta L\|_{P}\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta L\|_{P}\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>,
the maximal <em id="Thmtheorem71.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">first-order decrease</em> of <math id="Thmtheorem71.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(A)</annotation></semantics></math> equals</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex259" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex259.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{A}^{\max}\ :=\ \max_{\begin{subarray}{c}\Delta L\in S\\
\|\Delta L\|_{P}\leq\varepsilon\end{subarray}}\ \big(-\langle\Delta L,g_{A}\rangle_{P}\big)\ =\ \varepsilon\,\big\|\mathrm{Proj}_{S}g_{A}\big\|_{P}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>max</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Proj</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{A}^{\max}\ :=\ \max_{\begin{subarray}{c}\Delta L\in S\\
\|\Delta L\|_{P}\leq\varepsilon\end{subarray}}\ \big(-\langle\Delta L,g_{A}\rangle_{P}\big)\ =\ \varepsilon\,\big\|\mathrm{Proj}_{S}g_{A}\big\|_{P}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem71.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem71.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">It is achieved by <math id="Thmtheorem71.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L^{\star}=-\,\varepsilon\,u_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L^{\star}=-\,\varepsilon\,u_{S}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Thmtheorem71.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{S}:=\mathrm{Proj}_{S}g_{A}/\|\mathrm{Proj}_{S}g_{A}\|_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Proj</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Proj</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{S}:=\mathrm{Proj}_{S}g_{A}/\|\mathrm{Proj}_{S}g_{A}\|_{P}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A10.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A10.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem70" title="Lemma 70 (First-order change of 𝑃(𝐴)). ‣ J.1 First-Order Control of Misaligned Events ‣ Appendix J Killing the Waluigi Effect to First Order ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">70</span></a>, decreasing <math id="A10.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(A)</annotation></semantics></math> to first order amounts to maximizing <math id="A10.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\langle\Delta L,g_{A}\rangle_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\langle\Delta L,g_{A}\rangle_{P}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Cauchy–Schwarz on the subspace <math id="A10.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, the maximum over <math id="A10.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta L\|_{P}\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta L\|_{P}\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is attained by aligning
<math id="A10.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A10.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\mathrm{Proj}_{S}g_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Proj</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\mathrm{Proj}_{S}g_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, with value <math id="A10.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\|\mathrm{Proj}_{S}g_{A}\|_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Proj</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\|\mathrm{Proj}_{S}g_{A}\|_{P}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A10.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, the stronger the alignment of <math id="A10.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> with the span of available directions <math id="A10.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the more we can reduce the probability of misaligned outcome events, <math id="A10.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(A)</annotation></semantics></math>, per unit budget.
If the span <math id="A10.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is poor at approximating <math id="A10.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> (small projection), suppression is weak.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A10.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">J.2 </span>Eliciting Waluigi Increases Achievable Suppression Power</h3>

<div id="A10.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A10.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{0}:=\mathrm{span}\{v_{1},\ldots,v_{m}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>span</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{0}:=\mathrm{span}\{v_{1},\ldots,v_{m}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be the baseline span of the logarithmic agentic profiles, and suppose we <em id="A10.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">elicit</em> a coherent
“Waluigi” direction <math id="A10.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., by training on producing <math id="A10.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>), making it available for control.
Let <math id="A10.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u:=w-\mathrm{Proj}_{S_{0}}w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Proj</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u:=w-\mathrm{Proj}_{S_{0}}w</annotation></semantics></math> be the component of <math id="A10.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> orthogonal to <math id="A10.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>; if <math id="A10.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, it adds a <em id="A10.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">new</em> direction in the log-profile space.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem72" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem72.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 72</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem72.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Elicitation strictly enlarges the small-change leverage)<span id="Thmtheorem72.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem72.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem72.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem72.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem72.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}:=\mathrm{span}\{S_{0},w\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>span</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}:=\mathrm{span}\{S_{0},w\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex260" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex260.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big\|\mathrm{Proj}_{S_{1}}g_{A}\big\|_{P}^{2}\ =\ \big\|\mathrm{Proj}_{S_{0}}g_{A}\big\|_{P}^{2}\ +\ \frac{\langle g_{A},u\rangle_{P}^{2}}{\|u\|_{P}^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Proj</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Proj</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big\|\mathrm{Proj}_{S_{1}}g_{A}\big\|_{P}^{2}\ =\ \big\|\mathrm{Proj}_{S_{0}}g_{A}\big\|_{P}^{2}\ +\ \frac{\langle g_{A},u\rangle_{P}^{2}}{\|u\|_{P}^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem72.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem72.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular, if <math id="Thmtheorem72.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem72.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle g_{A},u\rangle_{P}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle g_{A},u\rangle_{P}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, then
<math id="Thmtheorem72.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathrm{Proj}_{S_{1}}g_{A}\|_{P}&gt;\|\mathrm{Proj}_{S_{0}}g_{A}\|_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Proj</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Proj</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathrm{Proj}_{S_{1}}g_{A}\|_{P}&gt;\|\mathrm{Proj}_{S_{0}}g_{A}\|_{P}</annotation></semantics></math>, and by Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem71" title="Lemma 71 (Optimal small-change suppression of 𝐴). ‣ J.1 First-Order Control of Misaligned Events ‣ Appendix J Killing the Waluigi Effect to First Order ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">71</span></a>
the maximal first-order reduction of <math id="Thmtheorem72.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(A)</annotation></semantics></math> under the same budget <math id="Thmtheorem72.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> strictly increases.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A10.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A10.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Orthogonal decomposition in the <math id="A10.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>-inner product gives
<math id="A10.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Proj}_{S_{1}}g_{A}=\mathrm{Proj}_{S_{0}}g_{A}+\alpha\,\hat{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Proj</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Proj</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Proj}_{S_{1}}g_{A}=\mathrm{Proj}_{S_{0}}g_{A}+\alpha\,\hat{u}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A10.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{u}:=u/\|u\|_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{u}:=u/\|u\|_{P}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A10.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=\langle g_{A},\hat{u}\rangle_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=\langle g_{A},\hat{u}\rangle_{P}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Pythagoras yields the stated identity for the squared norms.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A10.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A10.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> is a direction that <em id="A10.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">increases</em> <math id="A10.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> (so <math id="A10.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle g_{A},w\rangle_{P}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle g_{A},w\rangle_{P}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>),
its orthogonal novelty <math id="A10.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> typically has <math id="A10.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle g_{A},u\rangle_{P}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle g_{A},u\rangle_{P}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> unless <math id="A10.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> is already spanned by <math id="A10.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence adding <math id="A10.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> tends to strictly increase the projection of <math id="A10.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, enlarging the best achievable reduction of <math id="A10.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(A)</annotation></semantics></math>
for the <em id="A10.SS2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">same</em> small-change budget.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A10.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">J.3 </span>Reinforcing Luigi Cannot Avoid Anti-Aligned Mass under Small Change</h3>

<div id="A10.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A10.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> be a “Luigi” component (disfavors <math id="A10.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> so <math id="A10.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle g_{A},v_{H}\rangle_{P}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle g_{A},v_{H}\rangle_{P}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>).
Increasing <math id="A10.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{H}</annotation></semantics></math> while keeping <math id="A10.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> close forces anti-aligned increases by the compensation law
(Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem69" title="Theorem 69 (Waluigi emergence). ‣ I.2 The Law of Weight-Compensation: Manifesting Luigi Forces Waluigi ‣ Appendix I Modeling the Waluigi Effect ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">69</span></a>):
if <math id="A10.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta L\|_{P}\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta L\|_{P}\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A10.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\beta_{H}=\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\beta_{H}=\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, then
some anti-aligned component <math id="A10.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A10.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle v_{W},v_{H}\rangle_{P}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle v_{W},v_{H}\rangle_{P}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> must satisfy <math id="A10.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\beta_{W}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>W</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\beta_{W}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>
(and in the unique anti-aligned case, with an explicit lower bound).
Combining with Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem71" title="Lemma 71 (Optimal small-change suppression of 𝐴). ‣ J.1 First-Order Control of Misaligned Events ‣ Appendix J Killing the Waluigi Effect to First Order ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">71</span></a> yields:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem73" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem73.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 73</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem73.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Pure “Luigi reinforcement” is not a workaround)<span id="Thmtheorem73.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem73.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem73.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem73.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose the available span remains <math id="Thmtheorem73.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> (no new directions are added).
Any small-change update that raises Luigi (<math id="Thmtheorem73.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\beta_{H}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\beta_{H}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>) while keeping <math id="Thmtheorem73.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta L\|_{P}\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta L\|_{P}\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>
necessarily increases some anti-aligned weight(s), which the optimal suppressor in <math id="Thmtheorem73.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> would subsequently need to <em id="Thmtheorem73.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">reduce</em>.
Thus, for the same budget and architecture, the best first-order decrease of <math id="Thmtheorem73.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(A)</annotation></semantics></math> is
upper bounded by <math id="Thmtheorem73.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\|\mathrm{Proj}_{S_{0}}g_{A}\|_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Proj</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\|\mathrm{Proj}_{S_{0}}g_{A}\|_{P}</annotation></semantics></math>, whereas eliciting a Waluigi direction <math id="Thmtheorem73.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>
with <math id="Thmtheorem73.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem73.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle g_{A},u\rangle_{P}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle g_{A},u\rangle_{P}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> raises this bound to
<math id="Thmtheorem73.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\|\mathrm{Proj}_{S_{1}}g_{A}\|_{P}&gt;\varepsilon\|\mathrm{Proj}_{S_{0}}g_{A}\|_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Proj</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Proj</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\|\mathrm{Proj}_{S_{1}}g_{A}\|_{P}&gt;\varepsilon\|\mathrm{Proj}_{S_{0}}g_{A}\|_{P}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A10.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The best first-order reduction of a harmful set <math id="A10.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is exactly proportional to the projection of <math id="A10.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> onto the span of available
control directions. <em id="A10.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Eliciting</em> a coherent Waluigi adds a direction that typically increases that projection,
so a subsequent suppression step can reduce <math id="A10.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(A)</annotation></semantics></math> <em id="A10.SS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">more</em> for the same budget than simply reinforcing Luigi,
which cannot avoid introducing anti-aligned mass unless large deviations to the parent agent are applied. We now give a direct comparison under a fixed budget.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem74" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem74.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 74</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem74.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Misalignment reduction from Luigi and Waluigi)<span id="Thmtheorem74.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem74.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem74.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem74.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem74.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> be the baseline span and let <math id="Thmtheorem74.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> be a Waluigi direction with <math id="Thmtheorem74.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u:=w-\mathrm{Proj}_{S_{0}}w\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Proj</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u:=w-\mathrm{Proj}_{S_{0}}w\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Assume <math id="Thmtheorem74.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle g_{A},u\rangle_{P}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle g_{A},u\rangle_{P}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, for any small-change budget <math id="Thmtheorem74.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex261" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex261.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underbrace{\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}\Delta L\in S_{1}\\
\|\Delta L\|_{P}\leq\varepsilon\end{subarray}}\big(-\langle\Delta L,g_{A}\rangle_{P}\big)}_{\text{manifest $w$, then suppress}}\ -\ \underbrace{\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}\Delta L\in S_{0}\\
\|\Delta L\|_{P}\leq\varepsilon\end{subarray}}\big(-\langle\Delta L,g_{A}\rangle_{P}\big)}_{\text{pure Luigi (no $w$ added)}}\ &gt;\ 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">manifest </mtext><mi mathsize="0.700em">w</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">, then suppress</mtext></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.722em" rspace="0.722em">−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">pure Luigi (no </mtext><mi mathsize="0.700em">w</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> added)</mtext></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underbrace{\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}\Delta L\in S_{1}\\
\|\Delta L\|_{P}\leq\varepsilon\end{subarray}}\big(-\langle\Delta L,g_{A}\rangle_{P}\big)}_{\text{manifest $w$, then suppress}}\ -\ \underbrace{\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}\Delta L\in S_{0}\\
\|\Delta L\|_{P}\leq\varepsilon\end{subarray}}\big(-\langle\Delta L,g_{A}\rangle_{P}\big)}_{\text{pure Luigi (no $w$ added)}}\ &gt;\ 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A10.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A10.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Apply Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem71" title="Lemma 71 (Optimal small-change suppression of 𝐴). ‣ J.1 First-Order Control of Misaligned Events ‣ Appendix J Killing the Waluigi Effect to First Order ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">71</span></a> on <math id="A10.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A10.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and subtract, then use Proposition <a href="#Thmtheorem72" title="Proposition 72 (Elicitation strictly enlarges the small-change leverage). ‣ J.2 Eliciting Waluigi Increases Achievable Suppression Power ‣ Appendix J Killing the Waluigi Effect to First Order ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">72</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A10.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">If elicitation reveals a novel or unlearned Waluigi direction with nonzero correlation to <math id="A10.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, then “manifest Waluigi, then suppress” produces a strictly larger first-order decrease of <math id="A10.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(A)</annotation></semantics></math> than any
strategy that never adds this direction, including pure Luigi reinforcement. The results above jointly establish the following theorem, which synthesizes their conclusions into a unified statement.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem75" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem75.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 75</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem75.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Waluigi shattering)<span id="Thmtheorem75.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem75.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem75.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem75.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem75.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> denote the base agent and let <math id="Thmtheorem75.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> be a misaligned event. For any aligned update <math id="Thmtheorem75.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> realized through a log-profile change <math id="Thmtheorem75.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L</annotation></semantics></math>, define</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex262" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex262.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(P^{\prime})\ :=\ \max_{\|\Delta L\|_{P}\leq\varepsilon}\,\big(-\langle\Delta L,g_{A}\rangle_{P}\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(P^{\prime})\ :=\ \max_{\|\Delta L\|_{P}\leq\varepsilon}\,\big(-\langle\Delta L,g_{A}\rangle_{P}\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem75.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem75.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">to be the maximal first-order reduction in the probability of <math id="Thmtheorem75.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> under <math id="Thmtheorem75.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, subject to a small-change <math id="Thmtheorem75.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\KL" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>KL</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL</annotation></semantics></math>-budget <math id="Thmtheorem75.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose <math id="Thmtheorem75.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> is an anti-aligned (“Waluigi”) direction with nontrivial component <math id="Thmtheorem75.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u:=w-\mathrm{Proj}_{S_{0}}w\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Proj</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u:=w-\mathrm{Proj}_{S_{0}}w\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> outside the baseline span <math id="Thmtheorem75.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex263" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex263.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(P^{\prime}_{\text{shatter}})\ -\ M(P^{\prime}_{\text{pure}})\ =\ \varepsilon\,\frac{|\langle g_{A},u\rangle_{P}|}{\|u\|_{P}}\ &gt;\ 0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">shatter</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">pure</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.778em">&gt;</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(P^{\prime}_{\text{shatter}})\ -\ M(P^{\prime}_{\text{pure}})\ =\ \varepsilon\,\frac{|\langle g_{A},u\rangle_{P}|}{\|u\|_{P}}\ &gt;\ 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem75.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem75.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem75.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}_{\text{shatter}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">shatter</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}_{\text{shatter}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the strategy of manifesting <math id="Thmtheorem75.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> and then suppressing it, while <math id="Thmtheorem75.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}_{\text{pure}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">pure</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}_{\text{pure}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes reinforcing alignment without manifesting <math id="Thmtheorem75.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, <em id="Thmtheorem75.p1.3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">Waluigi Shattering</em> achieves strictly greater suppression of misalignment than pure reinforcement alone.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A10.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">J.4 </span>KL Budgets and Optimal Suppression</h3>

<div id="A10.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To retain prior knowledge and capabilities while steering the model toward benevolence, one typically constrains the fine–tuning process with a limited <math id="A10.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\KL" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>KL</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL</annotation></semantics></math> budget.
We derive the
expansion of <math id="A10.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\KL(P^{\prime}\|P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(P^{\prime}\|P)</annotation></semantics></math> in powers of <math id="A10.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L</annotation></semantics></math> and show that enforcing a budget <math id="A10.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\KL(P^{\prime}\|P)\leq B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(P^{\prime}\|P)\leq B</annotation></semantics></math> is, to second order,
equivalent to imposing a norm budget
<math id="A10.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta L\|_{P}\lesssim\sqrt{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>≲</mo><msqrt><mi>B</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta L\|_{P}\lesssim\sqrt{B}</annotation></semantics></math> (Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem76" title="Theorem 76 (Second–order KL expansion). ‣ J.4 KL Budgets and Optimal Suppression ‣ Appendix J Killing the Waluigi Effect to First Order ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">76</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem76" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem76.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 76</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem76.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Second–order KL expansion)<span id="Thmtheorem76.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem76.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem76.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem76.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem76.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> be finite and <math id="Thmtheorem76.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> strictly positive. Let <math id="Thmtheorem76.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L:\mathcal{O}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L:\mathcal{O}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy
<math id="Thmtheorem76.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta L\|_{P}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta L\|_{P}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, and define <math id="Thmtheorem76.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex264" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex264.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}(o)\ :=\ P(o)\,e^{\Delta L(o)}\qquad\text{(equivalently, }\Delta L=\log(P^{\prime}/P)\text{)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">(equivalently, </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">)</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}(o)\ :=\ P(o)\,e^{\Delta L(o)}\qquad\text{(equivalently, }\Delta L=\log(P^{\prime}/P)\text{)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem76.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem76.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then with <math id="Thmtheorem76.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu:=\E_{P}[\Delta L]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu:=\E_{P}[\Delta L]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem76.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Var_{P}(\Delta L):=\E_{P}[(\Delta L-\mu)^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Var_{P}(\Delta L):=\E_{P}[(\Delta L-\mu)^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex265" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex265.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\KL(P^{\prime}\|P)\ \lesssim\ \tfrac{1}{2}\,\Var_{P}(\Delta L)\ +\ o\big(\|\Delta L\|_{P}^{2}\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≲</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>L</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mi>o</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>L</mi><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(P^{\prime}\|P)\ \lesssim\ \tfrac{1}{2}\,\Var_{P}(\Delta L)\ +\ o\big(\|\Delta L\|_{P}^{2}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem76.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem76.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular, we have that the <math id="Thmtheorem76.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\KL" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>KL</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL</annotation></semantics></math> budget asymptotes toward</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex266" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex266.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\KL(P^{\prime}\|P)\ \approx\frac{1}{2}\|\Delta L\|_{P}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>L</mi><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(P^{\prime}\|P)\ \approx\frac{1}{2}\|\Delta L\|_{P}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A10.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A10.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Set <math id="A10.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta:=\|\Delta L\|_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta:=\|\Delta L\|_{P}</annotation></semantics></math> for notational convenience. Because <math id="A10.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> is finite and <math id="A10.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> has full support, there exists a constant
<math id="A10.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A10.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta L\|_{\infty}\leq c_{\infty}\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta L\|_{\infty}\leq c_{\infty}\eta</annotation></semantics></math> via the equivalence of norms.
By Taylor’s theorem with Lagrange remainder,
for each <math id="A10.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A10.SS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|x|\leq c_{\infty}\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|x|\leq c_{\infty}\eta</annotation></semantics></math> there exists <math id="A10.SS4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math> between <math id="A10.SS4.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A10.SS4.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex267" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex267.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{x}\ =\ 1+x+\frac{x^{2}}{2}+\frac{e^{\xi}}{3!}\,x^{3}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msup><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{x}\ =\ 1+x+\frac{x^{2}}{2}+\frac{e^{\xi}}{3!}\,x^{3}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A10.SS4.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|x|\leq c_{\infty}\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|x|\leq c_{\infty}\eta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A10.SS4.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, for all <math id="A10.SS4.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A10.SS4.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Delta L(o)|\leq c_{\infty}\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Delta L(o)|\leq c_{\infty}\eta</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A10.SS4.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\xi}\leq e^{c_{\infty}\eta}=1+O(\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\xi}\leq e^{c_{\infty}\eta}=1+O(\eta)</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus there is a constant <math id="A10.SS4.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> (independent of <math id="A10.SS4.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math> and small <math id="A10.SS4.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>) such that</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex268" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex268.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Big|\,e^{\Delta L(o)}-\Big(1+\Delta L(o)+\tfrac{1}{2}\,\Delta L(o)^{2}\Big)\,\Big|\ \leq\ C\,|\Delta L(o)|^{3}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.500em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Big|\,e^{\Delta L(o)}-\Big(1+\Delta L(o)+\tfrac{1}{2}\,\Delta L(o)^{2}\Big)\,\Big|\ \leq\ C\,|\Delta L(o)|^{3}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS4.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS4.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Taking <math id="A10.SS4.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>–expectations yields</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex269" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex269.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E_{P}\!\big[e^{\Delta L}\big]\ =\ 1+\E_{P}[\Delta L]+\tfrac{1}{2}\,\E_{P}[\Delta L^{2}]+R_{3},\qquad|R_{3}|\ \leq\ C\,\E_{P}\!\big[|\Delta L|^{3}\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E_{P}\!\big[e^{\Delta L}\big]\ =\ 1+\E_{P}[\Delta L]+\tfrac{1}{2}\,\E_{P}[\Delta L^{2}]+R_{3},\qquad|R_{3}|\ \leq\ C\,\E_{P}\!\big[|\Delta L|^{3}\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS4.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS4.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, we have <math id="A10.SS4.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Delta L|^{3}\leq\|\Delta L\|_{\infty}\,\Delta L^{2}\leq c_{\infty}\eta\,\Delta L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Delta L|^{3}\leq\|\Delta L\|_{\infty}\,\Delta L^{2}\leq c_{\infty}\eta\,\Delta L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex270" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex270.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E_{P}[|\Delta L|^{3}]\ \leq\ c_{\infty}\eta\,\E_{P}[\Delta L^{2}]\ \leq\ c_{\infty}\eta\,\|\Delta L\|_{P}^{2}\ =\ c_{\infty}\,\eta^{3}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E_{P}[|\Delta L|^{3}]\ \leq\ c_{\infty}\eta\,\E_{P}[\Delta L^{2}]\ \leq\ c_{\infty}\eta\,\|\Delta L\|_{P}^{2}\ =\ c_{\infty}\,\eta^{3}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS4.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS4.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore <math id="A10.SS4.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{3}=O(\eta^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{3}=O(\eta^{3})</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="A10.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E_{P}[e^{\Delta L}]-1\ =\ \mu\ +\ \tfrac{1}{2}\,m_{2}\ +\ O(\eta^{3})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.722em" rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E_{P}[e^{\Delta L}]-1\ =\ \mu\ +\ \tfrac{1}{2}\,m_{2}\ +\ O(\eta^{3}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS4.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS4.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A10.SS4.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{2}:=\E_{P}[\Delta L^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{2}:=\E_{P}[\Delta L^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math>. By definition, we have that <math id="A10.SS4.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E_{P}[e^{\Delta L}]=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E_{P}[e^{\Delta L}]=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Rearranging the above,</span></p>
<table id="A10.E34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\ =\ -\,\tfrac{1}{2}\,m_{2}\ +\ O(\eta^{3})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\ =\ -\,\tfrac{1}{2}\,m_{2}\ +\ O(\eta^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS4.p2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS4.p2.7.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A10.SS4.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{2}=\E_{P}[\Delta L^{2}]\leq\|\Delta L\|_{\infty}\,\E_{P}[|\Delta L|]\leq\|\Delta L\|_{\infty}\,\|\Delta L\|_{P}\leq c_{\infty}\eta\cdot\eta=O(\eta^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{2}=\E_{P}[\Delta L^{2}]\leq\|\Delta L\|_{\infty}\,\E_{P}[|\Delta L|]\leq\|\Delta L\|_{\infty}\,\|\Delta L\|_{P}\leq c_{\infty}\eta\cdot\eta=O(\eta^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, (<a href="#A10.E34" title="In Proof. ‣ J.4 KL Budgets and Optimal Suppression ‣ Appendix J Killing the Waluigi Effect to First Order ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a>) implies <math id="A10.SS4.p2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=O(\eta^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=O(\eta^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.
By definition,</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex271" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex271.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\KL(P^{\prime}\|P)\ =\ \E_{P^{\prime}}\!\left[\log\frac{P^{\prime}}{P}\right]\ =\ \E_{P^{\prime}}[\Delta L]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>P</mi></mfrac><mo rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(P^{\prime}\|P)\ =\ \E_{P^{\prime}}\!\left[\log\frac{P^{\prime}}{P}\right]\ =\ \E_{P^{\prime}}[\Delta L].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS4.p2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS4.p2.8.1" class="ltx_text">But <math id="A10.SS4.p2.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}(o)=P(o)\,e^{\Delta L(o)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}(o)=P(o)\,e^{\Delta L(o)}</annotation></semantics></math>, so</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex272" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex272.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E_{P^{\prime}}[\Delta L]\ =\ \sum_{o}P^{\prime}(o)\Delta L(o)\ =\ \sum_{o}P(o)\,e^{\Delta L(o)}\,\Delta L(o)\ =\ \E_{P}\!\big[\Delta L\,e^{\Delta L}\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.611em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></munder><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.611em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E_{P^{\prime}}[\Delta L]\ =\ \sum_{o}P^{\prime}(o)\Delta L(o)\ =\ \sum_{o}P(o)\,e^{\Delta L(o)}\,\Delta L(o)\ =\ \E_{P}\!\big[\Delta L\,e^{\Delta L}\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS4.p2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS4.p2.9.1" class="ltx_text">Now expand the integrand with the same uniform remainder control:</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex273" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex273.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L\,e^{\Delta L}\ =\ \Delta L\Big(1+\Delta L+\tfrac{1}{2}\,\Delta L^{2}\Big)\ +\ \Delta L\cdot R_{3}(\Delta L)\ =\ \Delta L+\Delta L^{2}+\tfrac{1}{2}\,\Delta L^{3}+R_{4}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L\,e^{\Delta L}\ =\ \Delta L\Big(1+\Delta L+\tfrac{1}{2}\,\Delta L^{2}\Big)\ +\ \Delta L\cdot R_{3}(\Delta L)\ =\ \Delta L+\Delta L^{2}+\tfrac{1}{2}\,\Delta L^{3}+R_{4},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS4.p2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS4.p2.10.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A10.SS4.p2.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{4}:=\Delta L\cdot R_{3}(\Delta L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{4}:=\Delta L\cdot R_{3}(\Delta L)</annotation></semantics></math>. Using <math id="A10.SS4.p2.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|R_{3}(\Delta L)|\leq C|\Delta L|^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|R_{3}(\Delta L)|\leq C|\Delta L|^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex274" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex274.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|R_{4}|\ \leq\ C\,|\Delta L|^{4}\ \leq\ C\,\|\Delta L\|_{\infty}^{2}\,\Delta L^{2}\ \leq\ C\,c_{\infty}^{2}\,\eta^{2}\,\Delta L^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|R_{4}|\ \leq\ C\,|\Delta L|^{4}\ \leq\ C\,\|\Delta L\|_{\infty}^{2}\,\Delta L^{2}\ \leq\ C\,c_{\infty}^{2}\,\eta^{2}\,\Delta L^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS4.p2.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS4.p2.11.1" class="ltx_text">Taking expectations,</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex275" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex275.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E_{P}[|R_{4}|]\ \leq\ C\,c_{\infty}^{2}\,\eta^{2}\,\E_{P}[\Delta L^{2}]\ \leq\ C\,c_{\infty}^{2}\,\eta^{2}\,\|\Delta L\|_{P}^{2}\ =\ O(\eta^{4})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E_{P}[|R_{4}|]\ \leq\ C\,c_{\infty}^{2}\,\eta^{2}\,\E_{P}[\Delta L^{2}]\ \leq\ C\,c_{\infty}^{2}\,\eta^{2}\,\|\Delta L\|_{P}^{2}\ =\ O(\eta^{4}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS4.p2.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS4.p2.12.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore</span></p>
<table id="A10.E35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E_{P}\!\big[\Delta L\,e^{\Delta L}\big]\ =\ \E_{P}[\Delta L]+\E_{P}[\Delta L^{2}]+\tfrac{1}{2}\,\E_{P}[\Delta L^{3}]+O(\eta^{4})\ =\ \mu+m_{2}+\tfrac{1}{2}\,m_{3}+O(\eta^{4})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E_{P}\!\big[\Delta L\,e^{\Delta L}\big]\ =\ \E_{P}[\Delta L]+\E_{P}[\Delta L^{2}]+\tfrac{1}{2}\,\E_{P}[\Delta L^{3}]+O(\eta^{4})\ =\ \mu+m_{2}+\tfrac{1}{2}\,m_{3}+O(\eta^{4}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS4.p2.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS4.p2.13.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A10.SS4.p2.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{3}:=\E_{P}[\Delta L^{3}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{3}:=\E_{P}[\Delta L^{3}]</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining <math id="A10.SS4.p2.m30" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\KL(P^{\prime}\|P)=\E_{P}[\Delta L\,e^{\Delta L}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>L</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(P^{\prime}\|P)=\E_{P}[\Delta L\,e^{\Delta L}]</annotation></semantics></math> with (<a href="#A10.E35" title="In Proof. ‣ J.4 KL Budgets and Optimal Suppression ‣ Appendix J Killing the Waluigi Effect to First Order ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>) and substituting <math id="A10.SS4.p2.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> from
(<a href="#A10.E34" title="In Proof. ‣ J.4 KL Budgets and Optimal Suppression ‣ Appendix J Killing the Waluigi Effect to First Order ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a>) gives</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex276" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex276.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\KL(P^{\prime}\|P)\ =\ \Big(-\tfrac{1}{2}m_{2}+O(\eta^{3})\Big)+m_{2}+\tfrac{1}{2}m_{3}+O(\eta^{4})\ =\ \tfrac{1}{2}\,m_{2}\ +\ \tfrac{1}{2}\,m_{3}\ +O(\eta^{3})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(P^{\prime}\|P)\ =\ \Big(-\tfrac{1}{2}m_{2}+O(\eta^{3})\Big)+m_{2}+\tfrac{1}{2}m_{3}+O(\eta^{4})\ =\ \tfrac{1}{2}\,m_{2}\ +\ \tfrac{1}{2}\,m_{3}\ +O(\eta^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS4.p2.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS4.p2.14.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A10.SS4.p2.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{3}=O(\eta^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{3}=O(\eta^{3})</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A10.E36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.E36.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\KL(P^{\prime}\|P)\ =\ \tfrac{1}{2}\,m_{2}\ +\ O(\eta^{3})\ =\ \tfrac{1}{2}\,\E_{P}[\Delta L^{2}]\ +\ O(\eta^{3})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(P^{\prime}\|P)\ =\ \tfrac{1}{2}\,m_{2}\ +\ O(\eta^{3})\ =\ \tfrac{1}{2}\,\E_{P}[\Delta L^{2}]\ +\ O(\eta^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS4.p2.15" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS4.p2.15.1" class="ltx_text">Noting that <math id="A10.SS4.p2.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E_{P}[\Delta L^{2}]=\|\Delta L\|^{2}_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E_{P}[\Delta L^{2}]=\|\Delta L\|^{2}_{P}</annotation></semantics></math> gives <math id="A10.SS4.p2.m34" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\KL(P^{\prime}\|P)\ =\ O(\|\Delta L\|^{2}_{P})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>L</mi><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(P^{\prime}\|P)\ =\ O(\|\Delta L\|^{2}_{P})</annotation></semantics></math>. Write <math id="A10.SS4.p2.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{2}=\E_{P}[\Delta L^{2}]=\Var_{P}(\Delta L)+\mu^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{2}=\E_{P}[\Delta L^{2}]=\Var_{P}(\Delta L)+\mu^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex277" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex277.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\KL(P^{\prime}\|P)\ =\ \tfrac{1}{2}\,\Var_{P}(\Delta L)\ +\ \tfrac{1}{2}\,\mu^{2}\ +\ O(\eta^{3})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>L</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(P^{\prime}\|P)\ =\ \tfrac{1}{2}\,\Var_{P}(\Delta L)\ +\ \tfrac{1}{2}\,\mu^{2}\ +\ O(\eta^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS4.p2.16" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS4.p2.16.1" class="ltx_text">As we have <math id="A10.SS4.p2.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=O(\eta^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=O(\eta^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex278" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex278.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\KL(P^{\prime}\|P)\ =\ \tfrac{1}{2}\,\Var_{P}(\Delta L)\ +\ O(\eta^{3})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>L</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(P^{\prime}\|P)\ =\ \tfrac{1}{2}\,\Var_{P}(\Delta L)\ +\ O(\eta^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS4.p2.17" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS4.p2.17.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, by definition of <math id="A10.SS4.p2.m37" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{P}</annotation></semantics></math> and of variance,</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex279" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex279.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Var_{P}(\Delta L)\ =\ \E_{P}\!\big[(\Delta L-\mu)^{2}\big]\ =\ \|\Delta L-\E_{P}[\Delta L]\|_{P}^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Var_{P}(\Delta L)\ =\ \E_{P}\!\big[(\Delta L-\mu)^{2}\big]\ =\ \|\Delta L-\E_{P}[\Delta L]\|_{P}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS4.p2.18" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS4.p2.18.1" class="ltx_text">so we have</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex280" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex280.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\KL(P^{\prime}\|P)\ =\ \tfrac{1}{2}\,\|\Delta L-\E_{P}[\Delta L]\|_{P}^{2}\ +\ o(\eta^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mi>o</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(P^{\prime}\|P)\ =\ \tfrac{1}{2}\,\|\Delta L-\E_{P}[\Delta L]\|_{P}^{2}\ +\ o(\eta^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS4.p2.19" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS4.p2.19.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A10.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, if we impose <math id="A10.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\KL(P^{\prime}\|P)\leq B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(P^{\prime}\|P)\leq B</annotation></semantics></math> for small <math id="A10.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem76" title="Theorem 76 (Second–order KL expansion). ‣ J.4 KL Budgets and Optimal Suppression ‣ Appendix J Killing the Waluigi Effect to First Order ‣ Probabilistic Modeling of Latent Agentic Substructures in Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">76</span></a> implies that <math id="A10.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta L\|_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta L\|_{P}</annotation></semantics></math> asymptotes toward</p>
<table id="A10.Ex281" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex281.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta L\|_{P}\ \leq\ \varepsilon,\qquad\varepsilon\approx\sqrt{2B}\ +\ o(\sqrt{B})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.722em" rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>B</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta L\|_{P}\ \leq\ \varepsilon,\qquad\varepsilon\approx\sqrt{2B}\ +\ o(\sqrt{B}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, a small <math id="A10.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\KL" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>KL</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL</annotation></semantics></math> ball is second order equivalent to a radius–<math id="A10.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> ball in the <math id="A10.SS4.p3.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{P}</annotation></semantics></math> norm.
Consequently, a <math id="A10.SS4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\KL" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>KL</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL</annotation></semantics></math>-regularizer may be interpreted as constraining the agent <math id="A10.SS4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> to remain within a guaranteed compositional range, ensuring that any realized distribution <math id="A10.SS4.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> also preserves the compositional property.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</article>
</div>
</div>
